{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000068OEP', 'answerTime': 'Dec 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388131200, 'question': 'When Connecting to my M-Audio BX5 D2 speakers to my PC using the XLR to 1/8 stereo RCA Y cable how do i tell which XLR cable goes to which speaker?', 'answer': "For my cables, the dotted side is the left side, and the solid line is the right side. In case there is a mismatch and it's the reverse... The quickest way I found out was by taking a song that images (certain sounds in the left and different sounds in the right) one way using headphones, or another source, and playing that through my iPhone. Once both sources had the same sounds coming from the right and left, I knew I had connected correct cable to each speaker."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000068OEP', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388304000, 'question': 'how far do the two xor cables spread apart?', 'answer': 'The cable is a \'y\' where the two XLR connector legs can be pulled apart all the way down to the 1/8" connector if you want. That would allow up to over 8 feet for each leg. Mine are used to connect two powered monitor speakers to an MP3, tablet, phone, etc.'}
