{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000C5NYD', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'I hate to be a pain but I want to get it right for my use which is better s arm or strait', 'answer': 'Hi, The Straight arm is only good for scratching - the needle sticks to the record more - but it also wears out your records faster. Unless you are a scratch DJ, the S-shaped tonearm is by far superior. Please let me know if you have any other questions. My very best, Jennifer Millennium'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0000WS0SC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'Which one would you recommend this Korg or the Novation MiniNova Analog Modeling Sythesizer?', 'answer': 'Each of the units has comparable advantages and disadvantages. If you are looking for more current dubstep-style bass resonance, you will probably prefer the MiniNova. If you are content to do without that, the Korg has similar classic synth sounds, including trancey industrial sounds.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0000WS0SC', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421827200, 'question': 'Does it come with recording/editing softaware, and if so what kind?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "you will need an interface to record an analog line level signal into a computer. you can hook it up usb from midi with a converter, bit you will only be communicating MIDI signals, not analog sound. That goes for most usb connections between digital keys and OS's. You can control virtual instruments using it as a midi controller but thats not what you buy this for. For example though:you could control the microkorg with another MIDI controller if you want bigger keys, and with a controller with surface control faders /knobs you can assign all functions to those as well. In summary: No it doesnt come with editing software."}
