{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002A2RTU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406530800, 'question': 'can i connect these to a old sherwood amp? And, how big are they?', 'answer': "These are 4 ohm speakers and they can take a lot of power, 120W continuous, 200W peak output. if your amp isn't rated for 4 ohm speakers you could burn it up trying to drive these. Older amps were typically rated for 8 ohm speakers."}
