{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002BG2S6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425801600, 'question': 'Has anyone used this mixer for pod cast or voice over recording? If so, can you give some feedback? Thanks', 'answer': "I'm guessing you want to hook up a microphone and another audio source like a CD player or iPod at the same time and be able to mix background music in realtime, rather than having to edit a multitrack recording after the fact in GarageBand or similar software? This little mixer will work fine for that purpose. If you are thinking of mixing multiple microphone inputs simultaneously on one recording (several people talking at once), it won't work for that: you'd need a bigger mixer with more than one XLR input jack (as many as you plan to have mikes going at once)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002BG2S6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422345600, 'question': "How does the switchable phantom power work? The images and description don't make it clear how that part is set up.", 'answer': 'You just move the jumper in the back from pins 1&2 to pins 2&3 and then phantom power will be available on Ch1 Input (the XLR connector on the back).'}
