{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002CZV6E', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'Can the BD-2 also be used with a bass guitar', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sure- however... Boss guitar pedals have their low end limited from the get go. One of the easiest mods to do is replace the input capacitor to get more bottom. Without that, a bass won\'t get quite the "blatt" (mimic the low chirp that come from pushing a speaker till it breaks up) that a bass distortion pedal might.'}
