{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002CZVU0', 'answerTime': 'Oct 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412838000, 'question': "Is this the least obtrusive capo out there? I have a shubb which is about 1/3 inch high off the strings and I'm always banging it.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'On the fretboard side of the neck, I think the G7th capo has a lower profile. As far as the back side of the neck, probably this or the Marshall capo are about the same. The Marshall capo is also compact, and uses a velcro strap to fasten it. This makes it a little more adjustable as far as the amount of pressure on the strings is concerned. The lever system on the Dunlop can sometimes be too strong and pull the strings sharp.'}
