{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002CZVXM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419580800, 'question': 'I would like to know if the seller (Music123) or the Mfr. (Dunlop) could get me the right screws to mount these "Strap Loc\'s) to my \' 75 Rickenbacker?', 'answer': "Not sure about the Rickenbacker...I bought two sets of strap locks for my Ibanez SR500 and Fender American Standard Precision Bass. The supplied screws fit both basses perfectly without any modifications needed. Again, I'm not sure about your guitar, but you could try searching the web forums to see what other guitarists say about it. Good luck!!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002CZVXM', 'answerTime': 'May 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400828400, 'question': 'Any idea what size screw these use?', 'answer': 'As far as size not really..........but I have them on all my guitars. I love \'em. I don\'t think you have to worry about size, unless the screws currently in your guitar is way oversized. If that\'s the case use an old carpenters\' trick and put a toothpick in the hole and then put in the smaller screw. I\'m thinking 1/8" but I don\'t really know.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002CZVXM', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'Does it need to be drilled to work with a seagull guitar?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It does require drilling a screw that\'s usually slightly larger than the screw holding the strap knob currently. As always (put barsoap in the tip/threads of the new "straplock" screw) and use the recommended size drill bit when "re-coring" for the new larger screw (have a electric drill and various small wood drill bits). If you have ANY doubt, then I\'d say take it to a well trusted and referred guitar technician/luthier. Their experience is almost ALWAYS worth the money!!'}
