{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002D0KG4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373353200, 'question': 'Would this be a valuable addition to my 44VSL and headphone amp for podcasting?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'For podcasting the preamps on the 44VSL should be good enough to give your voice enough body to sound great. The tubpre is good for vocals and instruments since it utilizes a tube and can be over-driven. Also the tube tends to "warm up" your voice, making it sound more like you\'re using a full amp. I love the tubepre, but I use it for vocals with an AT2020 condenser mike. If you feel your voice is a bit too flat or just needs an extra boost... then this little baby would be perfect, but its all preference at that point. What do you feel your voice is missing?'}
