{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002D0N70', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386489600, 'question': 'How does this mic do for Brass instruments?', 'answer': "I've tried it on a trumpet, and it sounded pretty clean and accurate. I've also tried it on vocals and drums, it will do really good on almost anything really. If all you're looking for a mic to record just a brass instrument though, and don't already own an audio interface, I'd recommend the Blue Snowball USB. It's $100 I believe, it'll sound similar, and you won't have to buy an interface for it (which are $100-200 in addition to the mic itself) hope this helps!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002D0N70', 'answerTime': '20 days ago', 'question': 'Is there a certain xlr mtf cable that produces phantom power that I have to use with this mic? If so, I want a noise free one with good quality', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Phantom power is produced by audio mixer or mic preamp, or phantom power unit. There is no XLR cable MtF that can produce phantom power by itself. Please check your mixer, it should have a 48v button.'}
