{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E1J3Q', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372143600, 'question': 'what is the difference between slinky and non slinky?', 'answer': 'Short answer: marketing. For the real story see the Ernie Ball website, but if you trust my memory... many, many moons ago there were few guitar string makers and they pretty much made the same thing- strings that helped a guitar be heard in a Big Band environment. The Ernie Ball company was one of the first to start marketing "boutique strings" that were easier for the player to fret and to bend. Compared to other strings at the time (anybody remember Black Diamonds?) the word "slinky" pretty much described how they felt.'}
