{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E1P2Q', 'answerTime': 'Oct 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382684400, 'question': 'I have a condenser mic (phantom powered) and I get RFI thru it: Will this cable eliminate it? Thanx!', 'answer': 'These quad cables are shielded, but the RFI may be from your cell phone, wifi or other rlectronic devices. Turn them all off, wifi off, and move all unnecessary devices away from mic, cables, preamp and audio interface. It could also be buzz from the outlets/ground; try moving plugs and switching ground switch off or on. If all else fails, look for an RFI blocker, available at radio shack. Keep power cables seperate from audio cables anytime you work in the studio.'}
