{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E2TVM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'Can this be used to tune the timpani?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Absolutely! I am a high school student and the timpani at my school have always sounded terrible with plenty of overtones and awful ringing. We used this on them and they sound better than ever. Timpani are sensitive, especially since they get retuned multiple times within a single song, so they will be out of tune, practically every day. So maintenance is key, keep up with them and they will shine. Also, ours need new heads so that's definitely a factor. In other words, this doesn't solve every single problem, but it does correct a very big one and beautifully at that."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E2TVM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425110400, 'question': 'Am new to drumming. Is there set tensions to set each drum to in a set? Does this drum dial come with any parameters to set drum heads to?', 'answer': 'This tuner comes with full instructions and suggestions about setting up your drums. It will be up to you what tension to finally tune your drums to.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E2TVM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': 'Would this be good for tuning hand drums? How would I know what tension to tune for?', 'answer': 'This is a very good tool to have for anyone who has drums with nearly any kind of tuning system. My son uses this tool on his hand drums with mechanical tuners. I use it on my Tabla set. We both use it on our trap sets. The drums sound noticeably better after a tuning. A previous answer detailed how this tuner works, so I will not repeat those instructions.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E2TVM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402729200, 'question': 'Hi, can the drumdial be used to tune timbales?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. Any drum with a drumhead big enough for the dial. It's a great tool."}
