{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E363C', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396681200, 'question': 'Are the bells all one size?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "The bells are all one size. They have numbers l-8 on the end of the handles. However, I renumbered using a Black Magic Marker on the face of the bell according to the piano with middle C as C4 and an octave higher as C5. A 20 note set is B3 through E5. Each note does give it's own sound even though all bells are the same size. Prepare felt pads with corresponding labels for returning each bell to its own pad after it is played. Felt can be attached with safety pins to the table cloths. I use heavy bath towels for table cloths."}
