{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E363C', 'answerTime': 'Jul 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406358000, 'question': 'Do they come with any type of case?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'They come in a very sturdy cardboard box. However, I purchased the 8 note black fabric cases with zipper closure. I prefer the 8 note cases to the 13 note cases. I just ordered four 8 note cases to cover my 20 note set of Bells. To play different key signatures a total of 20 bells purchased as a 20 note, or individual sets, is more beneficial than just 8 notes. A3 thru E5. Recommend; Handbell accompaniment Books: "Sweet Pipes Books with CD"'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E363C', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385712000, 'question': 'is this a set that has hand-held cards by a leader, so bell players can follow the cards via colors?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'We love our bells however they did not come with color cards'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E363C', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'PLEASE let me know Where they are made. I cannot buy from China.. etc. And is the paint child-safe? Thanks!', 'answer': "I'm sorry I can't answer your questions since the original boxes are long gone. We use the black padded cases specifically designed for the bell sets to store them. I can tell you we use the bells with our Childhood Center preschoolers as well as our Sunday school children. The bells are of good quality and sound amazingly clear. I highly recommend them."}
