{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E38AS', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'How do you claim the lifetime warranty? I have a cable that went bad , need a new one?', 'answer': 'Did you purchased it from Amazon? Go to "Your Account" then go to "Your Orders" find the invoice of the purchase and print it. Then you contact Monster directly and they will provide you with instructions on returning it. If you bought it elsewhere take it back to where you bought it with receipt and ask for a replacement. lol I remember the sales pitch at Guitar Center selling me one stating that I could simply walk in anytime and proceed to cut the end off in front of a salesperson and trade up for a new one. Nowadays they no longer carry this cord. Care to guess why? Rock on!'}
