{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E3CJ0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': "What is the difference between the EXP16 and the EJ16 strings? They're both phosphor bronze so wondering. Thx. : )", 'answer': 'EXPs are Extended Play, meaning they are coated to last longer than normal phosphor non coated bronze. Also a little bit smoother of a tone in my opinion.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E3CJ0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409036400, 'question': 'My Teton came with these EXP strings and sounded great. I tried the non-coated kind of same gauge and were SHRILL. Does the coating mute the highs?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Maybe a small amount. It's mostly due to the design and materials used in the strings. I've found that D'Addario strings tend to be bright. Phosphor bronze strings offer a rounder, warmer tone. 80/20 bronze offers a brighter, cleaner tone. The coated strings tend to be darker than plain strings of the same gauge and manufacturer."}
