{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E50XG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'I\'m using 1/4" mono to RCAs hooked up to a Carver C-1 External Processor Loop. I get sound with audio in, but nothing with the audio out engaged HELP!', 'answer': 'Make sure to come OUT from the FBQ going to the input on the Carver, then OUT from the Carver to the amplifier. If this does not work try coming OUT from the mixer to the Input of the Carver, then OUT of the Carver to the amp and see if you get sound. If not the problem may be in the Carver. Good luck!!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002E50XG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403074800, 'question': 'Does this model come with both fuses, making it compatible for multi-county use?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Power input depends on where you buy it. Mine is set up for 120V 60Hz only. Manual lists three voltages, plus a "General Export Model" that can be used worldwide. Ask sweetwater.com or behringer.com about how to order the voltage options.'}
