{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002E51PI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423728000, 'question': 'I believe I need XLRF to XLRM cable for the mic (AT2035) to preamp, but what do I need for preamp to pc? XLRF to usb?', 'answer': 'I have another XLR cable that goes to my interface (a gizmo that has six ins and outs both XLR and standard instrument "phone" jacks). To hook that interface up to the computer there is a Firewire cable. It has a Firewire plug on both ends. There is no such animal as a XLR to USB or Firewire. The XLR is a patch cord while USB (or Firewire) carry power and data. My interface is called a Presonus Firebox. I\'ve had it a long time and it works pretty well. Line 6 has some good interfaces too. I am really liking that Behringer pre amp. It\'s well worth the $50'}
