{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002F77L8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398495600, 'question': 'can this keyboard case hold the PSR S910?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have both a 900 and a 910. Either one will fit in this case. The case is satisfactory for carrying the keyboards but does not provide as much protection as cases with thicker padding or hard-shell "airline" type cases. I also have a Yamaha YBV612 "Virtuoso Series" case that has better padding. That model is now discontinued but the Yamaha website says the similar YBV611 is still current (although I don\'t see it on Amazon or other retailer sites). http://usa.yamaha.com/products/musical-instruments/keyboards/accessories/cases/ybv611/?mode=model#page=1&mode=paging If there is any chance of rough handling you might want to consider a different case. After all, you\'re protecting an expensive instrument. But if you will be carrying it yourself and are careful, this case is fine.'}
