{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GXPF4', 'answerTime': 'Jun 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370674800, 'question': 'my plug is the opposite of everything I found if the ground is North, the T is on the West and the vertical is East is this something different?', 'answer': "What you have there is a Nema 6-20P 240V appliance. Leg1+Leg2+Ground instead of Leg1+Neutral+Ground. You can't run such an appliance off 120V (unless you use a step-up transformer). The easiest and least expensive solution is probably to install a 240V circuit."}
