{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GXPF4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1373439600, 'question': 'i need an adaptor for GE2400 BTU Air Conditioner to regular 15V outlet. the plug says 20A -250V will this work?', 'answer': 'It will function but you must keep all contacts very clean. Any oxidation will cause heat to build any will overheat the conectors. It may get hot anyway. It is a little light duty. 15 amp outlets often have 15 amp breakers. The A/C probably is less than 15 amps but it would be worthwhile to check. I am assuming it is av110v A/C unit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GXPF4', 'answerTime': 'Jul 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404889200, 'question': 'I have a Wolff Systems Solar Wave 16 Lamp Residential Tanning Bed .It says I need a 110v power cord. I was wondering if i needed something else?', 'answer': "This adapter will convert your 20 amp power cord to fit a conventional 110v wall plug. If the plug on your lamp is a standard three prong, then you don't need this. If one of the prongs is turned sideways, indicating a 20 amp requirement, then this will be what you need. Unless, in the unlikely event that you already have a 20 amp wall socket!"}
