{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GZD5Y', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'I use this for my bass guitar but can I use this to DJ too? I have a 2000wt peak, 1000 rms 8ohm cabinet....i dont know if it will push', 'answer': 'I\'ve had people ask about using bass heads connecting to a PA speaker for bass gigs, but this is the other way?? I think the "growl" from head will taint the sound output. Also you should watch out for the amount of heat it will be generating running consistent full range at high volume which I don\'t think these are made for to handle.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002GZM00', 'answerTime': 'Apr 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396594800, 'question': 'Hi, will this fit the Boss PSM 5 power supply/master switch pedal? Thanks a lot.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This fits all Boss pedals, as well as 99.99% of other pedals.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GZM00', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419926400, 'question': "Is this a negative tip polarity or is adjustable? My Boss Chorus requires a negative tip. Why isn't this in the product description?", 'answer': 'This is just a daisy chain. What goes in comes out. If source adapter is center -, then all output will also be center -. I also have the 1 Spot 9 volt, it is center -. I have 2 Boss pedals amongnst other brands on my board all center -. I started with this http://www.amazon.com/Visual-Sound-Spot-Combo-Pack/dp/B000RNB720 Im not sure what power source you have but this is only an extention. Be careful of grabbing any power supply around the house. Many are unregulated, center +, or even AC.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002GZM00', 'answerTime': 'Oct 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414566000, 'question': 'Will this fit the line 6 dl-4?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, not the correct power source for Line 6. Most Line 6 pod type effects require AC power. This is for DC.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002GZM00', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'Will this fit the Korg Volca series?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I do not see why not. Just daisy chains a number of devices if you have a transformer that is powerful enough to drive more than one connection. I don't have the specifics of what you're hooking up other than the Korg. I take it you're trying to connect a number of devices with this cord and an existing transformer. On the transformer you should have the amperage. If I was hooking up multiple devices I would worry more about that aspect. Each device will draw power and the transformer needs to be powerful enough."}
