{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002H0GF0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'Is this possible to just play and not connect it on the computer ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No, this is only a controller. You need to connect it to a computer with music/instrument software or a MIDI-compatible instrument (like a synthesizer).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002H0GF0', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'Looking primarily to learn piano, but would sacrifice SFX of most boards to get midi; any downside to getting a midi to learn on?', 'answer': "Not at all. Most of the sound effects and things that you would eventually want will be available through software on your computer. Just note that this keyboard itself won't emit sound. Just MIDI commands. The sound will come from your computer."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002H0GF0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Does it have a headphone port', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "No. the keyboard is a controller. It has no sounds of it's own. Therefore there is no audio out plug. Only midi out. The audio out will come from the laptop, desktop or iPhone/iPod/iPad that you connect the board to. That computer (or other) must have the instrument software. You will also need headphones and or speakers."}
