{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002H0GF0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402297200, 'question': 'Does this midi controller keyboard come with software or do I have to buy separate software to play piano through my computer speakers?', 'answer': "The software most likely already resides on your computer, and definitely if it is an Apple. The basic MIDI software can be enhanced by a great number of software packages, providing features and sound samples. The software for PC's that comes with the product may not suit you as well as others. Get to know how MIDI works and you will soon be getting the hang of it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002GZSNQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'In this description it does not state what size it is? Does anybody know what size this is??', 'answer': "Yes, it fits the sound hole on a standard body, dreadnaught, and jumbo size from most makers. If it doesn't fit tightly but covers the sound hole, it will still help. If it is a little bigger than the sound hole you can slid one of the tabs in and either trim the other tab or let it sit on top of the face. Even without a perfect fit it is better to keep the right humidity level inside the body than let the body dry out."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002GZSNQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409295600, 'question': 'Can this humidifier be used if the guitar is hanging on the wall sometimes ?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Of course, it will stay in the hole until you remove it, but the moisture will only help the body of the guitar from the inside obviously, whereas if it is in the case, the humidifier lets a small amount of moisture escape into the case to benefit the whole instrument.'}
