{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002JEV04', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388649600, 'question': "Can someone explain this spec? *Maximum Load: 10A per channel / 20A total I would've thought that being a 4 channel dimmer, if it is rated at 20 A max, then it would've been rataed at 5A per channel not 10 A per channel. What am I missing?", 'answer': "I completely understand your logic I'll let me help explain. The entire dinner is 20 A maximum. Each channel can handle 10 amps each. For example you can put 10amps on channel 1 and 10amps on channel 2 but if you put any more load on channel 3 or 4 the entire dinner will be overloaded. This allows flexibility if you want more or less loads (beyond just 5amps)... Within the 20amp max total. Hope this helps."}
