{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002MSCC4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 8, 2012', 'unixTime': 1352361600, 'question': 'can you adjust the height while sitting down?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not easily. In my experience, the knob has a lot of tension (so it's tiring to raise it or lower it a lot), and it's quite slow to raise and lower the bench. It makes more sense to adjust it before sitting down. It's not like a lot of office chairs, where it's really easy and quick to go up and down."}
