{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386748800, 'question': 'Includes the power supply?', 'answer': 'Unfortunately no - it runs great on a 9V battery, otherwise you need a special RPS-1 9V adapter; Pro Co makes one: http://www.amazon.com/Pro-Co-Battery-Eliminator-Supply/dp/B0002GZLYM/ref=sr_sp-atf_title_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1386789875&sr=8-1&keywords=RPS-1+9v'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'Will a standard 9 volt power supply work for this (ex: a One Spot daisy chain)?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, but you will need an adapter to fit the RAT's 3.5mm power input. It is correctly oriented in terms of tip and ring. Just look for an adapter to the 1Spot's 1/8th inch output."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'Can you use it as well as Bass Distortion Effect and how it sounds?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes and it sounds pretty good but it definitely has that Rat character. I really like the Hardwire Valve Distortion for my bass.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412578800, 'question': 'What\'s the difference between this pedal and the Pro Co Turbo Rat Distortion Pedal? I\'ve always wondered what the "turbo" offered in terms of sound.', 'answer': 'My understanding is that the Turbo RAT is marketed for those looking for extra "output" - considering that my RAT2 has what seems to me as already having strong output, I can\'t imagine how much more oomph the Turbo gives. Depends on one\'s tastes. It could be too much. Having not played through one though, I can\'t give you a detailed explanation as to how the extra output differentiates the sounds between the two models. However, if you check out youtube, there are some side-by-side demonstrations as to the differences. Hope I could help!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380870000, 'question': 'If possible, how would you compare this to the Big Muff Pi from Electro-Harmonix? I bought that pedal and am not too happy with it.', 'answer': "I personally find the RAT a lot less noisy in my chain and I like the nuances I get from the filter knob and hence the different kinds of distortion I get from it. But then again I guess it's a matter of personal preference and taste. I personally would pick the RAT over the Big Muff anytime but I'm sure there are others out there who think otherwise. Also, if you play on-stage live I really appreciate the clear light on this RAT especially when it's dark on stage. It's a lot easier to change the battery too if you are not connected to a power source. I realise these are not sonic features but as I stated above I am hesitant to say one sounds better than another because it really depends on your taste. I'd recommend you try out a few candidates at the store first to figure out the sound you wanna get and go from there."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002MSQVQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408172400, 'question': 'is it true bypass?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Hi Mark, Please explain what you mean by, "True Bypass". When you press on the pedal, it gives you an awesome distortion effect that you are looking for. This rat pedal is my second rat pedal. The first one was from the earlier generation. If you want distortion, then you should get it. Thanks, Dave'}
