{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0002Y6BJI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'Should you replace all strings if one breaks?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If the string failed due to age and normal wear from usage, then replace them all since many times a new string will not match intonation with the old ones. If , however, it failed due to over tightening or a kink and the set is relatively new, then you may be okay with replacing only the one string.'}
