{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0002ZPLPC', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416902400, 'question': 'Is this open cell or closed cell foam?', 'answer': "I don't think it says on the advert from Amazon wether this product is open or closed cell, it has been a while since I bo it. If I had to guess, I would say open cell. I do not believe that this product is designed to be used outside and does not appear to have any water vapor infiltration properties, it is very flexible and it appears to be designed to be used as primarily as a sound deadener or absorber. Mine was used to construct a round tubular sound baffle for a grow room customer do eliminate the sound of the loud exhaust fans for his grow room. It worked great and saved over a hundred dollars making it myself with over the counter air duct parts from Home Depot Hope this helps"}
