{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006676A0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 17, 2010', 'unixTime': 1289980800, 'question': 'Midi Controllers vs. simple electric keyboards: Can someone please explain to me the difference between getting a midi controller like this one or another electric keyboard?', 'answer': 'A MIDI controller does not produce its own sounds; it primarily controls MIDI information only. For example, I have a Korg N5ex keyboard and software instruments on my computer. The MIDI controller can control the sounds on either the Korg keyboard or the computer software, but it does not have sounds of its own. I could not use the MIDI controller as a stand-alone performance keyboard. One of the advantages of using a MIDI controller is that if you already have the sounds on another keyboard, sound module, or instrument software, you may only need the keys. You can easily save hundreds, if not thousands of dollars for just buying the controller. A fairly decent 88-key MIDI controller can be had for around $500, whereas an 88-key workstation or digital synthesizer/piano can run you into thousands of dollars.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006676A0', 'answerTime': 'May 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368255600, 'question': 'does it work with garageband', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, the M-Audio Keystation 88ES works fine with GarageBand. I believe just about any USB keyboard controller would work with Garageband. Garageband pretty much relies on you having an external keyboard controller to trigger the GB sounds. Work fine with my MacBook Pro.'}
