{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383289200, 'question': 'Does the 30 ohms have the same bass output if it is connected to an amp compare with the 250 ohms?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'So the resistance (Ohms of the headphones) tells you how easy it is to drive the speakers (produce sound). A higher ohms indicates that it is harder to drive the speakers; that being said that higher ohms means that the sound quality is better because there is less garbling of the signal. 30 ohms is standard and is appropriate for basically anything (mp3 players included) the 80 ohm can work with mp3 players but should have a amplifier, the 250 basically is useless without a good amp... if you want to get an amplifier I recommend the Fiio E11 portable amp (approximately 70 USD). Even if you get the 30 ohms DT 770 I am sure you will like it; I recommend getting an amp and higher "ohmage" if you want your music to sound just a bit nicer'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 25, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387958400, 'question': "Anyone know where these are made? Are they made in China like many competitor's models?", 'answer': 'Germany'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382943600, 'question': 'Can anyone clarify exact length of cable? And can they run full Dolby 5.1+/DTS surround or just simulated for movies/gaming?', 'answer': "There just a 2 channel headphone. I would have to stretch the cord out to see. Un-stretched it's about 5ft. I would guess 10-12ft stretched out. I use them for some gaming, but mostly music, make sure you get an amp for it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425542400, 'question': 'can this isolate the ambient sound when you are in the airplane', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Definitely. The dt770 are the best isolating headphones I've owned. Now be aware the 250ohm model will need an amplifier. If you don't want to use an amp get the 32ohm version Or 80ohm version. The lower the ohm the less need for an amp."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'Any issues with ears getting to warm when worn for awhile 2-5 hours?', 'answer': "I haven't exactly found that my ears get warm but I have noticed that sometimes I sweat between the ear cup fabric and my head. The fabric is velvety, FYI. Hasn't been a major issue, I mainly use these when traveling. So I am likely walking around a lot with luggage in warm weather much of the time or sitting on a stuffy airplane."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'On the Beyerdynamic website these headphones have the option of coming with a Limiter. Do these come with a Limiter? Is it just for limiting volume?', 'answer': "These don't have a limiter. The specifics are on Beyerdynamic's website, but I think it either limits volume or limits time at a certain decibel level to meet industry requirements (that being the music producers)."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421049600, 'question': 'If I purchase these 770s @ 250ohms what amp would I need for my Yamaha R-S201 receiver?', 'answer': "I'd start by just plugging right into your receiver and see how you like the sound. some receivers have decent headphone amps, others have horrid ones. I don't know your model, but my Yamaha has the horrid type unfortunately. if you find you don't like the sound, be it too muffled, thin, or lifeless, then add an amp. there are many you can add. I run mine on a schiit vali and I love the pairing. the schiit magni is a good amp as well, more versatile than the vali. there is the jds labs o2 amp, and many many more. you'll need a line out from your receiver though. I was shocked to learn mine did not have any line level outs, so I had to run an optical out to an optical dac, and connect my headphone amp to the dac."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421308800, 'question': 'Why are there 3 different ohm options? What differs between them?', 'answer': "the 32ohm version is made to be run off just about anything, and still retain good volume and dynamics. the 80ohm is tuned for a bit more bass than the other models. at 80ohm it sits on the border of needing or not needing an amp. I personally thought it needed one when I listened to it out of my phone. the 250ohm definitely needs an amp, and is the most balanced sounding of the 3 versions. it's far from a balanced headphone though. I only say balanced in comparison to the other ohm versions of the same headphone. the 250ohm version is really made for a studio plugged into monitoring equipment. doesn't mean you cant use it at home, but you have to have an amp. just remember this with headphones, the lower the ohm, the more likely it will sound good just plugged right into a source. as the ohm goes up, volume and dynamics start to suffer, to the point that a separate amp will be required. if you don't want to use an amp, get the 32ohm."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417852800, 'question': 'how comfortable are they when you wear glasses?', 'answer': 'Well the ear holes are pretty big so I imagine they would be as comfortable as any if not more.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0006NL5SM', 'answerTime': 'Aug 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376118000, 'question': 'Will my LG Optimus G E970 power them?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Not the 250 ohm. If you want to use them with a phone, I'd suggest the 32 Ohm version; get the Limited Edition if you can find them, they are nice. But if you are using a phone as your primary source, and want something on par SQ wise and more portable, check out the Sennheiser HD25 or Amperior. Both are more easily driven, and more portable too, with a similar V-shaped response to the DT770. Their sound is less spacious, but I prefer them to the DT770 when both are driven by my Nexus 4 (same chipset as your optimus G)."}
