{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006ODWUU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1365750000, 'question': 'Question: Is this microphone wireless??', 'answer': 'The WB98H/C plugs into a "body pack" (sold separately) that attaches to your hip and transmits a wireless signal. If you want to use it as a wired mic, it requires a Shure RPM626 preamp (sold separately). This mic requires one or the other: a body pack or a preamp. The primary market for this mic is people who will use it wirelessly.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0006ODWUU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'I have a shure headset wireless transmitter model T 1G-CL is my question is is the shure wb98h/c intrument mic is compatible or say is it gonna work ?', 'answer': 'YES 99.9% chance it will work, presuming your transmitter is mini XLR input. All Shure mini XLR wireless connectors (that I am aware of) are configured/wired the same.'}
