{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00079DRUO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': 'My stand came with the smaller arm holes the same width apart. The leg holes are not the same width. Do I have the right pieces?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The instructions are horrible. There are two holes close and two hole further away on the ends of the stand. This is correct. If you attach the wrong side, the other will not align correctly. You probably have the right pieces, just attaching it in the wrong order. The narrow holes legs get attached INSIDE the stand part with the wider holes (the nuts both face inward). So in the end, the left upper and right lower side are narrow hole, the upper right side and lower left side are wide hole. Hope this helps.'}
