{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0007WOX1S', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421222400, 'question': 'Hello, I am deciding between this auto harp and the OS150FCE Acoustic Electric Auto Harp. Does this one have the FT600 Fine Tuning?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I really like this auto harp, but it does NOT have fine tuning. I haven't had any problems fine tuning it myself though - just a laborious process and needs to be done frequently in the first few months."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0007WOX1S', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383202800, 'question': 'when electric is the harp also acoustic.will it come with EQ and fine tuning', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Just like an acoustic/electric guitar, when unplugged the acoustic characteristics of the instrument are the sole source of sound. When plugged in, the acoustic properties are the same as when unplugged, but would easily be overrun by the amplified sound. However, to the player, depending on where you are relative to the speakers, the "acoustic" sound would still be heard. The EQ has four bands (low, med, high, presence) that naturally only come into play when playing through an amplifier. The fine tuning feature was part of the reason I bought this harp, but in reality I rarely use it.'}
