{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0009FZWMC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427698800, 'question': 'Would there be a problem to purchase these and use them on a solid body non baritone guitar for a heavier sound?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have these strings on a non baritone Schecter Hellraiser Deluxe set up and tuned to B Standard tuning. It is absolutely amazing to play and sounds incredible. I took my guitar to a reputable luthier and guitar technician to get it professionally set up with the baritone strings about 2 years ago and it still plays wonderfully.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0009FZWMC', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381993200, 'question': 'I play a classical baritone guitar, and it is supposed to use nylon strings. Do you have this kind of strings?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'we do sell Nylon strings. you can do a search for our store on amazon, and you would be able to find them there. Hope that helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0009FZWMC', 'answerTime': 'Jun 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370761200, 'question': 'I\'ve ordered a 27" scale neck-thru baritone guitar with a Floyd. I\'ll tune to B or lower. Should I go with these? My concern is the locking nut and floyd accepting the thicker strings. I don\'t want to have to modify the nut or bridge to be able to fit...', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "These are very good strings. I put them on a Hellcat VI, which has a 30' scale, when I wanted to use it as a true baritone. Looking at Ernie Ball baritone strings, they are 13-72, as where these are 14-68. I doubt you would have to make any permanent mods to the nut or bridge to use these. I hope this helps. Cheers!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0009G1E0K', 'answerTime': 'Jan 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390204800, 'question': "What guitars will this strap work on? Would like to order the guitar for dummies but it doesn't come with a strap", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It should work with any guitar that has strap studs. These are the little chrome knobs at the bottom and usually the top of the guitar body. You must have 2 studs to use this strap.'}
