{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009W0BDA', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425110400, 'question': "What's the best way to connect the MX200 to a Boss BR1200CD digital recorder?", 'answer': 'The only connections on the back of the MX200 are 1/4" Analogue ins and outs, a midi in/out, S/PDIF in & out, and a USB port. Since the Boss BR1200 has all of those connections also, you pretty much just need to get whichever cabling that you prefer. Myself, I use the 1/4" Analogue ins and outs because I still do my recording in the analogue realm, then mix down to digital. If you want true digital, then the midi in/out, S/PDIF in/out, or the USB port would be your best bet. The Lexicon MX200 also comes with a CD to install the unit via USB cable to the recorder itself, to where you can use the MX200 like a virtual effect. Hope this helps.'}
