{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009XPMOM', 'answerTime': 'Apr 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397804400, 'question': 'dose it come with extra strings and a cable ?', 'answer': "It doesn't come with extra strings. Bass strings last longer than guitar strings. I changed the original round-wound strings for some GHS Black Nylon Tape Wounds, to give is a sound more like a stand-up bass. Plus they look really cool on this bass. No cable is included."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0009XPMOM', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394953200, 'question': "IS there a certain style it's goof for?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have found that it isn't a particular style, but rather in what is required by way of tuning. If your are tuned to an E standard no problem, but Eb or drop D then you might have an issue with the pickup."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0009XPMOM', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': "Purchased this bass guitar 10/2/14.On 11/19/14 one of the screws which holds machine head in place sheared off.Guitar can't be tuned. What do we do?", 'answer': "You can order 3rd party machine heads from Amazon, Musican's Friend, ect. and install them yourself or you can contact dean support. If you want to pay to shipping to their warehouse then they will probably fix it. That being said, shipping a bass is expensive and replacing them yourself or having you local guitar store do it will be easier, faster and cheaper."}
