{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000A2HOB6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': "I am very sensitive to high pitches and tones. I'm looking for warm low mellow strings. Which set of strings (type and gauge) do you recommend?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Phospher bronze are fairly even toned. No extreme highs or lows Nice and even'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000A2HOB6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': "I've just purchased a Martin 00-15M (folk size all mahogany tone woods). What would be the ideal gauge string for it?", 'answer': "I would personally use 11 starting on e first string. Which would be about a medium. 12's are ok but if you barr chord or bend notes they're kind of heavy. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000A2HOB6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391932800, 'question': 'What is the best sounding guitar string for my Martin and my Ibanez and not so hard on the fingers', 'answer': 'Are they full body guitars? I prefer Medium gauge strings for a full body guitar...if you pick a lot, light gauge are more flexible for bending. Light or Medium gauge strings should be okay on the fingers. Remember that the more you play the harder you build the callouses on the fingers putting pressure on the strings. Hope this helps. :)'}
