{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000BQ79W0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': "Does this mic works with only specific types of cameras or can be used generally? I'm regrettably ignorant about this type of stuff.", 'answer': "It can't be used on any dsrl camera because of 2 factors 1 it is a professional microphone with xlr connection that belong to amps, consoles and recorders like the TASCAM D40 which I own. 2 even if you get the adapter to plug it to the camera its a phantom type of microphone which need extra energy to work. Im sure you should buy the Audio Technica ATR6550 that can be pluged to the camera or computer. I do videos but I record the audio separated for better perfomance just need a little work of synchronization."}
