{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000CZ0RLK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393056000, 'question': "What's the difference between this and the C-3?", 'answer': 'The C-1 is a directional microphone, best used for vocals (singing, rapping) because it only picks up in one direction and ignores pretty much everything else. The C-3 is a Dual-Diaphragm Condenser mic, so it has 3 settings, it can pick up sound all around it, front back and then it has a similar setting to be used as a directional mic. Basically it gives you a few more options, but the C-1 is pretty good if you only want a directional mic.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000CZ0RLK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2007', 'unixTime': 1171612800, 'question': 'Does this need a phantom power adapter, or how does it draw power?', 'answer': 'This microphone does require phantom power. My board provides +48 V and it works flawlessly.'}
