{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000EE8YPK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380610800, 'question': 'is this worked on piano?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it should work on any stringed instrument, including a piano. However, tuning a piano is difficult, and best left to a professional tuner. But tuning a guitar or ukulele is quite easy.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000EE8YPK', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371020400, 'question': 'Will it tune saxes and clarinets', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It should be able to tune anything. It tells you the note it is "hearing" relative to A440 concert pitch that orcestras tune to. If you play a trnsposing instrument like a clarinet or sax, you need to make the adjustment yourself, just as you would when playing with an orchestra or band. I hope tis helps.'}
