{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000FMDIXY', 'answerTime': 'Dec 13, 2012', 'unixTime': 1355385600, 'question': 'Do you need to have a stand for this pad?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You don't need a stand, but it's better if you have one. You could rest the practice pad on your lap or on a chair. Mounting it in a snare drum stand is the best way to use this practice pad, as it allows you to sit comfortably (properly), and adjust the height and angle of the practice pad...so I would highly recommend getting a snare drum stand with this practice pad."}
