{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000FVZUFO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390032000, 'question': "I'd like to use this as a spot light for a comedy show. Anyone use it as a spot light?", 'answer': 'I don\'t feel that this light is bright enough, white enough, or sharp enough to be used as a spot. Despite the P36 name and "pin-spot" claims, I use my P36\'s as wash lights only. If you\'re looking for an LED spot but can\'t spend the $250-$500 for a proper one, the best solution I\'ve found is to look at the 15W LED gobo projectors. If the venue is small and dark enough, these can give decent results and actually look like a spot. Find one with zoom capabilities and you can even change the spot size and hardness of the edge.'}
