{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000GBAR5G', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382511600, 'question': 'Is this guitar worth using for a black metal/sludge/noise project?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Purely on its own, without inflection from any processing FX? Probably not. But no guitar is, really - is it? This guitar can handle being heavily processed though, so if you have outboard FX, or FX running on a computer, this guitar will give you the s/n ratio you need. I've used this through an old Roland GP8 multiFX processor, a Floor Pod and Native Instruments Guitar Rig and it holds up pretty well. If you're after speed picking, I'd say go with something more refined - this guitar is a great workhorse, but it is crudely constructed. I lucked out with the one I bought, but I've talked to people who've ordered the same guitar and gotten a dog - malformed fretwork being a particular complaint, and just the thing to kill speed picking."}
