{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J0N5TY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404630000, 'question': 'Does it come with a Mount Microphone Clip', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If you are talking about a clip that you screw on to the end to slide a microphone in then no it doesn't sadly. Only the spot to screw on a clip or screw on your mic"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J0N5TY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389427200, 'question': 'Can this mic hold up the Blue Snowball?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Out of the box: No. The proLine is a straight threaded mounting intended for use with a shock mount assembly that articulates. The bottom mount on the Snowball won't give you the correct angle. You are better off with the standard desk stand that come with the Snowball."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Aug 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375599600, 'question': 'what is the difference between H7, K7, M7?', 'answer': 'I did a Google search for "h7 k7 m7 shure" and turned up a Yahoo article that referenced this on the Shure site: http://shure.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/3392 ... when I purchased mine, I was thinking that I shouldn\'t get multiple sets in the same bands, but seeing that article, I\'m glad my city isn\'t listed. There is also a frequency finder link on that page as well.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Dec 3, 2012', 'unixTime': 1354521600, 'question': 'Is the receiver battery powered or AC?', 'answer': 'The reciever is AC plug in. The one I purchased is 110v AC. The Transmitters are 9v DC.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Oct 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381820400, 'question': 'Can you i use two transmitter mics with one receiver?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No only one microphone at a time can be used.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362470400, 'question': 'would this work well with canon t4i outdoors?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This has a 1/4" mono output which could be converted into another size with an adapter for receiving the audio. Otherwise, if you are looking to have the cameras mic sent, it uses a micro-XLR which would be very hard to convert, but it\'s possible. I believe there would be better solutions.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': "Is this a stand alone system with it's own speakers? We have no sound system.", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you need an amplified speaker system, this only gets you the wireless microphone.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425024000, 'question': 'Does the microphone have a spring clip on it? To attach to the speakers clothing? And is it discreet?', 'answer': 'Yes it does and it is barely visible to the audience.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'can this work with with a pyro pro microphone? http://www.amazon.com/Pyle-Pro-PMEMS1...', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'There are 2 channels only one device per channel, 1 channel at a time. As long as the mike is the same frequency as one of them it should work.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390464000, 'question': 'can I use this product outside the USA?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There should not be any reason as to why this owuld not work outside the US. this does not broadcast at any signals that would interfere with anything else. Esentially this would have as much interference as a cordless home phone. Make sire you get a power adapter that will fit non standard power outlets.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': 'is this work directly with regular computer for recoding?how(specify adapter) to make the sound also go into a speakers system for a big conference?', 'answer': 'The microphone has an output that can be plugged directly into a sound system or a computer. For a sound system you would use a mono 1/4 chord or a low impedence microphone cable depending on the type of imput the sound system uses. To use with a computer you would need a mini plug adapter to connect to the computer thru the line in jack.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J36ETE', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374908400, 'question': 'I want to plug this into my computer to record. I have the 1/4 to 1/8 adapter. Is that all I need and will it work well in that setup?', 'answer': 'It should work if the jack you are plugging it into can handle a microphone signal.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': 'What of the tone of this metronome ?', 'answer': 'It makes a ticking noise, and you can set it to 2, 3, 4, or 6/4 times, where a high pitched bell (ding) rings on the downbeat.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391760000, 'question': 'No Batteries, Great What powers it, not a wind-up is it?', 'answer': 'It IS a wind-up. A word of caution, this metronome is LOUD.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'I want a metronome that I can set to have no downbeat bell or other noise for the down beat-just a steady click-click. Can this one do that?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. It just goes click click. you can se it for a ONE two three four, but I just leave it clicking the quarter beats. I love it. It's really a good metronome, considering it is almost all plastic. But it's sturdy plastic."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421308800, 'question': 'Mine just arrived with no user manual. How do I set the time? If I want 80, do I line up the top of the pendulum with the 80 mark?', 'answer': 'To set the tempo: move the sliding weight up or down and line the top at the desired tempo. ( directly from the user manual )'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': "I don't know how to open the cover. It seems to get stuck.", 'answer': 'Use fingernail at top and pull straight out toward you.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Um....how can I tell what "time" it is? 2/4, 3/4 or 4/4 time...it came with NO directions.....', 'answer': 'On the right side of the device, there is a plunger that you pull out for 2/4, 3/4, 4/4, or 6/8 time. It controls how often you hear the "DING". There are number markings on the plunger.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410418800, 'question': 'Where is this product made?', 'answer': 'It is stamped on the bottom "made in China". I gave this supplier an out but he choose profit over integrity. This a very poorly quality controlled item. The supplier is penny wise and dollar foolish.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'can this metronome continue playing for about 9 minutes?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391241600, 'question': 'Can I adjust the volume? How loud does it get? I would like to sing with the tempo.', 'answer': 'You cannot adjust the volume, but it is pretty loud. I have no problem hearing it over my guitar. This is something that was important to me because the electronic ones are soft.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J4I9VO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407740400, 'question': 'Just clarifying.... it can make a bell sound at the 1st downbeat of a measure? Different time signatures?', 'answer': "Hi Raffi, yes, this metronome sounds a bell on the downbeat, accommodating meters with 2 beats to the measure, 3 beats to the measure, 4 beats to the measure, and 6 beats to the measure, as well, as a constant, rhythmic ticking with no bell sound at all. All of these options are easily available with the pull of a little silver rod on the side of the unit, and each option is easily marked to satisfy any of your needs. I am very grateful for the affordability of this fine 'instrument'!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413183600, 'question': 'Does this mixer support 48V Phantom Power?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. It does have phantom power.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407740400, 'question': 'i am not sure if i need this, PLEASE ADVISE, i have two technical pro powered monitors and a powered bass box..i was told to get a preamp.', 'answer': 'Check out the specks on the Xenyx. I think it has only one preamp. Also check your other equipment to see if they have preamps built into their systems. Any mixer is mainly for routing multiple units to the amps and then on to the speakers or speaker/amps. Most mixers have preamps as part of their input system but not all the inputs are preamps. You can usually tell by the xlr inputs which are always preamps. Juts make sure your mixer has the amount of preamps you need, but most amplifiers now have preamps built in. Feel free to emailme with more info about your system or what you want to do and I will be glad to help you. John'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': "I didn't really understand the inputs on this mixer. So I have 3 electric guitars, and an electronic drum kit. Can all of these,with mic,be connected?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "This mixer does not have sufficient mono channels for your application. Channels 2-3 and 4-5 are stereo inputs (meaning they are contolled with the same fader). Some of the larger Xenyx mixers will get you the inputs you need.... something with at least 5 distinct faders to control each instrument's mix individually. Hope this helps. :-)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'Could I hook the Line Out from my Kawai Piano and the Headphone Out from my Laptop and use one set of Headphones?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'All you need to do is buy some 1/4 inch to RCA plugs and plug those into the line inputs and you can plug in the line out from your piano and the line out from your laptop into the mixer. I exchanged the this model for the one with eight inputs because I wanted two microphone inputs, but it has the same kind of line inputs and I just plugged in those adapters and they did the trick. I used two RCA adapters on the mike inputs also to record some security microphones which had RCA plugs, and I used some XLR to TRS adapters to plug in my old microphones instead of buying new ones.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391328000, 'question': "Can this mixer use two microphones at the same time? How would you hook up two Audio-Technica ATR2100's into this?", 'answer': 'It could conceivably be done if you used an XLR-to-dual 1/4" adapter and ran it into either of the stereo faders, but I don\'t recommend it. You\'d be better off with the Xenyx 802 because it has 2 XLR inputs and you wouldn\'t need to McGyver your second mic.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'Can this mixer connect to a PC via a soundcard?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, to an analog soundcard. All you need is a 1/8" stereo to dual-RCA cord. Mixer has both input and output RCA capability, so you could feed the output of the mixer to the line/mic of the soundcard or feed the output of the soundcard (line out/speaker out) to the input of the mixer. There is also a headphone jack on the mixer so that could also be patched back to the soundcard\'s line in/mic. For me, I am usually running the PC speaker out to the mixer RCA input -- the volume is controlled by the Main, and then I can either use headphones from the mixer or run the 1/4" output into my guitar amp. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382857200, 'question': 'does this power the microphone MXL 990?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It powers my 990 just fine.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': '29 days ago', 'question': 'Can use a Dynamic Mic with out 48v like the SM58 Microphone?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you could...not sure about recording with that type of mic though. Maybe for a small performance or something. But again it would be better to use a studio recording microphone. that dynamic mic you would need the jack for that type of mic.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408345200, 'question': 'does this work with phantom powered microphones?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, the XLR input has phantom power. It's always on. I.e. There is no switch to turn on or off the phantom power."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5UEGQ', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381388400, 'question': 'Can I use this with a USB Mic?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. You need either a mic with a XLR connection or Hi-Z (1/4")'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Aug 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377586800, 'question': 'does this come with a/c power?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. Mine included an AC cord and seems to work fine. I did notice on a couple of the pots that you should turn down the volume while adjusting as it sometimes gives a rather loud pop that can be very loud in headphones but once you have it stable at the level of choice, the mixer works great. Good solution at low cost for a small studio.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'May 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401433200, 'question': 'Does "2 Bus Mixer" mean that two inputs (eg guitar and vocal) can be separated in a recording software? Thanks!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'You could if you in put mic in 1 channel with balance all the way 1 direction, and then guitar in another channel with the balance all the way the other direction. You would then have 2 seperated mono recordings. Easily edited in recording software.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Jun 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403593200, 'question': 'How many microphones can I connect to the mixers. Will it be able to have 4?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can. only 2 with Phantom power.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396076400, 'question': 'Does it come with the cable to plug it in to the computer, and i have an usb mic what kinda jack should i buy for it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, mine came with cable to connect to computer. This unit is designed for use with r microphones, not USB mics.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'a/c power 110~220 50~60 hz?', 'answer': "The power pack says: Behringer Eurorack Power Supply Model MXUL3 Item No: PSU-MX3-UL-01 Input: 120 VAC/ 60 Hz/ 13W Output 1: 2 X 18.5 VAC/2 X 250 mA Output 2: 3.0 VAC/100 mA I've got it plugged in to a standard 110V household current outlet (American). Hope that helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Dose this have phantom power? How much?', 'answer': 'Yes, it does have phantom power; the other answer is wrong. +48V per the official documentation.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379055600, 'question': 'Is a direct box needed or recommended for guitars to use with this mixer, or not necessary?', 'answer': 'No direct box needed. The unit has regular guitar cord inputs & two XLR mic inputs that you "could" use with a direct box if you had some reason to do so but as it stands, just plug in and play.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Jun 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403506800, 'question': 'CAN I INTERFACE MY PRO TOOLS THROUGH IT', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, it goes like this.. Your computer (USB) to interface. From interface (left right 1/4 speaker cable output) to 1/4 line/input on this behringer mixer. Then from the mixer (output) to your subwoofer, then from subwoofer to left/right monitors.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397631600, 'question': "If I connect a guitar amplifier to this via the amp's headphone jack using 1/4' male to male cable will it damage the board?", 'answer': 'A guitar amp\'s headphone, fx send, or aux out will all give you a line level signal that will be just fine going direct into the board with a 1/4" instrument or 1/4" balanced cable. However, the "amplifier out" powered output from a guitar amp will damage the board.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5XS3C', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': 'My home theater system does not have a mic input. Do i need this if i want to use a microphone?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, this would definitely be one way to adapt a home theatre amplifier to allow any microphone through it using the multiple Mic inputs. It even had phantom power so it can literally handle any Mic you hook to it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Can you use the Equalizer that is on Mono mike inputs on sterio inputs 5/6 thu 11/12. (Xenyx 802 has Equalizer usage on sterio inputs 3/4 5/6)', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The Behringer 1202 mixer does not have equalizers on the stereo inputs. It only has them on the mic inputs. Most anything that you will use with this mixer on the stereo inputs will have its own equalizer. The mic inputs have a three band equalizer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'How do I monitor the sound with headphones? Is there a headphone jack?', 'answer': 'Yes there is, you probably need an adapter for the headphone jack! It comes as a 1/4 inch RCA slot that you will need an adapter (1/4 -Inch Stereo Jack into Mini(3.5mm) or (2.5mm)Stereo Jack!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421654400, 'question': 'is there way to be able to plug this into a computer to record?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The Behringer Xenyx 1202 does not have the USB interface. It does have RCA jacks that interface directly to a computer sound card, or you can get a USB adapter. I have used both the Behringer UCA222 and the Dell line input of my sound card for good results with this mixer. If you would prefer, there is a version of this mixer (I believe it to be the Behringer 1204) that has the build in USB interface.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'How many channels can be used at the same time? Planning to use with 7 mics for recording drums. Thanks.', 'answer': 'About 8 channels.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419235200, 'question': 'Is this actually a powered mixer?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'no'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Nov 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415520000, 'question': 'is this a good mixer for the behringer 215d speakers', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am not familiar with the behringer 215d speakers, however, they appear to have a 1/4" input that you could set to line. This mixer, the BEHRINGER XENYX 1202, has 1.4" line outputs. The Speakers theoretically should work with the mixer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Oct 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413097200, 'question': "I am new at this.. how many in's and how many out's?", 'answer': "I'm not sure what you're referring to. The question is too vague. In and out of what?"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412924400, 'question': 'All I need is something to plug my condenser mic into, would this work fine or over the top for me?', 'answer': 'It should work just fine with the XLR inputs, although it only has 1/4" and RCA out, no XLR out.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Sep 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411455600, 'question': 'Also a newcomer here. Will this and most Behringers plug directly into my computer? I would use this for podcasting on a mac using garageband. Thanks', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You will need the correct cable to connect the sound output from your computer to this mixer. Most likely you can use the correct connection for your computer to an unbalanced 1/4" input on this mixer. For example 1/8" TRS miniplug (headphone type) split into two 1/4" connections such as this: http://www.amazon.com/Hosa-CMP153-Cable-Inch-Dual/dp/B000068O3C/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1411535734&sr=8-1&keywords=1%2F8%22+to+1%2F4%22+unbalanced'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y282', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410764400, 'question': 'This is a "stand alone" powered amp/mixer? For this price doesn\'t seem possible . What am I missing?', 'answer': "You're not missing anything. It's a great little mixer, as advertised. The mic preamps are very nice as well. You don't get a built in USB interface, but that's about all you're missing. It's a very nice board, and I use mine daily :)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y214', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'Is this effects mixer good for Karaoke?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, there are 99 effects on the mixer. I use it for karaoke and for my instruments. Here's a list of the effects. http://www.soh.cz/data_images/Image/pronajem/manual/XENYX-1202FXcz.PDF I recommend it if it's for family get togethers and parties. I really enjoy it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000J5Y214', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': "Can you apply the digital effects to just certain inputs like 2 mics, but leave the music alone? I'm looking to upgrade from the 802 without FX.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I believe there is an fx knob on each channel so you can add as much or as little fx as you want. You can only use 1 setting at a time. You can't put reverb on one track and chorus on another. You get 1 fx for all the tracks."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000J5Y214', 'answerTime': 'Aug 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408777200, 'question': 'How can I connect wireless Microphones to this mixer', 'answer': 'You would connect the output from the wireless receiver to any of the inputs of the mixer. No other way. Run the output to any one (or two for stereo) of the inputs instead of going to a speaker system or amplifier. Then the output of the mixer would go to an amplifier for the speaker system. Hope this helps.'}
