{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000JLU26W', 'answerTime': 'Feb 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359705600, 'question': 'How exactly does this hook an Ipad to a MIDI keyboard (musical instrument) ? It looks like you need a USB adapter?', 'answer': "You would use Apple's Camera Connector Kit, which plus in to the dock connector on the bottom of the iPad (1-3 models) and then provides a USB port. This would hook up to that, and is it doesn't take too much power, it may work. I have plugged up USB keyboards to the iPad that way, but never an adapter. The iPad USB port has limited power, so if this adapter draws too much, it will not work. In that case, you would plug a powered USB hub (that plugs in to wall power) in to the camera connector kit, then plug this in to that. I have not tested that, but I have plugged up USB joysticks and such to an adapter I built in to the USB port on the iPad just fine."}
