{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000M3DZHA', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422604800, 'question': 'Will this stand fit a 88-keys digital piano measured at 3.5 x 50 x 11?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Hi David, I like this stand very much. It's light weight, no tools needed to set up or break down, and my piano stays put even when I play with a heavy hand. I have a Yamaha P-35. 88 keys. 52 3/16 (L) x 11 5/8 (D) x 6 1/16 (H) WEIGHT 25.6 LBS. I hope this was helpful. Judy T."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000M3DZHA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419840000, 'question': 'I have a Yamaha YPG-235. Will this stand work well for this piano?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Hi Cassandra, I don't know the dimensions of your YPG-235 but my P-35 measures 52 3/16 long,11 5/8 wide, and 6 1/16 high. It weighs 25.6 pounds. I love this stand. It is so simple and light but extremely sturdy. If you play very hard it handles it well. The piano does not jump around at all. It's very easy to adjust the height. It breaks down and sets up in a second. No tools needed. From 1-10 I would give it a 10! Judy T."}
