{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OMG0KI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': 'I have an Ovation Elite which has non traditional epaulet sound holes. How could I use this product to humidify my guitar?', 'answer': 'The humidipak just rests in the guitar case, not in the instrument itself so it should be ideal for your Ovavtion. I use this for a lute which has a rosette (no open sound hole) and it works great.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OMG0KI', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'is this the newest version, will this fit good in a Grand Auditorium Guitar? Are they easy to take out, Thanks', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It is the newest version if it comes in brown wrappers; this packaging looks like the one I ordered, so yes, this is the newest version. I used them in my Taylor Dreadnought 110e, and they fit fine and came out very easily. They didn't last as long as the older version although we did have very low humidity in VA this winter."}
