{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OR6HS8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418716800, 'question': 'on acustic guitar,wich strings style have a better crystal clear sound?', 'answer': 'I think Phosphor Bronze does.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000OR6HS8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420790400, 'question': 'I need to buy the string #6 for an acoustc guitar. Will this item get me a 6th string?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Firstly, I'm assuming you know that strings are traditionally numbered from bottom to top, smallest to largest. Secondly, I don't know anybody that sells individual strings. Typically, even if they did, it would do no good, as the strings will not sound good unless they are all fresh and clean and very similar to each other. Believe me, you mix new and worn (stretched) strings together, you're likely to make dogs howl and people with good pitch perception cringe!"}
