{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000OY4WA6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371711600, 'question': 'What cable do I need to connect it to a Roland RD 150 electric piano? What cord do I need to plug it into 220 volt electricity overseas?', 'answer': 'It has three channels. Channel one has a choice of and "XLR" three pin input, like most microphones use or a 1/4 inch "guitar" cable. The other two channels use 1/4 inch only inputs. Every keyboard I\'ve ever seen has a 1/4 inch jack, so you\'d just need a guitar cable. If I were going to Europe, I\'d get a wall socket converter that could handle the wattage (32 watts), which is not very much. (Different countries use different systems, so be careful.) It requires about half the power of a 60w light bulb. Hope this helps.'}
