{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000PARIZU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': 'Would this be good for my granddaughter who likes to sing, I thought she could record herself and play back. Is this what I need?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "For singing, I wouldn't recommend this for someone who would just be starting. If she knows her way around sound equipment and software then I'd definitely recommend this or something of equal quality for the price. The microphone itself can only interface the computer through the mixer and then the USB hookup. This provides better quality than some other microphones when configured properly, but it's also more sensitive and will require a stand, and pop filter, which are not included in the set. I spent no more than $150 on this and the other equipment I bought for the purpose of live-streaming on the internet. Overall I'm highly satisfied with the use and quality i've gotten out of behringer products, but for your purposes I'm unsure of wether this is the best option."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000PARIZU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388304000, 'question': 'Is it compatible for Windows 7 &amp; 8?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It's compatible for both 32 and 64 bit versions of 7. Not sure if it is for 8, but you can Google it to find out if this is compatible with 8. Since it's USB, it might, but with 8 fairly new, it may not be yet. Behringer has both 32 and 64 bit drivers on their site for everything including 7. Didn't see anything for 8 yet."}
