{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000PGMSZY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389168000, 'question': "how do I operate this unit with phantom power so I don't have dissassemble to install a 9v battery? do I need a speacial cable ???/", 'answer': 'No, the phantom power should come from your sound board through your microphone cable. It does not need a special cable. There is a phantom power button on analog sound boards and on digital boards it will usually have phantom power for each individual channel.'}
