{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Q87DAQ', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422604800, 'question': 'what is difference between LO Diatonic and Melody maker harmonicas?', 'answer': 'If the melody maker is like the Hohner Golden Melody, they use a more exact tuning so they are good for first position "straight harp" styles where you play more melodies as opposed to riffing. This does not mean that you can not play them in second position (cross harp for blues and rock), but they are also very good for folk and country. Although the tuning is slightly different, I have not really noticed much difference in playing, though they seem to have a more clean sound but not much different.'}
