{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000RW0GT6', 'answerTime': 'Oct 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382511600, 'question': 'i have short fingers, will i be able to play this guitar?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have short fat fingers and it's my favorite guitar to play. I had a takamine that I disliked immensely because of the narrow fretboard. The short fingers should not make a big difference. Good luck."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000RW0GT6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383289200, 'question': 'Would this be a good beginner choice for my 13 year old daughter? She is an accomplished piano player and begging for a guitar.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The "Seagull S6 Original" has a slightly larger nut width than your typical guitar "approximately 1/8 of an inch wider at the top of the neck near the tuners" which makes this guitar great for players with large hands and people that play finger style. However, many players just prefer this width. It\'s my opinion that since she is an accomplished piano player with excellent finger dexterity, this guitar will be a very good choice. Please keep in mind that this is a full size dreadnaught body so if she is small in physical size, ANY full size dread could be a problem. Take her to a music store and have her try ANY full size dread just for fit. If you can swing the few extra dollars, go for a Godin Seagull SWS Maritime guitar, http://seagullguitars.com/seagull_maritime_series.html No matter what guitar you go with, keep $40.00 set aside for a guitar action job "setup". Almost ALL new guitars straight off the show room floor have high string action. ALSO, since she should already know music theory, skip paying for guitar lessons and get her "Gibson\'s Learn and Master Guitar". She should tear through it. Amazon cost is $125 As for the build and material "quality" of the S6, you can\'t go wrong, she will grow with it for many years.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000RW0GT6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406876400, 'question': 'left handed', 'answer': 'I am not left handed, but I know that the S6 is available for left handed people.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000RW0GT6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 26, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422259200, 'question': "What is the difference in playing between a Seagull S6 and a Seagull S6 slim? I'm a beginner and I don't know which one is better for me.", 'answer': 'Hi, I can only tell you my experience with the S6 Original, I absolutely love it! I\'m a beginner too, female, in my forties. I\'m 5\'7" and medium build, I would say I have average sized hands. This guitar sounds so amazing, it has such a rich beautiful tone, I never felt like it was too wide or big to comfortably play. Hope this helps.'}
