{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000TNBFS4', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': 'Is this a solid spruce top ? And is there a truss rod ?', 'answer': "I believe this is a very good laminate top. It looks great and I can't find a seam between pieces, but it is slightly thicker that my solid top classical guitars both cedar and spruce. I've seen many acoustical electrics both steel string and nylon with laminated tops. If a guitar is well made, laminates sound very good. Even many high end guitars have laminated tops. Yes, the OC11CE also has a truss rod. The guitar sounds good. I started with high tension Augustine Blues, but I think the medium tension Augustine Reds are a better fit for this instrument sound wise."}
