{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000UJHIS8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'Will this work as an expression pedal with the Line 6 M13? Is a "volume pedal" the same thing as an "expression pedal"?', 'answer': "A volume pedal is usually one that you insert in line with your AUDIO signal to allow volume changes. Those have two jacks so you can put them into the signal path. An Expression pedal usally means that it has a single 1/4 plug on the end which is meant to go into the 'control voltage' jack of a keyboard (as opposed to a sustain pedal plug attached which goes into the jack of the keyboard or controller). That will allow you to control more than just volume depending how your keyboard allows you to assign that jack. But the point is - you need a 'control' input for this pedal."}
