{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UJHIS8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411023600, 'question': 'Will this work as a volume control with my Korg keyboard?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Almost certainly. I use one of these with both a Yamaha and a Nord and it works great for both. In general, keyboard control pedals are pretty universal. Sustain pedals vary in default polarity, but generally not control pedals. And even for sustain pedals, keyboards are designed these days to detect the default polarity.'}
