{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000UMLDA4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1420012800, 'question': 'Is the action high?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I measured mine. The action (or string height) on my Ami at the 12 fret is: approximately 3mm for the treble E string (that's standard classical height), and approximately 4.5mm for the bass E string (maybe 0.5 mm higher than standard classical height). Great projection and no buzzes anywhere, using phosphor bronze lightweight strings -- straight out of the box with no custom setup. Perfect for me. If you want to lower the action, you can sand down the bottom of the bridge saddle (the action is already quite low at the nut). Your local guitar shop can do that for you. It's not expensive."}
