{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000VTFQCM', 'answerTime': 'Jan 5, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420444800, 'question': 'i have two 15s being powered by a gli xa-2200 amp and it is running from my american dj dj controller. can i run my speakers through this and how', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "You would want to run the sound through this device before the amp. What I do is I have my mixer's left and right sent to input 1 and 2 and then send the outputs directly to the amp. Some people likely use the 2 processors as sends from their mixers, but I wanted to process the whole output instead of just one member of the band."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000VTFQCM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412751600, 'question': 'Would I benefit from this in a PA system that already includes a 2 channel 15 band EQ?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The result is definitely different than an EQ. The bass channel is more like an overdrive that doesn't clip (hard to describe it's not distortion) and the high-end is this subtle octave harmonizer. I was very impressed with the inprovement on early 90's gangsta rap that sounds muddy. We use it for our live electronic band to make our sound less muddy and it's really be a big help. I'm not sure it would make a different on the latest music releases though."}
