{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000VYHKO4', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'is this actual string for pianos?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This wire can be used for a Single note on some pianos. You have to measure the diameter of the wire and compare them. The lower notes have additional wire wrapped around them and this wire will not work unless you happen to have the means to perform the wrapping.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000VYHKO4', 'answerTime': 'Oct 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381129200, 'question': 'Is this wire the same as used for forming fish hooks?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I am guessing that it is a trade secret. However, it is high carbon steel and can be tempered, like a fish hook. We use it in picture framing for holding 3-d objects in place in shadowbox framing. We use polyolefin heat shrink tubing over the exposed ends so as to not damage the object being framed.'}
