{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000WKW59C', 'answerTime': 'Feb 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392451200, 'question': "What are the recording lengths of this unit, and can it play MP3's?", 'answer': 'This unit records and plays compact disks (CD-R & CD-RW) with maximum of 120 minutes. CD-R can be recorded only once while the CD-RW can be recorded and erased hundreds of times. According to the Manual, MP3 files recorded onto a CD are handled the same way as files are handled in an ordinary PC, with some MP3 held within a directory. The CD-RW900SL can also play back MP3 files recorded to formats that conforms to ISO9660 LEVEL 1, LEVEL 2, and the Joliet extensions. Discs recorded in multiple sessions may also be played back. CDs containing MP3s to be played by the CD-RW900SL, must be within the following maximum limits: 255 directories, 8 hierarchical structures, and 999 MP3 files.'}
