{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Y040ZC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385884800, 'question': 'Does anyone know if this will fit a Flesch flat center-mount chin rest? It looks like the same shape from what I can tell.', 'answer': "The thing is, it has a sticky back, so you don't have to worry about the placement of the chin rest on your instrument. Plus, I like to think that the chin rest is designed more to fit you than the chin rest itself, so even if it isn't the perfect shape to fit the rest, it will stick to it and it will cradle your chin perfectly. I would say definitely go for it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Y040ZC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 6, 2012', 'unixTime': 1346914800, 'question': "Unsticking the gelrest: Does this gelrest make the original chin rest sticky when it's removed?", 'answer': '"Detachol"--from surgical supply stores or "Goo Gone"--from dollar stores, should remove it without damaging the chinrest surface. Just be sure NOT to get any solvent on your violin top. If you do not remove your chinrest, put a freezer bag and rag under it to protect your violin top.'}
