{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421136000, 'question': 'Can I connect iPad to input Karaoke down-streaming music via 3.5 mm TRS to dual 1/4 in TS cable to this mixer? Can I then connect mixer to AV Receiver', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'YES. As long as you have the jack adapters. The mains output is 1/4 TS to whatever you need on the AV. Output level is standard +4 dBu. There is also RCA recording outs'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428649200, 'question': "Yes I'd like to know why Amazon don't have tech support # to help someone that is blind &amp; drummer to help hook this up to speakers...", 'answer': "I didn't have any experience with mixers and it took me a while to figure it out but now I am very happy with this unit and feel I made the right choice in buying it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401260400, 'question': 'I need the headphones to have more volume, but the phones output seems to be tied to the stereo output, I need the output lower and the phones higher.', 'answer': "You might try adjusting the main output high enough to give you adequate headphone volume, then reduce the gain on your power amp until it compensates. I assume you'd not be using the power amp at the same time as phones anyway so if your power amp sounds good the way it is, just increase the gain for your phones when you use them and down again after. It doesn't get any easier than one-knob control- that's why I love the compressors in this."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'I would like to use this mixer for Karaoke. Does this mixer have key changer?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'no key change just effects, i have it hooked up to my magic sing and the magic sing karaoke mic has the key changer on it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397286000, 'question': 'how would you hook one of these up to a preamp or does it connect directly to a cpu?', 'answer': "This unit is for basic mixing. It has built in preamp for mic and has instrument inputs also. It doesn't have a USB or FireWire for recording to a computer. This would require an audio interface to communicate with a computer (CPU)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': "Does this unit have such a function that removes singer's voice from pre-recorded CDs?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This unit does not remove vocals. It does have effects (reverb), but will not remove vocals to produce a "music only" track.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7567A', 'answerTime': 'Mar 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395730800, 'question': 'If my source is my tv, do I connect to 7/8 LR or 2TR IN LR? As for output to receiver, will it be REC OUT (RCA) or MONITOR or STEREO OUT? Thanks.', 'answer': "You can actually plug into either the (7/8) or the (2TR). I would plug into the (7/8) so you can control the bass/treble etc, and you can get more volume. Unless if you want to control everything from your receiver then plug into the 2TR. So from your TV go out to the board into the inputs (7/8) or (2TR). Then (Rec Out) into your receiver, usually to the (Aux) but any input should do. I'm guess you're setting up a karaoke system because if you wanted your TV connected to your speakers then you would just plug straight into your receiver. If you do decide to get a powered amp to plug in instead of your receiver you'll get better sound quality IMO. Hope this helps you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7CTLG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363590000, 'question': 'does this come with a mocrophone and will it work with a sure PGX transmitter?', 'answer': "It doesn't include a microphone. The compatible microphones are PG185 and PG30-TQG. Those use the shure ta4f connector compatible with this transmitter. I use a shure PG4 receiver and it works well, but i don't know if this series works with the PGX series of receivers... My guess would be that they don't.. But i can't be sure of that without testing... JCML... from Venezuela..."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7CTLG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359619200, 'question': 'With a ShureWH30 wireless mike and this transmitter, can I use them with a Nady receiver?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Almost certainly not. Each device has a frequency it uses and they won\'t match up. Note the "H7" for the Shure bodyback. Not even all Shure receivers will work, it has to be an \'H7\' receiver, too. You could buy whatever microphone for the bodyback you wanted, as long as it\'s the correct kind of connector'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7CTLG', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1359532800, 'question': 'With a ShureWH30 wireless mike and this transmitter, can I use them with a Nady receiver?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sure not a problem'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B000Z7C9T8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 21, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382338800, 'question': 'Can this be hooked up to output to my home theater system?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Sure you could do that but unless your home system consists of pro audio gear (loudspeakers or powered loudspeakers, amplifiers with balanced xlr connections etc) and you need to mix vocal mics and/or instruments, it might be overkill (as you will not be using many of the functions available). For instance if your audio system uses RCA connectors, the mixer does have RCA inputs/outputs, so you could easily do it, I am just not sure if it would be worth it. If you post a picture of your gear or give a more detailed list of expectations I can give a better answer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B000Z7C9T8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'Is this something that can be hooked up to my sons computer or keyboard to mix beats to out of his computer?', 'answer': "You could use it for that if he already has speakers awesome! But you will need a power amp as well. I really recommend this product I use this mixer for my band we plug in the guitar, bass, and mics great and if you are interested in buying a power amp I will recommend the behringer 4,000 power amp it's a bit pricey but works like a charm! I hope I answered your question if you have anymore please feel freed to ask good luck :)"}
