{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0010K8IM6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1370847600, 'question': 'What is the major problem with the hum in this amp, can it be fixed', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I completely disassembled my amp and used it for a juke box restoration. I installed a preamp for the 45 record portion of it and grounded it to the metal frame of the juke box and used rca jacks to connect to this amp with no problems or hum. Now I also installed an 1/8" input jack so that I could plug in an I pod and that did not work out so well. Lots of hum. I believe this amp uses an isolated ground which is why the rca jacks worked for the preamp but the metal casing on the 1/8" jack for the ipod grounded to the frame did not work. As soon as I replaced it with a plastic cased one the hum went away.'}
