{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00154KSA2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420185600, 'question': "Just bought this used to use with my new Mac for recording, but it didn't come with software. I'm new to recording. Help me find the software link?", 'answer': 'Go to &lt;Apple menu&gt; / System Preferences / Sound, and choose "AudioBox USB" for the Input and Output. That will set the default input/output for recording/playback software (e.g. Garageband, Audacity) to be the AudioBox USB. Note that many audio apps allow you to override the default audio input/output with preferences within the app itself.'}
