{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0015RIN6U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394092800, 'question': "Would this tuner work with an acoustic/electric violin? I have had trouble with the built-in one I've been using, it's no good for on stage tuning", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': '(1.) The pitch black is not an acoustic tuner - meaning, it does not have a mic. You must connect to the Pitch Black via 1/4" cable. (2.) On-Stage effectiveness has a lot to do with how sensitive the violin pickup (Magnetic, Piezo, Mic) is to interference from other instruments playing on stage while you are tuning your violin. I suggest you buy the Pitch Back from somebody with an extended return policy so you can give it a thorough test. Aside from the question of possible interference from other instruments on stage, I expect the Pitch Black will work very well for you.'}
