{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0015XIAYY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394953200, 'question': 'I have a 96kHz preSonus with the buffer rate past 2000 in FL Studio, &amp; my soundcard sucks, will a 192kHz do better to stop clipping in playback?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I record everything in 192. You will need softwear that records it. I use SoundTrack Pro. i used presonus at 96 and love 192. I save the file in 96 and reopen it in 192 without much loss. I usually digitally edit in 192. Clipping sounds like too much level, give it some headroom or use limiter at zero db.'}
