{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00167UQLO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424073600, 'question': 'I have the mic with the BEHRINGER XENYX 3 mixer and the mic compresses my audio (Makes me quiet when im loud and loud when im quiet) How do i disable', 'answer': 'Not sure why you would want to do that. There are many settings on your mixer and recording software. Did you use a pre-amp? This microphone is designed to compress vocals, but you can adjust how much compression by the settings on the fornt of the microphone. I used the neutral setting ( - ) and zero ( 0 ) for all my clean vocals, my screams, and my harmonies. You can check out what my band Soundstill recorded by visiting www.soundstillband.com and listen to all songs from album "Before The Sunset Ends". Thanks!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00167UQLO', 'answerTime': 'Sep 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409986800, 'question': 'Does this microphone output straight Xlr which i can plug directly into a preamp? Or do i need a special converter?', 'answer': 'You can plug directly into the preamp (using xlr cable). I plug the mic into an Event preamp, and the preamp into the recorder. Very simple.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00167UQLO', 'answerTime': 'Aug 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407826800, 'question': 'Does this require phantom power? If so will a balanced xlr cable w/ balanced xlr 1/4 adapter work for my Avid M-audio computer direct box, which only has 1/4" inputs and does have a phantom power source? Thanks!', 'answer': "Yes it does require phantom power. I'm pretty sure all condensers do. Regular xlr cables work. The power comes from your mixer or recorder."}
