{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016LVAOC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': 'Can this be hooked up to a interface, also does it come with any sound kits/drum kits?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'No drum kits are included, if by interface you mean compatible programs then yes. The list off programs it works with is the usual suspects.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0016LVAOC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380265200, 'question': 'Can this be hooked up to a interface, also does it come with any sound kits/drum kits?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The mpd32 is only a midi controller. It will control midi information. It's connected to your computer via USB. Then you can use it with whatever music program you have. It doesn't come with any sound. You'll have to look into the MPCs. The premise of the MPD, is to control whatever sounds inside your music software. It gels we'll with REASON, which is my program of choice. Hope this helps. Check out my website for tutorials. www.AOSbeats.com"}
