{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0016MN4I6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': 'I am using a Korg X5DR module with a pretty good patch for Hammond and using the modulation wheel for the Leslie sound. Is this better or the same. Also any recommendations for a better Hammond patch. Thanks', 'answer': "the mod wheel will not give you a true leslie sound...I do have the behringer and it is ok...I mean it's 50 bucks so it's not going to sound like a rotosphere or a quality pedal but it does the job....i would say spend the 50 bucks...if you are a true gear head it would not be the first time you bought something that didn't quite sound like you expected...but if you don't buy it you will never know"}
