{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0017Y2TAC', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419926400, 'question': 'I mainly make hip hop and rock beats with Magix Music Maker. Is this compatable? and would you suggest it for Hip Hop beats?', 'answer': "I'd guess that you could export midi from Magix Music Maker but it would playback with the sounds on the Midi machine, which are pretty unhip hop. If you have a tablet another option would be exporting the audio to something like Anytune and use something like AirFlip pedal to control playback /looping."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00181T20O', 'answerTime': 'Jul 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405321200, 'question': 'I noticed that there is another place to plug in something next to the rca outputs.how can both play something?whatcablesdoineedtohavethem...', 'answer': 'The inputs/outputs are (from left to right): Input 1 - stereo plug, Input 2 - R and L phono plugs, Output - connection plug to left speaker, AC Power. On the front there are inputs for a mic and for headphones, as well as volume and balance controls and on-off power switch.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00181T20O', 'answerTime': 'Feb 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391932800, 'question': 'Can I use these with a StagePAS 400i portable sound system from Yamaha . I want to use them as a vocal monitor.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'They are a powered monitor system with left and right RCA inputs and a single mini stereo input and a 1/4" mic input in the front. Basically a mini PA system. They are fairly loud and have a very good sound quality. There are treble,bass and volume attenuators. I use them for a recording studio and they work great with MP3 players. Hope this helps! My guess is they would be loud enough for a personal monitor.'}
