{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0018SJLFS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396076400, 'question': 'I have an Ampeg GVT52 that came stock with JJs. Love the JJs for their smooth tone, but would like to try something else, will these make much diff?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Each amp takes tubes so differently so it's hard to say. I can only speak for my 2013 vox ac30 and they did make a nice difference. Subtle but different. It's kinda like different brands of strings. All similar but slight variations. I ended up recording with my phone to help hear the difference side by side. Overall I'm glad I tried them and I did keep them in. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0018SJLFS', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387267200, 'question': "Will this work with the Bravo Audio Ocean tube amp? It seems that it's an 12AU7 vs a 12AX7, but maybe that does not matter.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'All "12" series tube pins are identical. A 12ax7 has a higher output than a 12au7 (which has the lowest of the series) and may cause distortion or some other unforeseen issue with the circuitry. Before proceeding, you need to know why the manufacturer chose to use a 12au7 and its application in this amplifier. A great rule to follow is don\'t re-invent the wheel - if the manufacturer designed a circuit to use a particular tube, there\'s a reason why.'}
