{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00191WVF6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394434800, 'question': "I've purchased 3 of the 9volt Planet Wave Adapters for my Fender Mini Twin Reverb Amps. When I plug them in, I only get a humming noise. Troy,txs", 'answer': 'That not a question, but I\'ll turn it into one and try and answer that question that I just wrote. "Why do I get a humming noise when I plug my planet waves adaptor into a mini twin fender amp?" First off, does your mini twin work with a nine volt battery? Check that. If not, then the amp\'s broken. If yes, continue. I just checked, and the mini twin seems to be center negative, like the adaptor. Still, check to see if your mini-twin power in is expecting a center negative power supply. Perhaps the power supply input jack on the mini twin is broken? Perhaps you\'ve gotten three bad power supplies. Have you checked them with a multimeter? Good Luck.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00191WVF6', 'answerTime': 'May 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400050800, 'question': 'What are the inner and outer diameters?', 'answer': 'The measurement in inches is .215 outer diameter and .0815 inner diameter. Make sure that the piece you are buying it for is center negative.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00191WVF6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'The spec says a Max Current of 300mA. I want to use it for BOSS MT-2 pedal which requires 200mA@9V DC. Can this be used?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'If the pin configuration (pin + on the planet waves power supply) and size are the same as the boss pedal, than yes. A DC device will ALWAYS only pull what it needs on the current side. (THE VOLTAGE NEEDS TO BE THE SAME THOUGH!!!!!.... true of ANY DC device) In the case of the planet waves power supply, it is 9V so you are fine. On the BOSS pedal, look at where the power supply plugs in.... there should be a + and - symbol near it.... the one in a circle is the pin which must be positive.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00191WVF6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398322800, 'question': 'Will it work with a Boss Looper?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "You'll have check the current series order on the looper itself my plug is:+-0- - (best interpretation of symbols with keyboard) that translates to a circled positive sign with a solid circle second and last is a minus sign circle . This is used on my ditto looper so take that into consideration. Good luck it's a fine power supply don't let the low price dissuade you."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00191WVF6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375340400, 'question': 'Would this power source work with the Electro-Harmonix XO Big Muff Pi Pedal?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "tip negative...outside ring positive....if that's how your pedal is set up..this will work with it. the Electro-Harmonix XO Big Muff Pi Pedal seems to be set up that way"}
