{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001CQ8VJS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'How is the outdoor performance? Would it work well with a projector and outdoor screen for backyard summer movies?', 'answer': "It works but in term of a limited audience about 10 and sit about 10 feet from the screen. Besides, for audio input (aux in), you can't control the volume from the unit itself (except for playing guitar). It just does not support that. You have to control sound from your sound source device such as DVD player or whatever. I played electric guitar outdoor for an audience of 30 and I turned on the volume all the way. I still felt it is not loud enough. For your info, there is another model that allow volume control from both guitar in put and aux in is Roland MOBILE AC Acoustic Combo Amp. Another model is Roland MOBILE-BA which has the control of echo and delay for microphone input (designed for voice)."}
