{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EKECC2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2009', 'unixTime': 1245049200, 'question': 'Pod Studio UX2 vs. Tone Port UX2: Anyone know what the differences between these two models are aside from color?', 'answer': "Not much difference in the hardware itself. It now comes bundled with Pod Farm (instead of GearBox). Both provide similar functionality. Live Lite will allow you to save recordings, but Live Lite isn't a real recording package. It's really just a very limited demo that you can use as a way to more cheaply upgrade to a full version of Live. Pod Studio is an audio interface + amp/cab modeling package. Despite the name, you still need to invest in some decent recording software to go along with it (or use something free, like Audacity). I have the older version (i.e. TonePort UX2) and really like it. I use it with Ableton Live 6 and GarageBand '09."}
