{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001ELP5WM', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1361174400, 'question': 'What if I want to sustain a note/chord for a minute or more? Is there a way to achieve this? What do I need? Thx.', 'answer': 'You should be able to keep the pedal down to sustain any note for an indefinite amount of time. But note two things: 1) You can only achieve this with a tone that does not fade out (e.g., "piano" will fade out, but "strings" and "pad" won\'t fade out). 2) Keyboards have a limit on how many notes can be heard simultaneously. I.e., if you try to sustain too many notes, the older notes will drop off as soon as you introduce new notes.'}
