{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EW5YQS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383289200, 'question': 'How long Is The USB Cable?Will I Be Able To Comfortably Record Music With My Mic Stand Or Should I Buy an Male To Male XLR', 'answer': 'It comes with a USB cable about 6 ft long. If you need a longer cable you should buy a XLR male to female for your mic as long as you need. (up to about 100 ft max) They recommend in the instructions, using a XLR cable rather than plugging mic directly into Icicle.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001EW5YQS', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': 'Does this device hook straight into the XLR male connectors on the mic itself? Is an XLR cable really needed?', 'answer': 'It can connect directly into a mic, but the car cable will help keep weight down if you are handholding the mic and more importantly, using an car cable will greatly reduce the stress placed on the connector itself, which will allow the icicle and your mic to last longer.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001EW5YQS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394265600, 'question': 'When connected to an AT2020, I noticed that only half of the "ICICLE" is lit up. Is the Icicle defective?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "If it allows your 2020 to work with the computer, It is basically a cosmetic thing. I don't know if they use one or two LED's to illuminate the Logo, but If it works with the mic & computer, I would think that, they probably use two & one LED is defective or there is a poor solder joint. Even if it works OK except for the light, I would return it for a replacement. If you file a claim for replacement because it is defective, Amazon will arrange a FREE UPS pick-up for the product. They will ship out a replacement the moment defective one is received."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001EW5YQS', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403334000, 'question': 'Provided I had the right cable, could I hook up my guitar to my computer with this device?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Hook up yes, will it work, I cant promise anything. It's heavily implied for mic usage so I don't know how it would handle a guitar, I'd suggest checking out their site http://bluemic.com maybe send them an email if you cant find what you're looking for. Blue's really big on mics, I know if they do anything other than that though."}
