{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001G53NZC', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'Does anyone know if this software can be used within the Akai MPC Ren Software as VSTs? And compared to Komplete 10 how does it stack up against?', 'answer': "Can't answer the first question but it is a standard VST so any proper VST container should be able to run it. As for the latter, it's apples and oranges. I have both. Komplete has several great synths, samplers, and effects. Omni is a power synth (which also has a bucket load of samples too but really for sound manipulation). Omni doesn't have drum machines or the like, but has an incredible depth and flexibility in sound design and sequencing. The arpeggiator is amazing. So it depends what you need, but I love them both."}
