{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001IPUJJI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416902400, 'question': 'Can this be placed on the center of a small table and used by two or three speakers (for a podcast)?', 'answer': "In my experience that would not be the best usage for this microphone. While what you're trying to achieve is technically possible, you'll have much better success with a bidirectional mic for two speakers or an omnidirectional mic for more. The Procaster is an end-address cardioid mic which means it is designed to be spoken into from one direction. Rode makes some at least one omni, and the Blue Yeti series has some pattern switchable mics."}
