{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B001PB3VUY', 'answerTime': 'Nov 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384761600, 'question': 'Does each of the presets have a Amp a/b switch like the rp355/And how do you switch preset to stomp(rp355 needs two buttons pressed perfectly or else', 'answer': 'No a/b it is all done by buttons and so is the preset to stop, just press one button but unless you are shoeless (toe pressing) it must be done by hand.. Nevertheless if you use a lot of different sounds the RP1000 is the way to go.. I had the 355 for a week to try and there is no comparison..the 1000 is perfect for multisounds and live applications. It is more of a pre amp processor..'}
