{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B001Q9EE4W', 'answerTime': 'Jul 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405234800, 'question': 'I am a newbie. Is this banjo worth it? I really want to learn to play and I have heard great things about Deering banjos.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The Deering is an excellent quality banjo made in America, but I think the Oscar Schmidt OB5 is a much better value. The OB5 will do everything the Deering will do for about one-third the price (a Chinese-made banjo). If its quality you're after, the Deering is a better choice, but you can learn just as well on the OB5. Deering also sends emails from time to time with ideas on improving your play. You won't get that from the Chinese banjo."}
