{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0023LQE7M', 'answerTime': 'Feb 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391587200, 'question': 'I will mount these into concrete. What diameter and length of concrete masonry screws do I need to use? Do I also need to use plastic "anchors"? I\'ve tried to use plastic "anchors" other times that I\'ve drilled holes in concrete, but have never been...', 'answer': "Hi! I own these, but I installed with hollow wall anchors into drywall. I feel you in regards to plastic inserts into concrete, NOT the way to go ! Get wedge type anchors from Menards, Home Depot, LOWE'S, etc. if memory serves correctly, the mounting holes are only about 5/16, so 4 small concrete anchors would be more than enough to hold up a speaker. The anchors won't need to be more than 1.5 inches long. Hope this helps! Loni S Howard Howard Productions, LLC"}
