{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0023LXSCQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 14, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387008000, 'question': 'Can the stand portion that holds the laptop lie flat? Or does it always need to be at an angle like in the images?', 'answer': 'You can turn it to any angle and fix in any position.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0023LXSCQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394607600, 'question': 'I need a stand to hold a 13" MBP on a gig. I can\'t see how the 4 pegs will hold a laptop securely in place. Can someone describe for me how it works?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The pegs are adjustable in both length and width. It holds my 17 inch laptop no problem. You can secure the length of the peg with individual turn locks. (Same as the height and angle adjustments. I love mine.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0023LXSCQ', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422691200, 'question': "I think I have parts missing. I got no instructions. All I got was a base and the part where the laptop sits but they don't seem to fit together?", 'answer': 'The part where the laptop sits has a tube attached. This tube slips into the base tube. The tightener mechanism has probably slipped to cover the bottom tube opening. You can pull it back where it should be with you finger so it looks like an open tube. You may have to loosen the screw that presses the tightening piece against the inner tube to keep it from slipping down once you have set the height. Once together, set at the height you want and tighten that screw.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0023LXSCQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'can adjustable brackets squeeze a 14" LCD screen tight enough to be tilted 90 degrees without slipping out?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. The amount of compression is up to you. You can push in the brackets as hard as you want and then tighten down the screws. For example, my 12" laptop cannot be removed from the stand until I loosen the brackets first.'}
