{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002AKKO7C', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Does this mandolin sound loud and good without being plugged in or does it have to be plugged in to sound good?', 'answer': "You can play this mandolin with or without being plugged. When unplugged you have a loud and good sound depending on the picks and strings you use. When plugged to a 10 watt amp you fill ,let's say, a pub or a small hall with its sound, when you want to play in a concert hall you need more, of course. I use different picks for different songs and kinds of music, but you have to try out what suits you best. All in all it's a very nice instrument."}
