{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002AKKOFY', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396335600, 'question': 'anyone know the inside measurements or will a yamaha guitalele fit it?', 'answer': 'I bought the Oscar Schmidt UC4 case for my Yamaha guitalele. It\'s a perfect fit. The case inside measurements are: length 27 3/4"; upper bout 7 1/8"; and lower bout 9 3/8". The depth is just right for the instrument allowing no movement but not too tight. The case closes normally. You cannot go wrong with this case.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002AKKOFY', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': "I have a Cordoba Tenor Uke. Does anyone know if it will fit in this case? Amazon doesn't have a hard case by Cordoba so I'm looking for a replacement", 'answer': 'If the Cordoba is a normal (Oscar Schmidt sized) or smaller sized tenor it should fit. Check and compare the bout diameters and body length. While I do not have a Cordoba tenor, I do have a lot of tenors. Most of my tenors fit in my UC4, several are tight but fit. A couple are over-sized and do not fit.'}
