{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002CWP2NY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395039600, 'question': 'can this mic get the sound when it is not close to your mounth', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes. I have used it for years to clip onto the subjects' shirt or jacket. Works great. These do pickup some sound from the environment. If you're look for something more directional to not pickup environmental sound, you may want a reporter's mic like an MD42."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002CWP2NY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427698800, 'question': 'I have a SHURE 93 lav mic with a female mini XLR 3 pin (4 if you count the one in the center). Is there an adapter so I can use my SHURE lav on this?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'There aren\'t any adapters made for Shure TA4F lavaliers to fit onto 1/8" locking Sennheiser wireless. In order to use it, it would have to be stripped and rewired (should only be done professionally). RODE, DPA, and Que Audio all make lavaliers or headset mics that use a modular connection system that allows the connection to be unscrewed and another connector for another wireless system to be screwed on. You just buy the connector for the wireless that you want to use.'}
