{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002DUCRXS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389427200, 'question': 'If I have three units running in close range of one another will they interfere with one another? (Three cameras and Three microphones and receivers.)', 'answer': "I have never tried more than one pair at a time. But my assumption would be that three distinct pairs would NOT interfere with one another because each microphone/receiver pair has a unique Bluetooth address; they're not designed to pair with anything else. However, any other kind of device operating in the 2.4Ghz band may potentially cause interference. You will have to experiment. Good luck, and let us know if your set up works out."}
