{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002IVK0FE', 'answerTime': 'Apr 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397977200, 'question': 'Can someone point me in the right direction? If I wanted to hook this up to my computer to record, what cables will I need?', 'answer': 'Well if you just want to record the audio of what your playing then the simplest way would be to use a 3.5mm cable into a microphone jack on your computer. http://www.amazon.com/Mediabridge-3-5mm-Stereo-Audio-Cable/dp/B004LTEUDO/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1398041305&sr=8-1&keywords=3.5mm+cable If you want to use the MIDI features of the keyboard you would need to use a cable like this: http://www.amazon.com/CREATIVE-EMU-XMIDI-MIDI-Interface/dp/B000JLU26W/ref=sr_1_3?s=electronics&ie=UTF8&qid=1398041405&sr=1-3&keywords=usb+midi In either case you will also need the appropriate software on your pc to accomplish what you want. I think windows may actually have a recorder built in if you go with the 3.5mm cable to record audio file.'}
