{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002KI8X40', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421136000, 'question': 'well this mic work with BSR EQ14/14XR? WHAT IS ITS IMPEDANCE?', 'answer': 'The Dayton EMM-6 is a balanced mic with an (3pin) XLR connector. It requires a minimum of 15 V dc bias voltage. The BSR uses a typical electret mic which is usually biased with 5 V dc and uses a different socket. So the simple answer is no ,you cannot use it with the BSR.'}
