{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002N4GBLI', 'answerTime': 'May 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401260400, 'question': 'Has anyone used this with a bass guitar? Does it provide adequate results when used with a bass?', 'answer': "I have a Bass Guitar too, but I never thought to use it whit bass. I don't know if it makes a good work because all the effects are tuned for the guitar's audio spectrum. In fact there is a Zoom for Basses. But I can try an tell you the results. ....... Out of curiosity I've tried with my bass, but as espected, the effects more frequency dependent like the wah-wah work really bad, the less dependent like the delay work better. There is the Bass counterpart of this pedal effect: Zoom B1 Bass Multi Effects Pedal It's quite better ti take it."}
