{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002N6PAMM', 'answerTime': 'Jul 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404198000, 'question': 'Will these work with a Zoom h4n? The Zoom has phantom power, but no mic. power. If power is needed to operate the mics, what module do I need to get?', 'answer': 'The H4N phantom power only works when there are XLR ins, so the workaround I use is +24V phantom power in the H4N settings, feeding the mics into a Y-splitter to 1/4" stereo, and I feed those to impedance adapters, female 1/4" to the male XLR\'s (x2). I bought these products to get the job done, http://www.amazon.com/Hosa-YMP-434-Female-8-Inch-Breakout/dp/B0010D0HO0/ and 2x http://www.amazon.com/Planet-Waves-Female-Balanced-Adapter/dp/B0002E53O2/ And no I don\'t endorse any of these.'}
