{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002Q93CGM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412924400, 'question': 'Is 20 gauge wire okay for one of these light units?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "20 gauge is fine for short connections but I would use 16 or 18 for long runs. I used lamp cord (18 gauge) for about a ten foot run and it worked OK. If you use smaller wire for a long distance it will work but your light output will be diminished. For those who don't know - the smaller the wire the larger the gauge, so a 20 gauge wire is smaller than an 18 gauge wire. Think of electricity flowing through a wire like water flowing through a pipe - the bigger the pipe, the easier it is for water to flow through it."}
