{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Jun 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402470000, 'question': 'What kind of battery does this use? Is it removable? Thank you.', 'answer': "It uses 2 AA batteries. Yes, they are removable. You can also use rechargeable AA batteries. The M10 has a menu setting so you choose whether you are using regular store bought batteries or the rechargeables. The menu setting determines how the battery charge indicator reports back to you. BTW - battery life is exceptional! The M10 is a favorite choice of many tapers. Check out the website taperssection.com. Do a search for the thread Sony PCM-M10 in the recording gear forum. It's a huge 7 part thread that has great information. You will not go wrong with this unit."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'The product is listed as a "voice" recorder. Any good as a music (e.g piano, band) recorder?', 'answer': "Absolutely!!! It's a great live Music recorder. You have the option also of reducing the sensitivity of the Mic for recording sounds in high decibel areas such as concerts , which helps in reducing distortion. In my opinion a collector's item ."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Jun 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401692400, 'question': 'Hello, can this recorder work with microSDHC "high capacity" memory cards or only microSD and M2 cards? I am considering a Sandisk 16 GB SDHC. Thx.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Wrong. I routinely use 32GB microSDHC and 64GB microSDXC cards in my Sony PCM-M10. The 32GB microSDHC cards can be used directly, without reformatting them. 64GB microSDXC cards have to be reformatted from exFAT to FAT32. See this link (with instructions for using a Microsoft Windows OS utility) that I posted to the Head-Fi forum almost two years ago: http://www.head-fi.org/t/456327/sony-pcm-m10-as-portable-player/120#post_8727898 I don't have a Mac, but it's my understanding that its OS has a built-in Format utility that allows you to select FAT32 at the type. Enjoy!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Nov 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414911600, 'question': 'Are any of the buttons backlit or just the display window?', 'answer': 'On my unit,, the record and pause buttons light up when engaged.'}
