{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': 'My specific planned use is unobtrusively recording normal conversation. So mike has to be very sensitive. Is it? Specifically, I want to record "oral history" conversations with my soft-spoken mother, who gets self conscious if a microphone shows up....', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Get her to a quiet area, preferably just you two. You can then put the unit away from you two and begin the conversation. I have used it in a dance hall setting to record dance instructions and have found it is great. I know that the New York NPR reporters use this device; I was at an event where they were using it and commented that it was the same one I used.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Mar 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394953200, 'question': 'how is the sound play playback using only the recorder?', 'answer': 'Hi, Using only the half inch speaker from the recorder, very limited in frequency response, no bass at all and very low level; but if you put it on a solid table surface and raise volume to max level, you can hear it ok from a foot or two, no distorsion. Using a pair of good headphone, sound is excellent, loud enough, no distorsion, can easily be used as a Walkman. When I use it to record musical performance, I always carry good headphone to get better monitoring. Louis'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421395200, 'question': 'How do I install the included Audio Studio LE on a Mac?', 'answer': "It's not a Mac application. You need to use Audigy or something that's equivalent. Alternatively you could use parallels or virtual box windows emulators and install Audio Studio"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002R56C4O', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2010', 'unixTime': 1284015600, 'question': 'Seeking Advice on Best Microphones for Use with this Recorder: Can anyone suggest what microphones/model/brand to use for this situation?', 'answer': 'I suggest going to "The Sound Professionals" website. I bought a set of their tiny SP-CMC-8 mics there and could not be more pleased with the sound. These were somewhat pricey, but they have MANY options. Good luck!'}
