{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002TUTUIM', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': 'Am I likely to have feedback issues with mic on an acoustic guitar vs a pickup? I use fairly decent cardiods but the Martins seem to grab room sounds.', 'answer': "I use the VoiceTone with an acoustic run direct so the only sound going in the unit is from the guitar. I don't think you'll have feedback issues as much as your harmonies may be effected from other sounds from the stage entering the mics. Good hypercardioid mics may help with this however if you are the only sound source than it may not be an issue."}
