{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002YL81RW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407913200, 'question': 'can you use this to trigger an 808?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, you can use this to trigger anything that receives a USB Midi signal. Literally anything that is a Midi Mappable trigger or on/off setup. So if you wanted to you could set each switch to a different 808 Drum, 1 for Kick, 2nd for clap, and 3rd for hi-hat... If you so desire.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B002YL81RW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'Has anyone used this for Ableton? AND can you assign specific keys for the 3 buttons. For Ex: "up" "down" "enter"', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have not used it for Ableton but the buttons are assignable in both Logic Pro X and MainStage 3. Logidy has an app on their website that allows you to program the UMI3 buttons to which ever notes you like.'}
