{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B002Z9JWZI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389859200, 'question': 'What are the similarities and difference between 440 and 840?', 'answer': "in not sure if the questions is about the headphones or if its about the replacement ear pads. if its about the earpads there ones specifically made for the 840 but its twice the price i think($14) on amazon. if you go the shure website there are no specific dimension for the ear pads. so i think it might be easier to pay to the 14 dollar ones which i think it sucks to double the price but cheaper than returning it if it does not fit. if you are talking about the headphones itself, i think it all depends on what you are using it for. I'm a sound engineer and the shure 440 does not have a good base response. its incredible clear when using for vocal voices, guitar or keys if you need to eq them, but not really that good for percussions. i have the audio technica m50 for monitoring. i do not have the shure 840 but i don't think paying an extra $100 is not worth it. There are better headphones out there for sound engineers at list. Sony MDR7506 is one of them (this one i have). i hoped this helped you. if not sorry."}
