{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0035EHLZK', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421913600, 'question': 'Can I plug a mono instrument into one of the inputs and still use both speakers?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. Channels 2 and 3 both have inputs marked "R" and "L/MONO." If you plug into the mono input, it will play out of both speakers. The single-input Channel 1 will also.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0035EHLZK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417766400, 'question': 'I do not see pan controls... so how is this truly stereo? I have left and rights out from my keyboard... need stereo output...', 'answer': 'Each channel has two inputs hard panned left and right.The stereo positioning is permanently set so there is no control of mixing in the stereo spectrum. This is is not worth the money they charge for it and is a big disappointment from Roland.'}
