{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0036B8A3E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404716400, 'question': 'Is it loud enough to fill apretty good sized gym? Also, how does the clean channel sound?', 'answer': 'I bought this for my son and he filled the gym of his school playing, it was actually over kill and was asked to turn it down. Pretty clean and if you have a good effects pedal the thing screams and sounds good.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0036B8A3E', 'answerTime': 'Apr 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398841200, 'question': 'i have been saving my money for a while. i play like school talent shows and small gigs will this amp cut it?', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0036B8A20', 'answerTime': 'Jul 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405666800, 'question': 'How loud can it get while staying clean?', 'answer': 'Not very, but it\'s by design. Since there\'s only a single knob to control both gain and volume, it breaks up pretty early, at least in my experience with a 1x12 and 2x12. The gain stepping is also pretty aggressive as you turn the knob. Others below seem to disagree but what constitutes "clean" and "loud" is highly subjective. There are however well published mods that you can do (or have done) to add tone, volume, etc. controls to the head. While it does sound great for a $100 tube amp, if you\'re going to consider investing in the mods it\'s probably more sensible to just buy a small head with more controls for the same additive price.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0036B8A20', 'answerTime': 'Aug 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1376722800, 'question': 'Ohms? Will this amp work and sound good if I use the the 2 Marshall cabinets?', 'answer': "it will sound good. louder than one might think. i love the little guy. i've had amps for way more $ and be equal or less than good. the el84 plus the 12x7 yadda yadda is the same as a Vox. A class too. sounds like a beatles amp, but raunchier. problems... the cheap ass plugs electric hook up thingsy is eggshellish. cut corners somehow i guess. if you can afford the speaker cab, i'd go for it. the speaker is voiced for the amp and breaks up when driven at the right time. lovely."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0036B8A20', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'Can I use head phones with this?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'This amp does not have a headphone output.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0036B8A20', 'answerTime': 'Sep 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411801200, 'question': 'Will this amp drive a single Kustom PA monitor whos requirements are 60W RMS, 120W peak?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'A short answer is yes but not very clearly even if the impedance load matches up. You will be under powering the speaker cone and will not be able to drive the highs well... but that could cater to a darker blues style tone. it would not hurt anything to drive a speaker then needed'}
