{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0038YX39U', 'answerTime': 'Sep 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1378364400, 'question': 'I have a tascam dm 24 portastudio. Can you record drum tracks to a portastudio with this unit?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, of course you can. It has standard line-level stereo audio outputs that can be plugged into inputs on the portastudio. For best results use two mono tracks or one stereo track so that you retain the stereo image of the drum sounds. Also, not sure if you can do this with the Portastudio, but if you record to PC or Mac-based recording software, you can also record the MIDI data from the Drum kit to a MIDI track as you play, then you have great flexibility to work with the data to easily make corrections, change sounds, quantize the track, etc.'}
