{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003BQ1Y82', 'answerTime': 'Oct 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412146800, 'question': 'Q1: Just switching to Mono (Izotope Ozone 5) in my DAW using my main monitors will not produce the same results? Q2: Headphone out to TS or TRS cable?', 'answer': 'Yeah you can reference mono with Ozone but the avantone is more than just a mono reference. Since it is a single tweeter unlike a standard near field which is usually 2 way consisting of a tweeter and a woofer, the sound is much different. It more or less replicates the sound of a tv, radio, or computer speaker but with a flat freq response unlike those examples which exaggerate certain frequencies to make things sound "better". Although they are full range, they really only help with freq between about 90hz - 15K so you won\'t be able to hear sub notes or really high end clarity. Many times I\'ve thought the mix sounded good but when I switched to the avantone the vocals sounded too far back or the "mid" bass was barely audible or the hi hats were too up front, etc. For connections, I would recommend using a secondary output from your soundcard instead of a headphone jack. Should be able to connect with a 1/4" cable or an XLR to 1/4" if you get the active ones.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003BQ1Y82', 'answerTime': 'Jul 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404975600, 'question': 'Is the better to purchase two of these monitors (left and right balance) or try to work with one? Thanks for the help! lowbitlogic.com', 'answer': "One should be just fine. Having two doesn't have much stereo field, and the Mixcube is more for checking mono compatibility and balance."}
