{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003EZXMS0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388217600, 'question': 'how would u reccomend changing between effects. a pedal? if so which one', 'answer': "Hey Adrian I am using the Ground Control by voodoo labs which also gives you 2 expression pedals to control the extra parameters in each effect but that's an expensive solution. A cheaper way to go is with the Behringer footswitch, it has plenty of options and expression pedals as well and its pretty flexible, dont remember the model name right now but its the one that looks like a pedalboard FCB something I think. You definitely need a midi controller. If you have other pedals then u may consider the voodoo labs since its the most flexible pedal I have found. Again, for cheaper solution the behringer footswitch is the way to go."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393142400, 'question': 'Someone told me that this violin does not come with strings when you buy it, is that true?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The violin that we purchased came equipped with strings already installed. Most of them snapped upon first tuning. We are experience with violins, so this means the strings are of poor quality. Do your self a favor and order a set of better quality strings in addition to the violin. Would suggest Daddario prelude steel strings ($15?). They are USA made, and will work well on an electric violin. All the best!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Can you attach shoulder straps to the case or does the case come with straps?', 'answer': 'Comes with it'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 3, 2013', 'unixTime': 1380783600, 'question': "Hi, I'm really interested in this product, but will the strings of the violin be tuned?", 'answer': 'They will be tensioned but not tuned. I found this to be an excellent practice instrument that needs minimal setup. Every violin needs to be tuned every time it is played, no exceptions.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'Can these be played without being hooked up to anything with cords? In other words, can you carry them around while playing like a traditional violin?', 'answer': "Yes, actually. It's very similar to an electric guitar, where you can still play without an amp, but it's just really quiet. You can't really perform on one without something, but you can still play without one."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'can you plug this violin into a wall socket and use the headphones (instead of an amp) and not use the battery?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Not that I can see. The back of the instrument has 3 jacks--Line out, Mic, and Phone. I'm thinking its battery powered only."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Jun 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404111600, 'question': 'How quiet is "silent" (...on a scale of won\'t-wake-up-the-baby to regular acoustic sound.)', 'answer': "It's not silent. But, it's pretty quiet, especially if you bow it lightly. You can also use headphones with it. It is definitely much quieter than a regular violin."}
