{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'Do you have complete control over volume? I just moved into an apartment and am looking at an electric so that I can silence it when I practice.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you have complete control over the volume.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384070400, 'question': 'This is for an accomplished teen violinist. Will the sound likely be okay if he is used to a nice violin or is the sound/quality more for a beginner?', 'answer': 'I am a beginner also. I would suggest going to YouTube and check out a video by fiddlerman. He reviews the black version of this violin. He gave a favorable review. What he plays in the video sounds good. Alot better than my playing. You will probably want to get higher quality strings. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1HVDU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': "I'm a beginner and I really know next to nothing on violins. Either I did something wrong or this is not silent? I applied a little resin and its loud", 'answer': "Nothing was done wrong sir. It will still produce sound just not a full crisp, sound that an acoustic violin would make. It's along the same lines as an electric guitar still makings tones without an amp."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1PK42', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395903600, 'question': "what are the advantages/disadvantages of having that left part of the body missing? because there's another model that's whole - what is the point?", 'answer': "Honestly, I don't think there is any significant difference outside of weighing a little less. However, the cut-out allows space in the case to store a shoulder rest."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1PK42', 'answerTime': 'Jan 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390118400, 'question': 'Does the kit come with strings attached or must you string them yourself?', 'answer': "The strings come attached. In fact, as soon as my violin came in, I took it to my local music store (who strung my acoustic violin) to have him check it out to see if the violin and strings are of good quality. He thought is was decent quality. I couldn't be happier with it, especially for the price. When you first get it, you will have to re-tune the strings every 10 minutes or so while you are playing, but after about a week of re-tuning (and it does need tuning less frequently with time) you are good to go. It doesn't hold a tune as well as my acoustic...I tune it before I begin playing usually, but it does hold well and the sound is fantastic. You can play it through an amp or into headphones and I think the sound quality is awesome. Hope this helps. :)"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003F1PK42', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': "What's the weight of the violin in pounds?", 'answer': 'I dont know, its a lottle heavier than a regular violin, its a solid body construction, but it sounds so good that you dont even need it plugged in or powered on to have a good rich sound'}
