{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GEBGA0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427871600, 'question': 'What is a good amplifier for this microphone?', 'answer': "I have only run mine through a Behringer PMP 2000 (Europower 800 Watt PA system). The microphone stays true and clean no matter how loud I get; it's sensitive enough to pick up softer tones when used. What you use it for will dictate what size amp to utilize, because the mic itself won't distort or adulterate what it picks up without external interference. If you run it through an 8 watt amplifier and use it for full force growling or screaming (my version of these vocals anyway), the truth to your efforts won't carry as well as perhaps a 100 Watt. You just have to decide how loud you would like to be and purchase accordingly."}
