{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GEKXRM', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'Does this tilt in all directions? (Or just forward and back?) I want something I can adjust to any angle.', 'answer': "The top only tilts forward to back (it's designed for heavy loads - a ball joint would not be sufficiently strong or stable). HOWEVER, the clamp on the mast for elevating the platform to specific heights allows the mast to rotate, so you can set where you want the tilt axis to face. It is not as simple as a one-joint solution, but the platform can face in any direction without having to move the legs. If you're going to rotate the platform in real time there is a locking pin which keeps the mast from dropping. The bigger issue is the platform has no lip, so I suggest you add one (easy to do) to prevent devices from sliding off."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GEKXRM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387872000, 'question': 'Is the platform now plastic or particle board?', 'answer': 'The one I have is plastic.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GEKXRM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388044800, 'question': 'What size is the platform?', 'answer': '23"x16"'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003GEKXRM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'Does this screw off the tripod and can be mounted on a 3/8th inch screw mount for a standard camera tripod, or is it permanently mounted to the stand?', 'answer': "Not sure about the 3/8th inch screw mount. The flat part where the laptop sits clamps onto what I'll describe as a T shaped rod. You screw the flat part into the clamps and the clamps slide onto the rod. Not sure if that answers your question."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003GEKXRM', 'answerTime': 'Jul 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405580400, 'question': 'Does this sit on a desk?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is a substitute for a desk. I use it to hold my laptop while programming at job sites. It can be set to comfortable sitting or standing levels. Too big for airlines but OK for keeping in a car.'}
