{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003HR30FU', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'I want to plug a mic into the Alesis, then connect the Alesis into my PC - to use the mic for speaking on skype, webinars - will that work??', 'answer': 'Yes definitely. Thats what this was made for. It has XLR, which is commonly used with condenser mics and has phantom power in the device. It also has 1/4 input. You just need to set up the iO2 as your input device either in your computer sound settings or in the Skype software.'}
