{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003HZV2JS', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415001600, 'question': "I have a onkyo 7.2 txnr -828 receiver, and I want to connect it, how to do it and I want to know if my polk rtia9's for my fronts will work ?", 'answer': 'If your Onkyo has "pre-out" RCA output jacks, which I think it does, you\'d simply connect an analog 2 channel "RCA" cable from the Onkyo "pre-out" to the inputs (L+R) of the Crown, and hook up your speakers to the Crown. The Crown also has a volume control, so read the manual. You have to decide which place you want to control the volume from - the Onkyo or the Crown. It is a lot of power for the RTA 9\'s but it should sound great. JH'}
