{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003HZQRHK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414825200, 'question': "Is this model really any better than the smaller and simpler Solo XT model which gets a higher Amazon rating? What's added here?", 'answer': 'I use the JML2 as a sample player exclusively. I do no looping. I am a singer/guitar player who uses the unit to start and stop backing tracks with my foot. Left = click ~ Right = tracks. Aside from the archaic procedures and limitations to maneuver the software when loading audio into the unit; (it cannot be read as an external drive without the quirky "JamManager" software which is cumbersome), it is a solid unit. I needed stereo so I can only say it\'s better than the Solo XT due to that fact.'}
