{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003KR7B34', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385107200, 'question': "If you don't have an angled jack, does the cable bump the sides of the bag when plugged into the left or right-most pedals?", 'answer': 'No, because both sides of the bag have openings for the cables (with velcro). The bag is great.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003KR7B34', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'is there an actual board in the bag, or is it just a bag? how many connector outlet holes are there?', 'answer': "It's just a bag with a couple dividers in it. You can move the dividers and there are Velcro slots on both sides for your cable. It's a fairly simple bag, been working pretty well for me."}
