{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003LQ2Z8A', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379055600, 'question': 'How do you change the valve/vacuum tube?', 'answer': "All you need is a Phillips screwdriver #2. Set the UNPLUGGED unit on its' face, handle towards you. Remove the four black screws on that secure the black amplifier assembly into the wooden frame (inside, along the sides). Now loosen the four chrome plated screws that are not part of the corner guards or handle. They have raised little aluminum collars beneath them. Now you will be able to gently work the amplifier assembly out, being sure not to yank on the speaker wires. Access to the tube is from the side, beneath the Input jack, and a spring holds it in place. Most bad tubes won't glow; the filament is fragile, and wears out over time. Good luck!"}
