{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003MUS35Y', 'answerTime': 'Apr 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429167600, 'question': 'Has anybody bought this harp and transported it on an international flight without incurring extra baggage charges?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I was worried about that as well....mainly the size, which even though small, looked as though it wouldn't fit. After I bought my first I was very concerned about that and the next time I flew (either American or United) I carefully inspected he size ......It would work. However, all the laws are changing and maybe the size inch wise would stop the problem. The overheads are definitely big enough. I understand that many professional musicians have flown with their Rees harps and it seems that they have been able to get on board. Another version of this answer is I have no proof to offer."}
