{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003U6CT5K', 'answerTime': 'Nov 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384329600, 'question': 'To plug an electric guitar into a Mac for GarageBand recording, can\'t I just use a 1/4" female-to-3.5mm-male plug adapter in the mic jack (vs. USB)?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Absolutely can you do that! Plugging straight into the Line-in (or mic) socket is how I first recorded my guitar. Do this for some time and you will realise two things: 1, there is background noise or buzzing leaking into the sound and 2, you lose some of the full guitar sound. The USB guitar Link removes noise (because the sound is converted to digital) and allows more guitar sound to the recording stage. There are much better ones than this but this is the best and cheapest starting point.'}
