{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003UTQO5S', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'Can an electric keyboard be hooked up to this? Can it support a mic at the same time?', 'answer': "Yes, it has four xlr inputs. Each input has its own gain and eq levels. The four inputs can then be mastered with a master volume. As long as you have the proper xlr adapter for the sound interface I'm sure it would transfer the information of a keyboard. It simply takes four standard mic inputs; one might need some kind of middle unit or wire adapter to get the keyboard's midi output turned into an xlr input. I am personally very pleased with this system for it can function both as a practice PA for band practice or it can be rotated and turned up to be great performance speakers."}
