{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003VOBLDW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397890800, 'question': 'Can you record tracks 1-8 while listening to tracks 9 &amp; 10?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes, you can listen to all other tracks that are not recording. Just need to select tracks 9-16 and set the ones you want to listen and volumes, later set back 1-8 and prepare them to record. As Eroach said bfore, the only thing is that you may record max 08 simultaneously , due to the limited inputs (08)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VOBLDW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409468400, 'question': 'Can i record first the tracks or accompaniment trax to sing , and after add one or many voices but all them synchronized, to make a song?', 'answer': 'If I understand your question is: can one record instruments to different channels and then later add multiple vocals to remaining tracks. If that\'s the question, the answer is yes: you "arm" the tracks you want to record to (light above each turns red), disarm those you want to play (light above should be green) and then use the record function, recording to the armed tracks while the R24 plays from the disarmed tracks. You would want to record each vocal track in turn (even if you have more than one vocalist) to avoid bleed-over from one vocal track to the next. Also, if you don\'t want a particular track to play, press the button above it until there is no light. The track is still there; it just won\'t be played. I hope this answers your question.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B003VOBLDW', 'answerTime': 'Oct 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382166000, 'question': 'Would this unit be compatible with Mac, i.e., what are the system requirements for the CuBase LE?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The Zoom ships with a version of Cubase LE for both Mac and PC. You can get a upgrade from the Steinberg website for at a discounted price as well. If you're looking to see if your Mac is fast enough or has the required RAM for Cubase LE, then you'll have to check out the system requirements that are on the Steinberg.net site."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B003VOBLDW', 'answerTime': 'Feb 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424505600, 'question': "I use Adobe Audition 3/Tascam US-428 (only works w Wnds XP) I'm gttng a new computer w/ Wndows 7 - Will AA3 recognize this as a Mackie Emulation or?", 'answer': 'Not sure what that is but does work with protools as an interface device. It also works when emulated as a midi controller. You should be able to emulate with anything. Took me a few days to get it working on protools but working great now.'}
