{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0040FJ27S', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408518000, 'question': 'what are the RGB Wires at the end of the light strip do/supposed to connect to?', 'answer': 'Nothing, they can be left exposed at the end of the strip. You can attach them with an adaptor to another strip of LEDs if you want.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0040FJ27S', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389168000, 'question': 'How many lumens does this put out on average?', 'answer': 'Well David, that is a good question. I have a light meter, but not where I have this equipment. What would you like to use this to illuminate? I may be able to answer based on your application. The range of color is amazing and it has worked perfect for anything where I have used this item. I have been quite pleased and I was trying to imagine the brightest setting and I can say that the light this strip throws is quite impressive. Sorry I cannot be exact with the lumens but If I knew what you would be using this for I could tell you if it would work, possibly.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0040FJ27S', 'answerTime': 'Mar 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1363590000, 'question': 'I want to put one strip under my bar top and another above the cabinets in my bar. Is there a way to control both, separate, strips with one remote?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Mike if you want both strips to do exactly the same thing at the same time then yes you just tie 2 strips together with a 4 conductor wire, if you want the 2 strips to do different things, you still can you would just have to block or somehow prevent one eye from 1 controller from seeing the remote as you change the other.'}
