{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0041OSWV0', 'answerTime': 'Nov 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415520000, 'question': 'Does this keyboard work alone or does it have to be plugged into a computer? (Can you just plug it into the wall and play?)', 'answer': "It needs to be plugged into a computer, hooked to either a DAW or plugin with MIDI support. It can't be used by itself."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0041OSWV0', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': "How is the velocity action? Are the curves good? My current controller has really bad velocity curves. It's not quiet or abrupt, is it?", 'answer': "It's pretty abrupt. You can adjust your play style to give it a better feel, but it's a pretty harsh curve. The only uses for this controller that I've found works best is composition and triggering loops. It works well for drum machines, but anything like velocity sensitive synths, keyboards, and orchestras are tricky to pull of perfectly with this."}
