{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044WVOJ6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427007600, 'question': 'How to play this drums with inbuilt speakers, my one only produces sound with headphones.', 'answer': 'The speakers automatically play when no headphones are connected, unless the Aux-to-amp connector is still plugged in or one of those cords. Take them out and turn the master volume knob all the way up. If there is no audio feedback then you have a defective model and must request a replacement or refund'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0044WVOJ6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425369600, 'question': 'Will this hookup to a computer for direct recording via usb?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I have it hooked up thru MIDI (not USB) as there are no USB ports on this. I'm using the DD-65 to play the sounds from my computer. No lag. Works great."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044WVOJ6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'Can I use a Yamaha digital cymbal with this and would it be capabale of closed hi-hat through holding a foot trigger?', 'answer': 'There are only two trigger inputs and they can be assigned to any of the internal voices. These are normally used for hats and kick. You would have to give up one of the foot pedals to use an exterior cymbal. The hats use a momentary open/closed switch to operate. They are either open or closed, nothing in between. I set them for choked and a 1/4 open voice, so I get a sizzle when they are open.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044WVOJ6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418198400, 'question': 'What is the power suppy? Is there a power adaptor or just batteries', 'answer': "I don't think this product is suitable for anyone who is learning drumming. The power supply is not suitable for Australia, need get additional power."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0044WVOJ6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416729600, 'question': 'Is an amplifier necessary or just optional? Can I play it right out of the box with no other equipment needed?', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393142400, 'question': 'how many times can you overdub on the same track, to build your arrangement?', 'answer': 'Every time you overdub, it creates a brand new track with the previous track along with the overdub. This means that you can overdub on the same track infinitely. I honestly would not recommend the overdub feature because it has no metronome and no blinking light to tell you when to come in.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': 'Will it play back your recording at slower speeds like 1/2 speed?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I think it will, you can slow down music on as card so as long as you record first I would think you could slow down don't know what speeds, manual is online somewhere"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401778800, 'question': "What type of file format does record on the SD Card? If I record a song from a jam so we don't forget it, can I make copies of that file to pass on.", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have not used this product to record as of yet. I used it to assist learning some choral music with previously recorded music that I transferred to SD. But now in curious and will test it out.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399878000, 'question': 'When you change the Key of one song does it change the key of all the songs you have on the gb10', 'answer': 'yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'May 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399618800, 'question': 'I need to record my own vocals at home. Can I use this and will I get great product (quality)? If not, can you lead my on my way to find what i need?', 'answer': "Sorry to say I haven't used mine much BUT, it does work. It will record your voice just fine. When you load MP3s it will also remove the voice track, but because it's blended in, you lose some of the music track as well. But, to just straight record your voice, it works fine. It has 2 external mic's but I would use a plug in. You have to be kinda close to the onboard mic's. I have used the GB10 guitar version extensively and that thing kicks butt so I would imagine this is no different. I have just used it in a very limited way."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'I have Tascam CD-VT2 CD vocal and instrument trainer. I want to be able to burn CDs without the vocal or transposed keys. How can I do this?', 'answer': "I can't help, I do not know this answer. Sorry"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2SI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': 'Hi! 2 questions here: 1) What is max record time of a single file? Iwant to record a whole gig 2) Can you disable mics &amp; record via Line-in ONLY. Thx!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "This isn't what I thought it would be so I haven't used it much. BUT, when I plug a mic into the line in, it doesn't work. I've gone through it to see if I have to tell it to use the line in and from what I can tell, it should be using it but I can only get the onboard mics to pic up sound. I have a TASCAM GB10 for my guitar and that thing kicks ass. I thought this was going to be another version of that but there's no guitar input as stated. As far as capacity it's all up to how much space you load into it. You use SD cards so if you put in a 2GB, I highly doubt you're going to record a set. So just get as big of a card as possible."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'May 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399618800, 'question': 'Can you change pitch, or only speed?', 'answer': 'My husband says it does both.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': 'Does it remove original guitar track during slower-speed playback, or is the point to play over original guitar track so you can hear it better?', 'answer': 'No, the guitar trainer does not remove the guitar track - - you simply play over it. I\'ve used this tool for a couple years now and I find it essential in learning new songs, particularly the following features : 1. The ability to variably slow a song down while keeping the same pitch 2. The ability to "loop" a passage of a song to play it repeatedly - - great for learning a difficult section. 3. The ability to dial up or down the key of song Highly recommended!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418976000, 'question': 'How to download mp3 music files to my Tascam gb10', 'answer': 'D/L music you want to practice to on a mini SD from your computer (or do it through the USB to the unit with the mini SD installed).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419753600, 'question': 'Can I plug my ipod into the USB port and use the USB port as an input for the ipod and play along with the tunes that are already on the ipod.', 'answer': "No, it doesn't work like that. What you can do is to convert your files to MP3 using iTunes (if they not converted yet) then copy them to GB-10 memory card and play along. There are plenty of backing tracks on the net so you can be whoever you wish!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424419200, 'question': 'Is it true that the "speed" portion of the unit can only be adjust in 10% increments, 100,90,80 and not in 1% increments, 100, 99, 98?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, regarding the tempo, I believe so. You can change the key or "fine tune" the recording\'s pitch in small increments. I had the earlier version of the tuner, which I was happy with, but this model is a big improvement.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404802800, 'question': 'How do you store the songs you recorded using the divice on your computer?', 'answer': 'Connect the trainer to your computer and it will ask you if you are connecting to use the USB as a power supply for the trainer or as a storage device; select storage device. Once you connect that way you can move files back and forth between the trainer and your computer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385539200, 'question': 'How is powered this Tascam Guitar Trainer&iquest;Batteries,Usb or AC adapter?', 'answer': 'The GB-10 can be powered from batteries or an AC adapter from TASCAM specifically for this Trainer.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372230000, 'question': 'Will this work with an acoustic guitar or will guitar need a pick up?', 'answer': "It needs a pick up, it doesn't have a microphone."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418803200, 'question': "I've copied all my CD's to iTunes. The files are stored in a .m4a format, will they work on this Trainer?", 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "U must convert your iTunes tracks to MP3. It's not hard."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00452V2S8', 'answerTime': 'Jul 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404543600, 'question': "Will this work with music downloaded from ITunes since they're not MP3 or WAV files?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If ITunes files are still m4p encoded with encryption ( .m4a .m4p or other files extensions), then you will have to buy or find "free-ware" or "share-ware" to convert then to mp3 or wav. A quick search on cnet.com has one such application: http://download.cnet.com/Free-M4a-to-MP3-Converter/3000-2140_4-187723.html'}
