{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004ARSMXQ', 'answerTime': 'Nov 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416643200, 'question': 'Can a use a standard 3.5mm plug on these? How do they sound with compressed music?', 'answer': 'If memory serves correctly these are 1/4" but come (original stock) with adapters to the standard 1/8" on phones/aux-input devices, or vice-versa. I\'m sorry I can\'t be certain, but in general adapters are great to have around. They are "flat" monitors so compressed (lo-fi) will be more noticeable because the headphones present sound more accurately. I used these for a couple years and only gripe is the squeeze on the head. Great for making music (due to accuracy) but if you just want to listen they show the wrinkles. Having a great pair of headphones is double-edged: On one hand you can hear everything, on the other you can hear EVERYTHING, so low quality recording or compression will bug.'}
