{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004ARSMXQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392364800, 'question': 'Using for transcription of voice. Any good with that range of sound?', 'answer': "Yes. These are great cans for all production work. My only negative about these is that they are uncomfortable when worn for long periods of time. The band rest uncomfortably on top of your head, regardless of the adjustment. They're great sounding though."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004ARSMXQ', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391328000, 'question': 'Are these good for mixing, making, and mastering heavy electro or dubstep?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yeah they are good for just about everything, you might want something that goes a little more low range for heavy dubstep, but I do bass heavy stuff all the time on them. You just have to get used to them, they r very clean and flat'}
