{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004IK5M0G', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'Does the button work as an on/off that you can feel with a click or do you have to hold the button down all the time to get effect on?', 'answer': "S. Martin, it works as an on/off button. I don't know if it's able to set the button to activate the effects while you hold it, but I think no. Changing the subject, I see an issue in these button mic: I'm used to run, jump etc. in the stage, so while performing these way I was turning on/off the effects unconsciously all the time, so I stoped using it. I bought an Electro Voice ND767 and I liked a little bit more of it's performance - but both are great."}
