{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004J96JTO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415606400, 'question': 'Hi is this product out of the market by the manufacturer? If so, Can you advise on some other product instead?', 'answer': 'hi. i think the m audio venom is out of production. but im not 100% sure. i have not seen any software updates 4 it since 2013. im not sure what your budget is, but their is a another great Electronic dance synthesiser called virus. also available is refx nexus or ni massive is great 4 electronic dance music. or if u like any old skool instruments 4 EDM, then ebay has tons of them & u might find an m audio venom synth their. when i mention these products, these are just suggestions. but be sure u listen 2 demos of what u buy 2 make sure u like the sound of it so that u r happy with it'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004J96JTO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417161600, 'question': "Just wondering why the price of the Venom shot from $254 to $444. New model? I don't get it.", 'answer': 'Don\'t know the answer but I can tell you a few things that may explain that: (1) this synth appears in the "legacy" section in the M-Audio website i.e. it is officially discontinued (2) just before being discontinued, they sold them for as low as $180 -and I know that for sure cos\' I bought one at that price tag in amazon (3) that price caused buyers to rush (many many forums spread the info an alerted buyers). Bottom line: they were sold so fast that the price had to be raised... Still the third point is my speculation, but make sense to me.'}
