{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004M8YPKM', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402556400, 'question': 'can i use it play effects and/or sample audio', 'answer': "Good question. I do not use for those things. I usually use Ableton Live for playing effects and sampling audio live. If you map the controls by pressing the midi button you may assign that to the nanopad2. Ableton can sample live loops as you play them and you'd have to go into midi mode while the music is playing in order to route it to a trigger on the Korg. I'd have to check into effects. Maybe, to the XY controller. will let you know what I find."}
