{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004MZOVKO', 'answerTime': 'Apr 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396508400, 'question': 'So, i was hoping to be able to plug in a couple of midi controllers, a mic, and possibly a guitar. is this a possibility?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Long answer short, yes. I currently have 3 midi/usb controllers plugged into the usb hub then a condenser Mic and my bass xlr Jack's in the front. All 4 of those have the option for 48v power. There is also one midi in and midi out port on the back."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004MZOVKO', 'answerTime': 'Nov 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415001600, 'question': 'Does this work with Pro Tools LE8?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, it does not. Pro Tools LE8 only works with Digidesign or Avid interfaces. Anyone who says otherwise is wrong.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004MZOVKO', 'answerTime': 'Jun 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403334000, 'question': 'Does this record and save multiple tracks?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, it is only an interface to connect your microphones/instrument/MIDI to the computer, and to route sound from the computer to speakers/headphones. You can attach up to 4 microphones simultaneously to your computer. To record and save tracks you must have an audio program on your computer such as Logic Pro/Pro Tools/Audacity. Also, I would not recommend this product if you plan on using it with a Mac, as the latest driver provided by Akai is not compatible with the latest Mac operating system.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004MZOVKO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422432000, 'question': 'this interface have a protools express??', 'answer': 'Yes, but I would suggest getting a more user friendly interface with better preamps.'}
