{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004NRVUMI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1377846000, 'question': 'Can this be used on a P-mount tone arm ?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you cannot mount a 1/2" or standard mount cartridge on a tone arm equipped with a P-mount headshell. AT makes a huge variety of cartridges though, and I\'m sure you can find a P-mount from them with similar specs. Good luck.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004NRVUMI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': '78 rpm needle for audio-technica lp120?', 'answer': "Yes, I think they still make it, but the cantilever is very fragile and unless the 78 styli has a stronger cantilever, it'll get bent with normal use like the LP stylus of mine did. I'd steer clear."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004NRVUMI', 'answerTime': 'Nov 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385280000, 'question': 'Will this work with a Technics 1700mk2?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Will you be usung your turntable as a DJ or for home audio? The AT is not a DJ cartridge. Other than that it will work in most any turntable/tonearm combinations, just keep the tracking force at or below 2 grams.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004NRVUMI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425024000, 'question': "Will this work with a technics SL 1910? I just wasted $30 on something I didn't need and I want to be sure this time?", 'answer': 'If you need a replacement cartridge and your turntable has a removable cartridge holder with four wires connected to it and with a very small tubular connector at the end of each connector, and at the roof of the cartridge holder there are two small screws either securing the current cartridge to the holder, or if there is no cartridge, you see the screw holes at the top of the cartridge holder, then this cartridge should fit as they are standardized throughout the industry.'}
