{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004OU2IQG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394434800, 'question': 'Is it realatively easy to operate? Can I record from my Boss loop pedal and download to my computer?', 'answer': "There is a LINE-IN plug. So you can record from the Loop Pedal. For an acoustic guitar you just place the recorder near the front of the guitar and it picks up the sound crystal clear. It took me a while to figure out how to use it. It is easy once you know how, but I did struggle a bit to set the recording levels etc. If you work with the booklet, you could probably get the recorder ready for use quite quickly. I will say I've used a bunch of other recorders and this one is the best."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004OU2IQG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394092800, 'question': "Can I listen to the recording through the headphones as I'm recording it in real time. Or only during playback? I need monitoring capability.", 'answer': "Yes, it can monitor. Input into mic jack, output to headphones. I use it off my Mustang 3 amp and listen to what I'm playing with headphones."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004OU2IQG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396162800, 'question': 'Would this be good for a podcast with 4 people?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'it might work if the room has acoustic treatment (quiet) and all 4 voices speak loud, If this is an investment for something semi pro, I rather go with the Tascam DR-40, which has 2 stereo mics like this tascam but you can also plug 2 extra mics http://www.amazon.com/DR-40-4-Track-Portable-Digital-Recorder/dp/B005NACC6M/ref=sr_1_10?s=electronics&ie=UTF8&qid=1396225154&sr=1-10&keywords=zoom+h4n'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B004OU2IQG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416124800, 'question': 'Is this able to pick up nature sounds, birds, crickets, thunder, etc.?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would say that this is best suited to nature sounds. It is very sensitive and works better with subtle noises than anything amplified which can really play havoc with it regardless of the sensitivity adjustment'}
