{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B004ZL3AEI', 'answerTime': 'Jun 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402988400, 'question': 'how thick is the foam?', 'answer': "About an inch, though it adds primary protection, this alone is not sufficient. This did it's job perfectly, but what matters also is the pattern on your Mic and your rooms protection. Initially I went to home depot and bought 2 bi-fold closet doors and lined them with foam on in front and one in back of the artist. And ultimately built a sound proof booth which is it's new home and it works at its optimal level of reflexion. I'm not saying you need to do all that but it will control and protect your voice from blending with ambient noise minimally, not all, and not album quality. But it's a start and a necessary step into the right direction. They make a couple models of which I tried two and I couldn't notice the difference, I purchased this one for the more professional look."}
