{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0052V8Q0S', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2013', 'unixTime': 1366182000, 'question': "i can't open the case, is it broken or i just dont know the method? the case is locked and no matter i turn the key how many times in either direction", 'answer': 'Place the violin case horizontally on a table/floor. To unlock the case, insert and turn the key so the keyholes are parallel to the case (keyholes are horizontal). Once the holes are parallel, push the button on the lock downward towards the table/floor. The case will not open if you push the button inward, towards the case. To lock the case, with the key, turn the keyholes perpendicular to the case (keyholes are vertical).'}
