{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005CX4GLE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389513600, 'question': 'what size drill bit should I use for the anchors that were sent?', 'answer': 'for the anchors that came with mine, 7/32" for dry, wall 1/4" for cinder block or concrete. The anchors are real cheap ones. If you have a problem with them, just get some better ones at at Home depot or Lowes, these should have drill bit size listed on package. the anchors should go in snuggly and flush to wall. You may need to tap them in lightly with hammer. (emphasis on "lightly")'}
