{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EHIN12', 'answerTime': 'May 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400655600, 'question': 'I have 1 4 ohm DVC 15 parallel to 2 ohms will this damage or overheat this amp by using only 1 channel', 'answer': 'I have the nu3000 with the same load and no problems so far. The fan can get loud at times.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EHINAS', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419580800, 'question': 'willl this amp power two behringer vp2520s?', 'answer': "Yes this amp with those speakers is a reasonable match the inuke 3000 will push 800 watts . If you back off the limiter about 1db you'll be at 600 to 700 watts and protect the speaker as well. I run mine on two 225 watt 8 inch speakers crossed with a 50 watt tweeter (450hz and up) for my upper mids and highs and it runs very well. I personally wouldn't expect a lot of low end response from your combination but I push my speakers really hard. With an inuke 6000 on 2 15s each side crossed at 125 to 450 and another inuke 6000 on double 18 each side from 40 to 125. However this will do a football field in a very small speaker footprint. Hope this helps."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EHINAS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410505200, 'question': 'this amp will cover a hall with about 300 people or i need to get the nu6000', 'answer': "You did not mention what you need it for and what speakers you have. For amplifying voice it is more than enough power. If you're a dj and are planning to play music you will need a second nu 3000 connected to a subwoofer. If you have 8 ohm speakers you get sbout 200 watts per channel. For more power you can connect two speakers on each channel making an impedance of 4 ohms."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005EHINAS', 'answerTime': 'Aug 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1409295600, 'question': 'will this amp be enough for 2 Peavey PV 215 dual 15 inch speakers 700 watts program at 4 Ohms in stereo?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It would power those no problem. I run 2 400watt 12" with mine and volume notch 2 blasts them things. Anyways those are 1400 peak right? So that\'s 2800 peak for both sides which should be right where you want to be. The amp is actually 2 1500 watt amps making 3000 total amps.'}
