{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005EZGSAW', 'answerTime': 'May 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1369897200, 'question': '1) Are the effects on board DSP or do they rely on the software/cpu? 2) If on board, can the effects act on AUX input?', 'answer': "The Aux input is just a straight audio input... it isn't a midi input. The Twitch itself is a software midi controller. It can be used with Serato Itch (soon with Serato DJ), it also comes with a controller overlay and mapping for Traktor and a mapping for Ableton Live. You can also edit your mappings in Ableton and Traktor. The controls on the Twitch only work on the midi functions not the audio through the Aux input."}
