{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FPXM0U', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'I need to know the weight and the size of this product. Thanks', 'answer': 'The xylophone is 40" x 21" x 32" high. It weighs about 10 -15 lbs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FPXM0U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383984000, 'question': 'Does this come with any type of warranty?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "To be truthful, I didn't even check. I bought it for my young daughter who instantly fell in love with it. It's a very nice instrument, and she plays it often. Has a great sound (though i would spend a few bucks and get a better set of mallets) We wanted to upgrade from the 2.5 octave glockenspiel to something a bit bigger and this was the only realistic option within my budget. I would definitely recommend this to anyone who likes percussive instruments!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': 'Can I use this stand as a sort of tripod to hold the iPad steady as well as allow me to pan the room while recording videos on the device?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Negative. The camera is covered up when locked onto the stand. So this is no good for that. If you're handy, you might be able to modify it to do that... but it it would involve cutting metal pieces off and installing some kind of jerry-rigged strap to hold the iPad in place. Or you can just punch a hole through the metal part that covers the camera."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Mar 30, 2012', 'unixTime': 1333090800, 'question': "Is the rubber corner issue now fixed out of the box? Does anyone know if PYLE-PRO has product now in the pipeline that doesn't require the replacement corners?", 'answer': 'I received the stand today. Surprisely it came with an extra set of rubber corners- the beefy ones. So i have both sets. I swapped them out. They seem to hold the iPad much better-very tight. I can turn the iPad upside and even giggle it without worring that it will fall out.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372575600, 'question': 'can this &iacute;tem hold a 7 inch Tablet?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I bought it for my Ipad 3 and it fit ok. However, the ipad was too heavy for the hinge and I was not able to get it to support my device. I tried everything to get it to work ... bungee cords and all to no avail. Turned out to be a very bad investment.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'Is it stable enough on carpeted floors? Must I add Velcro to it or weigh down the legs as some reviewers suggest?', 'answer': "I have not had any stability issues with it at all and I use it a lot. It's a good buy....worth the money."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': "Has anyone damaged iPad moving it around a lot? Use outside? winds blow over? I'm just worried about it because our house is very cluttered/remodeling mess... and the thing is probably top-heavy--easy to tip over? Guess using arm would be much less...", 'answer': "It's pretty stable. Especially if you make sure that the boom arm is directly above one of the legs. The longer you make the boom, the more tippy. With the arm 1/2 way extended or less, you should have no problems outdoors."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'Can you look at the iPad while flat on your back? with the iPad horizontal, or nearly horizontal? can even push the power button without holding the iPad?', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'How long does it take for the weaker parts to wear out(Foam iPad holder, that crucial plastic part)?', 'answer': 'Mine has held up fine for six months of relatively light use.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372402800, 'question': "No problem recharging iPad while on the stand? iPad holders trustworthy[Despite that reviewer's mishap]? Wouldn't it be good to have a little more space/ buffer around the iPad to protect against accidents?", 'answer': "I don't use the boom arm. I have the holder connected to the vertical stem. no problem charging it on the stand. The rubber corner holders are very secure. I let my grandsons play with the iPad in the holder while my son cuts their hair. They play rough and the holder stands up to their abuse."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005FSLI80', 'answerTime': 'Jun 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372316400, 'question': 'How much floor space does it take up? How many feet across is the arm with iPad on it?', 'answer': 'This included a basic, standard microphone stand, so the legs on the bottom are 2, maybe 2-1/2 feet from end to end. As far as the arm, it\'s also a standard length, maybe 36"? I\'ve never measured it, but I hope this helps.'}
