{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1381474800, 'question': 'can you do rim shots on this set?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, you can use the rim on the snare (it is a dual trigger pad) to trigger any sound including a "rim shot". This is an amazing little electronic drum kit. I have been playing drums for over 30 years and have owned other electric kits.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425884400, 'question': 'does this drum set have different sounds and kits? If so, how many?', 'answer': 'Yes, according to my son (who is the drummer here) it has 25 different kits and different sounds. Not performance quality but fantastic for practice.. with head phones... on him.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427871600, 'question': 'I only see a kick pedal in the picture,does it come with the drum pad for the bass drum or is that something i have to buy seperately?', 'answer': 'The drum pad is attached to the kick pedal platform and electronically connected to the rest of the kit.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426921200, 'question': 'Does it bounce off like a real kit or is it like hitting rubber', 'answer': 'Well I am a long time drummer (50yrs) and this is my 1st electronic set. It is nothing like a real set, heads do feel like rubber and cymbals and hi-hat are awful, but it does make noise and I do love the base sound and pedal action. To get a better feel and sound you would have to go up to a $600-$1000 set. It is just alright for the money in my opinion.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382857200, 'question': 'Is the brain capable of reproducing different stick velocities (Dynamics) or is the same volume produced no matter how hard you hit pads?', 'answer': 'I personally have never tried this, but, according to the user manual, you can set the brain to have dynamic response to the drum sticks.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 6, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428303600, 'question': 'is the hi hat controller variable or just on off?', 'answer': 'You can set all kinds of sound parameters for open and closed sounds, however I am quite disappointed in there sensitivity. Very poor cymbals in this kit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428130800, 'question': 'I have an acoustic drum set and I am looking for a cheap electronic set for practice. Is this a good idea if already have acoustic drums?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': '2 big advantages of this kit are that you can plug in a mp3 player and play along with headphones for much quieter practice, and secondly, the kit folds up to a very compact footprint you can carry with 1 hand and take with you in any car.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005G59WP8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427785200, 'question': 'Does it come with headphones? If not, can I use regular iphone type headphones?', 'answer': 'It does not. The headphone jack is a 1/4" jack. So you\'ll either need a converter (standard headphones are 1/8" or 3.5mm) or headphones that have a 1/4 jack. Converters are cheap and can be found at best buy or any music store.'}
