{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005HGM1HC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360742400, 'question': "Would you get this one, or would you prefer the epiphone dot? I'm trying to decide between the two? How do you like it?", 'answer': 'The Epiphone Dot has a larger Body size than the Epi ES-339 with less features... the ES-339 has a bound Rosewood Fret-Board & "push-pull" Volume Control to turn the Epiphone \'57 Classic Humbucker Pick-Ups into Single Coil (Coil Tap). Very comfortable guitar to play, with great tones, nice features & "fit-finish" is great for the $$$$ I ALSO OWN THE GIBSON ES-339 (which I love) but find myself picking up the Epiphone ES-339.'}
