{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005HH2GCQ', 'answerTime': 'Aug 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408086000, 'question': "Can you use this from a Nady phantom power supply? It's like a interface thats's not usb", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I have not tested the Nady phantom power supplys. I have used powered mics and a wireless box on it and I beleive that any mic or device that can be plugged into this cable will work. It works just like pluging a mic into an amp. I was also suprised by the sound quality when I plugged it into my laptop and my desktop.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005HH2GCQ', 'answerTime': 'Apr 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398754800, 'question': 'Does this work with the Audio-Technica AT2020', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes this will work with any XLR microphone as long as you have a phantom power supply. The way it works is you hook the microphone up with a regular xlr cable to the phantom power supply input then you connect this cable to the Mic Thru on the power supply and then hook it to your computer. I use the Behringer MicroPower PS400 for my phantom power supply.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005HH2GCQ', 'answerTime': 'Apr 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397372400, 'question': 'Does this work well with the AKG Perception 220 without degrading signal quality or losing volume?', 'answer': "It will not be as noiseless as a higher-end pre-amp or A/D interface, nor will it have as much gain as a dedicated pre-amp. It's a more fast-and-dirty solution than a home studio centerpiece. Chose instead a dedicated USB audio interface if you need studio quality, but if you're just doing youtube voiceovers, it'll sound fine."}
