{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005LZQTKE', 'answerTime': 'Jun 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403247600, 'question': 'Just got mine, but the first finger button is completely immovable. Stuck! Has anyone had this problem, or know how to fix it???', 'answer': "You need to open up the lid, next put valve oil in the area where it gets stuck, then close it and push several times (about 6-8 times). If that doesn't work, go to your local music store and ask the attendant to borrow a special compression tool for the trumpet. Good luck."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005LZQTKE', 'answerTime': 'Sep 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410246000, 'question': 'I am getting ready to order five of these. I see sticky valve problems. What kind of valve oil should I order?', 'answer': "I didn't have issues with my valves for this trumpet, I will say that the 3rd valve slide on mine is very loose and has a tendency to slide down and out on a regular basis. The tuning slide itself also was well lubricated. I believe these horns come with valve oil in their cases. I do not recall, but you can never go wrong with Al Cass valve oil but it generally run $6 a bottle."}
