{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005M02VPK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'How many notes polypony it has ? and which one is the best in its series?', 'answer': 'Polyphony is controlled by the software synth / sampler you are using... this just sends midi notes. As far as which is the best, I can only speak for the Impulse 61. Works great for me!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005M02VPK', 'answerTime': 'Nov 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417075200, 'question': 'does this work with mavericks 10.9.2?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yup works with Mavericks 10.9.2 via Automap on Logic Pro X, Presonus Studio One 2, Ableton Live, Just to name a few.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005M02VPK', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414393200, 'question': 'Would this keyboard work with an iPad air using the camera connection kit (to play synthesizer apps?)', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'The answer is yes, with a catch. The Novation Inpulse is USB bus powered and draws more power than the iPad puts out. I was easily able to get around this by using my powered USB hub (D-Link DUB-H4 plugged in with the camera connection kit. I love this controller! I use it with Alchemy, Animoog, Arturia iSEM, Garage Band, & Cubasis to name a few. Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005M02VPK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392796800, 'question': 'Can i use this as a stand-alone piano if i plug it into an amp? or does it only function when it is running through a program like Ableton?', 'answer': "It is a MIDI controller it has no sound stored on it yes you'll need to hook it up to the computer to get sounds or connect it to a synth rack/box for sound. So it can function without the computer but you'll need a synth rack for sound and you need power via USB such as a USB outlet adapter."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005M02VPK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1364367600, 'question': 'Would this keyboard be compatable with my "Yamaha Motif ES7" if I wanted to midi... And is it easily transposable?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'While I have not used it with a Yamaha Motif, I have used it with a QS series worked well. It is extremely easy to transpose. It was easily one of my best investments.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005M0TKL8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 11, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384156800, 'question': 'I was wondering how much signal gain/boost this pedal is capable of? Looking to get an instrument level close to line level to feed a headphone amp. TIA', 'answer': "I'm not sure on a technical level how much signal boost this pedal can provide, and I've seen nothing online either, but I've used it straight into a PA without a guitar amp (it's an amp simulator so that sounds pretty good) and it had more than enough signal to work with."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005M0TKL8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390982400, 'question': 'hi...is this good for bass?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I have indeed tried this on my bass. I ran my Fender USA Jazz bass with flatwounds through my electric guitar pedalboard and out to my 1974 Musicman HD130 head through 2x10 cab at my church. Excellent crunch distortion. I was surprised actually. Worked great through compressor than AC Tone. Had a some great bite to the tone. I didn\'t want to buy another "just for bass" pedal and I\'m glad I tried this one out first. Totally punchy and growly. It turns heads for sure. I also got some really great ambient lows (imagine long sustaining synths) with the combination of the AC Tone (took some fiddling to set to bass, as opposed to my electric), volume pedal for swells, through my delay pedals.. then later, my Strymon Blue Sky Reverb pedal (sometimes with the shimmer effect). Hope that helps. I don\'t think it was meant for bass necessarily, but it does the job for the one or two songs I needed.'}
