{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MR6IHK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392019200, 'question': 'Will it work on Mandolin', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It should work fine with any instrument you can clamp it onto. I has a chromatic tuner setting that I have used for Bass, Guitar and Uke and it will tell you what pitch it receives and when it is exactly on that note.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MR6IHK', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': 'Will it work with an electric guitar without amplifier? I have a http://amzn.com/B000BBRZ3S but it needs an amplifier for tuning =(', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. I have a Fender Ft-004 on my Telecaster right now. I just tuned it. It is NOT connected to the amp. The vibration, like a tuning fork, carries thru the wood to the Ft-004. I own 3 of them so far.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MR6IHK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'Can this be used to tune a acoustic guitar?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes this tuner is actually made for tuning acoustic guitars. I also use it to tune my Gibson electric guitar, but I do it when I have it unplugged. This is the best tuner I have found and easy to use. The screen is blue and when you hit the correct tuning the screen turns green. There is also a needle that shows if you are sharp or flat to know which way to turn the tuning knob.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MR6IHK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426057200, 'question': 'Can it tune in drop d', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. You can use the chromatic mode to tune any string to any note frequency. All you need to know is what each string should be tuned to for drop D (or any other tuning). If you do not know the notes then it is a good idea that you learn them :)'}
