{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005MR6IHK', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'would this work for a hammered dulcimer?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "it's a chromatic tuner and it picks the vibration from the instrument, so it should work with any instrument that has a large enough section where the tuner can be clipped. Looking at pictures of hammer dulcimers in Google I see that it has a box structure and I don't see where it could be clipped. Maybe the best option for it would be a tuner like a Korg CA1 or similar with a clip on adapter like the Korg CM-100L that could be clipped in the sound hole."}
