{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N4N2GW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397113200, 'question': 'How can I fix my Keyboard. It is not turning on. Can you help me?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Chances are, it's most likely your power cord/adapter. I work at a Radio Shack and we sell that same lighted keyboard. You can check it by taking the keyboard into a Radio Shack, and they'll be able to look at the power adapter, test it, and recommend a replacement which is part of their store stock. Average price of a power adapter like that should be anywhere from 15 to 30 bucks. :-)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005N4N2GW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Are the keys touch sensitive?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No... not in the true sense of the word where pressing lightly yields a quite ("pianismo", if you will!) tone and striking the key gives a louder tone. However, they do offer sustain such that the note will be sustained while you hold down the key. Some sampled sounds even change the longer you hold the key... but, that is more information than you asked for! Good luck with your decision.'}
