{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005NACC6M', 'answerTime': 'Apr 8, 2013', 'unixTime': 1365404400, 'question': 'How do the built-in mics compare with $50 to $100 MXL, Behringer, or Audio Technica condenser mics?', 'answer': "They're actually very accurate mics, in my opinion. In that low of a price range I think you'll find them to be better, however they are pretty susceptible to noise, whether it's from interference, wind (even just from moving them), or the rumbling of handling the unit while you're recording. If you use external mics you don't get the handling noise, but the wind can be protected against with a wind screen. Despite all that noise stuff, I'm very happy with the internal mics! You just have to be careful while handling the unit when it's recording with them."}
