{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B005OH07ZM', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419840000, 'question': 'If I want my friend to send me a bass line should he send it with a click track in the song? Should he play to a click track and send it? Or can he se', 'answer': 'What is the purpose? Are you trying to jam along to the track and have the bass line be a perfect loop every time? If that is the case then yes, have him play to a click. If you plug in directly or from a bass amp you can set the sample to start recording when he starts playing, but you will have to manually end the loop at the end of the measure or phrase. Then listen back to it and see how it sounds, if its not perfect you can edit the start/end point of the loop. It can be difficult to get a perfect loop but not impossible. Hopefully that helps!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005OH07ZM', 'answerTime': 'Oct 31, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414738800, 'question': 'Is this machine compatible with Roland V-Drums?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Absolutely YES! You can plug up to 4 trigger pads in the back (mono) Inputs are labeled (1/2) and (3/4). You must use an INSERT CABLE if you use 4 pads. Hope this helps :)'}
