{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B005P4NVJI', 'answerTime': 'Feb 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392710400, 'question': 'I am in a two piece band and would rather use a pedal to play back bass parts than to try and find another member.Is this the right pedal for that?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Sort of it definitely can be done but it can be tedious to map out a whole song for a bass line. A good thing is that you guys would be forced to stay on tempo. There would be couple different ways you guys could do it. One is to record the whole bass line front to back in one track. Or put verse on one track, chorus, on one and like a bridge on another. With that method you are limited to 3 progressions. It can be done. You would just have to sit down and record it all.'}
