{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0061OPQK8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1398668400, 'question': 'I have a L+R XLR outputs on my mixer, and XLR inputs 1+2 on my subwoofer. do I use this splitter to hook up to just input 1? will my JBL 500watt Sub turn the mono input from this into stereo output to my mains?', 'answer': 'This is a mono hook up to send one mono source signal to two separate mono inputs like the XLR L or R input on two different speakers. You would need a second patch cable to handle the other channel. It does not combine signals to make a stereo signal. It is mono in, mono out, either way the signal is flowing.'}
