{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0062RMHRO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'Where do I purchase all Gold Hardware for a TCI TC Style Alston Guitar?', 'answer': "I've not done this but I have bougth guitar parts from various vendors. There are many companies that sell 'gold plated' hardware. I have bought Gover tuners (gold) to replace some on a Les Paul that were great. I don't know if anyone has 'gold plate' hardware for a 'Telecaster' style guitar. Another possibility is to take the parts to a jewler and see if they might gold plate them for you. (I would NOT do this with the Pick-ups, however.) The bridge plate and other HW could be plated ... but remember gold is soft and without an OVERCOAT it will scratch easily."}
