{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387526400, 'question': 'Are these the right type of panels to be used on ceiling of my audio sound room to keep noise down for my upstairs neighbor? Is there better choices?', 'answer': 'Acoustic foam is not intended to be used as a sound barrier. It will not keep sound in or sound out although it may lead to some attenuation of the transmitted signal. Foam is intended to reduce sound reflections within the room and to deaden the sound of a space. Soundproofing is an entirely different application which required floating walls/floors/ceilings and sound barrier materials.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425369600, 'question': 'I set up a karaoke room in the house, all hard surfaces including a hardwood floor. Will these reduce the "echo" of the room if I put em on the wall?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes they will reduce the echo. Put a few rugs down as well. Good luck.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422691200, 'question': 'Objective is to block or reduce sound going out of a room especially &amp; coming into it.Placing these in the room-will this work, or is there better way', 'answer': 'If you insultated the walls and use these it will result in a sound reduction.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Sep 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379228400, 'question': 'can i apply these to a door for sound blocking?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes, they absorb sound. It won't be completely sound proof but it surely will dampen noise."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Apr 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428649200, 'question': 'What else do I have to purchase in order to put this on my window? And are these easily install/removed (in case I need to uninstall them)? Thanks!', 'answer': 'I used Command Strips that are used to hang picture frames, which makes putting them up really easy, and then there\'s no real mess when you go to take them down. Really, the foam itself shouldn\'t cause any huge issues when it comes to hanging them, it mostly comes down to the solution that you use to hang them. Just make sure you use enough to keep the panels up. I used 3 of the "Command Large Picture Hanging Strips" per panel in a triangular pattern, one in both of the top corners and one in the middle at the bottom.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Feb 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425024000, 'question': 'I bought one to reduce outside noise, which way shall face outside?', 'answer': 'The flat side goes against the wall with the side with the ridges facing into the room.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423555200, 'question': 'if i play saxaphone, will i be able to use these to sound proof my room?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Hi, in my experience, this is very basic sound proofing. So can't expect too much. But if you stick them all over the room including ceiling, and rug on floor, it dose help reduce the volume."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 31, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422691200, 'question': 'Will it lessen dog barking noise if I fill in a window with this Acoustic Foam?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It will diminish any noise to some degree, but if it's coming from outside, putting it in the window will block some of it. These work best to keep sound from bouncing off walls."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00759D22C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420704000, 'question': "My old neighbour's burping, farting &amp; blowing noise are unbearable. Would this product will help to reduce some? The wall is wooden. Thanks!", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Really the only way it would help in another room would be for it to be in that room. I'm sure it will help some but you would be tring to damper sound that is already bleeding into your space. It works best by receiving soun waves and stopping them. A cheaper method would be to hang stryofoam panels on your wall. you can get them at Lowe's."}
