{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007HVGLBC', 'answerTime': 'Feb 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392105600, 'question': 'My battery went dead overnight. Is this because it was plugged into the amp? There is no power switch. Thanx, Fred', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. Its the bad thing on this unit. No power switch to save battery. If you don\'t use your guitar every day, and afraid to loss the battery if taken out of holder, just cut a rectangular piece of paper, wrap around over the battery holder where the terminals are, and push it to the battery slot. Its the easiest and simplest thing that I think. Just make sure that the paper in long enough for its easier to pull out from the slot. In short , "NO BATTERY CONTACTS".'}
