{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394006400, 'question': 'Will the ac adapter work with this light? Is there a place to plug it into the light?', 'answer': 'Absolutely!!!! Better to use the adapter than batteries; they drain very quickly. Those other answers that state it only uses batteries are incorrect. If you have doubts contact mighty bright for a definitive answer. I will only say that from day one I have been using an adapter; it connects at the top rear of the light.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'Does this model require tiny screw removal instead of clip together case to change batteries? Tiny screws are only good for getting lost.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The battery area is a slide on/off case. There are no screws used to hold the case close. It is a wonderful light. The clamp which clips onto whatever you want to attach it to is strong. Hope this helps!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388390400, 'question': 'What type of batteries does it use?', 'answer': 'AAA. I love this light (I use it clipped on a music stand) but it does eat batteries! I guess the convenience of use outweighs the cost of the batteries.'}
