{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Jun 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403161200, 'question': 'can you use it on the piano', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Its sufficiently light weight (pardon the pun) to attach to a music book or the support for the music sheet so I see no reason why it couldn't be used to light up sheet music. If your intent was to light up the keys then you'll need perhaps have multiple units."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'May 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399878000, 'question': 'Is the base (clip) on this heavy enough to stand on its own without being clipped to a desk?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'It will stand up on its own, but the whole light is very lightweight and it would not take much to knock it over.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Mar 13, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426230000, 'question': 'power goes off when I depress the clip........is this by design?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't believe that your unit is working right. it should only go through the 3 positions via the push button. The clip is not part of the circuit."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Jan 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420099200, 'question': 'How many hours of light using the three AAA batteries?', 'answer': "You'll get 4-5 if you use it on high power, more if you use it on low power. I generally turn it off between songs if I use it as a stand light. I also suggest removing the batteries before you store it after use, as the power switch is easily turned on and the battery drained."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IHYBV2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'Does this light come with a bag/case?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Mine did.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IO8LYS', 'answerTime': 'Mar 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395471600, 'question': "I have a CD recorder. It has 4 plugs. I only see 2 on this item. am I able to record CD's with this?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes. The 2 RCA female plugs are the mixers output. 2 out of the 4 female RCA plugs on your recorder are inputs. You use these. The other 2 are outputs. They go to an external amp. Not the mixer. If you wanted to hear the recording thru the mixer from the recorder, get an RCA male 2 connector to 2 (1/4" ) plugs (like guitar plugs and run them thru 2 channels on the mixer'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IO8LYS', 'answerTime': 'May 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400223600, 'question': 'Some images of this model mixer has a usb and sd card port some dont. this is a bitn misleading to me. what is the real thing does it have or not?', 'answer': "To get real, it's wattage is 250 watts per channel. It has a USB port that will play .wav and .MP3 audio files. So far it's been an awesome PA. Get a case for it, the controls are delicate."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IO8LYS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 22, 2013', 'unixTime': 1379833200, 'question': 'Is there a separate monitor output?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I bought this unit for a friend and am not familiar with it myself. However, that being said, there are four outputs on the back. I imagine two are for the mains and the other two could be used for monitors, particularly if you're not running a widely panned stereo mix."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IO8LYS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'On the top of the unit are 4 1/4" female connectors, labeled as MAIN OUT, AUX SEND and AUX RETURN. Is one of these a low level line out?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The Max out Left and right can be sent to an amp. and it has the complete mix from the mixer, Aux send can be sent to other Sound Effects and returned to be sent out through The Max out as I stated earlier to external Amp.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IO8LYS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421913600, 'question': 'My current PA says: parallel speaker 70w and 4ohm min load total.If I buy this PA, would I be able to reuse my current speakers with it?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If you have a 70w at 4 ohms minimum, this puts out 500 at 4 ohms. It will have no problem driving your current speakers.'}
