{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IUYVRS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390809600, 'question': 'Will it work with 2 people singing harmony through the same mic?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes the GTX will work with duets I use the presets I don't have time to setup but I plan to in the future maybe but what really matters is the quality of the microphone most of these cheap 30-60 dollar model you don't realize is destroying your voice but you you get it when you experience a good condenser mic with the GTX"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IUYVRS', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'Are there any decent fx for acoustic guitar?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "My acoustic sounds great through the box. You can add chorus, delay, reverb, phlanger, etc..., and there's even a 12-string setting."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IUYVRS', 'answerTime': 'Dec 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419148800, 'question': 'how many guitar fx can it do at one time? Can it do like a chorus and delay or reverb all at the same time, can you set up your own patches?', 'answer': "The machine only does one effect at a time although some of them are combinations (like distort and flange). However, there is nothing to prevent you from using effects setting on your amp or PA. For example, you can have the GTX set on Honkytonk, but have your PA also include delay. Don't mix up the vocal settings with the guitar settings, they are separate."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007IUYVRS', 'answerTime': 'May 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399186800, 'question': "doe's this cover vocals and guitar or just vocals?", 'answer': 'Both very nicely. When you go to guitar settings (8th or last one on the choices), you will find everything from clean, phase, flange, distortion, etc. and these all have settings. the voice settings involve pitch correction, harmonies (use auto key for all harmonies). voice doubling and more. Harmonies sound real and not electronic.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IUYVRS', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'Does one of the bottons do guitar effects on/off ?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, you need a footswitch. This buttons are for change between presets and activate some voice effects. In addition, each preset or voice effect have a guitar effect. For example, the preset #4 is BRICKWALL FLOYD, this preset change your voice to emulate the voice chorus present in the song "Another Brick in the Wall", you can turn on / off this voice effect, but the guitar always have the same guitar effect.'}
