{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IXCZC8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388736000, 'question': 'am buying the boss fs-6 for my roland cube 80, what else do I need to order? thanks', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'You might need to buy the cable that goes from the pedal to the amp. Other than that you should be okay. If you have the manual for the cube, it might shed a little bit more light on the subject.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007IXCZC8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388822400, 'question': 'do you need the 2 in 1 cable? can you use 1 cable, does it need a trs cable, the 2 into one, one end is trs, not sure why, actually what does it do, be using with roland cube 80', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Your going to want a Roland ga fc pedal, not a fs6, i use the fs 6 for a boss loop pedal to add effects to a t track or switch tracks, hence the reason for the trs, the boss rc 30 only has one foot switch 1/4 inch in the back so for that you need to have the dual end trs cable......can't guarantee this is going to work for you....like i said look at the ga fc pedal, it's designed for your cube 80"}
