{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007SZJEJ8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410073200, 'question': 'does it come with a pop filter?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Yes and No. It comes with one built in. It\'s not visible unless you remove the casing but don\'t do that. Lol. I recommend buying the Blue "Pop" Filter. It\'s $25 on amazon and super nice. Now when I record mostly I don\'t need to use the popper but sometimes I do and it\'s nice to have it there. It depends how intense u sing. I personally don\'t feel it\'s good enough by itself for professional uses even tho most of the time I don\'t use it I don\'t need it. So it\'s good but if u want great pop protection then buy the Pop filter.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B007SZJEJ8', 'answerTime': 'Apr 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1365750000, 'question': 'When it sits in the shockmount, it seems to bobble...is there a way to stabilize it?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'It is supposed to "bobble" a bit... That\'s the whole point of the shockmount. The more stiffly the mic is held, the more noise is transmitted to it as a result of physical motion (such as moving items on the table where the mic is sitting, or walking near the mic, etc.). The flexibility of the mount allows these vibrations to dissipate. It IS possible for the elastic to be too loose (especially with age)... But as a general rule, the flexibility in the system is good.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007SZJEJ8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385971200, 'question': 'Any recommendations for a mic stand for this? How exactly does it attach? Or does this mic have to be set on a flat surface?', 'answer': "I'm so sorry, but I don't speak english (My english is very poor) . I'll try : The device has 3 parts : -1 : The Mic ; -2 : the aluminum base , and -3 : the cable to connect to iPhone, iPad (30 pins) , and USB. The mic must be attach to the base by rotation (like a screw), you must insert the mic into the center ring an rotate until it is firmly . The base must be on a flat surface because it is (the base) flat and rigid. Excuse me if my answer is doesn't clear , but I speak spanish an my english is very elementary"}
