{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B007X8296U', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1362211200, 'question': 'What is "koa-patterned high-pressure laminate?" Sounds like they don\'t really want to tell you what wood they used for the back and sides.', 'answer': "It's pretty much wood dust particles that are pressurized and pressed into shape, then covered with a koa patterned veneer to make it look like a solid piece of koa. It makes it more affordable and scratch an dent resistant. Since the top of the guitar is one of the more crucial pieces that affects the tone of the instrument, Martin uses real Sitka spruce so it still sounds great."}
