{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0082918X4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1388304000, 'question': "will this hold a samson c01u? or I need another shock mount? I know the cable won't work... but the stand and shock mount will they work?", 'answer': "I don't know for sure but the Samson C01U is thicker than most mics . But if it doesn't, the shock mount is slightly adjustable to hold a wider mic I'm just not sure how wide it will open . But the good thing is the shock mount is replaceable/removeable so you could always get a new one."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0082918X4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'Will this mount come and be able to be used on a Blue Yeti without having to buy any sort of extra adapters or cables?', 'answer': "In my case though using the Blue Yeti and the Blue shock mount it's a little to heavy for the arm and it has a hard time holding everything up."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0082918X4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 10, 2013', 'unixTime': 1360483200, 'question': 'I would have it butted up against the wall in my studio and need it to come out a good 26 or 27 inches. Will this boom make that kind of stretch?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Probably not - it\'s well-built, but a compact length arm. Each arm section is only about 14 inches long, so it\'d basically be extended out virtually straight at 27 inches. It\'s clamped to the side of my desk about halfway to the rear of a 36" wide top, and is a very comfortable "fit" in that setting. Sounds as if you need a "full size" boom.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0082918X4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393315200, 'question': 'Will this fit a audio technica at2035?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Jared, it will fit but just barely! My AT2020USB+ has a width of 2.6 inches, and yours a width of 2.8 inches. I had to do some twisting and gentle tugging and make my fingers do some weird maneuvers. Expect a little labor. Be aware that you should avoid removing the microphone from the shock mount often. Other than that, the mount is good for the price and looks, mind me, "hella" awesome on a nice clean desktop! If you have any more questions, drop a reply!'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0082918X4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389772800, 'question': 'Will the shock mount hold an Apogee mic?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It would but since the Apogee mic is USB this is probably not the arm you are looking for. Unless you remove the mic cable & somehow replace it with a long USB cable. Or, if you don't care how it looks, just ignore the mic cable & feed a USB cable on the outside of the arm. Hope this helps."}
