{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0083FTVB8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383811200, 'question': 'Is it easy to hook up a second microphone. Also, has anyone hooked this up to a separate speakers system? We have a home theater room, and wondering.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I've done both, and it's pretty straight forward. The mic part is really easy - the mic stand has a built in second mic port, so you can get any hand held mic with the same connector as the mic that came with the system, and you're good to go. As to running through a stereo system, if I remember correctly you need to purchase a separate 2.5mm-RCA cable. That way you can connect the 2.5mm side to the Stereo Out on the mic system, and the red/white RCA side of the cable to an input on your home stereo system. Hope that makes sense and is helpful."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0083FTVB8', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414306800, 'question': 'how many microphones can I plug in?', 'answer': 'There are two microphone jacks. But, I have a wireless microphone "receiver" that I have plugged into one of the jacks. That receiver runs two wireless microphones. So, I can have 3 going at once. One wired to the stand and the two wireless. All the sound comes through the SingStand. Is a great set up for my 3 kids. HTH!'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0083FTVB8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418716800, 'question': 'Is this a TOY? Is it suitable for my 2 year old grand daughter?', 'answer': "A 2 year old. NO! It's a real Mic with a stand that teenagers and adults can use."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0083FTVB8', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418112000, 'question': 'Does this work with a Smart T.V. which has You Tube capabilities?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It has a composite audio input so I would assume so as long as your tv has composite audio output you could use it that way. However, your vocal output would be coming from the built in speaker unless you then carry the audio output to another device-it's doubtful your tv has an audio in that would work for this. I can't imagine any way that you could loop vocals back to your tv speakers because they would need to be playing the music going out and then the voice and music coming back in. Basically, you would use your t.v. for giant lyrics display and audio out for the backtrack music. You can't use the tv as a mixer, of sorts. I hope this is helpful. I'm certainly not an expert on AV."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0083FTVB8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'I would like to use this for me to entertain residents at long term care facilities. Is this just a toy? or does it have a quality sound?', 'answer': "It's definitely not a toy and it's great for home entertainment or anywhere with a small gathering of family/friends. I use mine at my piano/karaoke bar where some of the patrons come up and sing.The sound quality is ok, but not great (it's lacks bass). It has inputs for CD/MP3 players and a guitar line in, so I would say it can work for your care facility entertainment."}
