{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Nov 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415779200, 'question': "will the top hold absolutely flat/horizontal? Would it support a flat screen monitor on it's own stand?", 'answer': 'Yes, it holds flat and horizontally. There\'s some extra room around the footprint of my 13" MacBook Pro, so just make sure your flat screen\'s footprint isn\'t much larger than that.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426921200, 'question': 'WILL IT HOLD AN ARTOGRAPH IMAGE PROJECTOR?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I see why not, as long the unit is the size of a laptop, LCD projector or even a vintage Kodak slide projector. Any bigger than those mention above, it's a no."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 27, 2015', 'unixTime': 1430118000, 'question': 'What is the diameter of the pole stand. I want to attach a mic stand clamp to it.', 'answer': 'It is actually quite thick. I attached an Ipad holder to it, but I had to get the Talent iCLaw Mic/Music Stand Holder for iPad, in order for it to fit on this stand. The claw indicated that it fit a 1 inch (the smaller upper telescope, not the bottom thicker telescope base) That said, I think a mic holder that takes a 1 inch tube should work. This is an excellent stand by the way, and I currently have my Ipad claw hooked to it.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Feb 2, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422864000, 'question': 'Can it also double as a music stand?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This particular stand does nothave a deep lip (about 1/4") so you won\'t be able to just rest the papers down without first finding a way of clipping them to the plate. I have done it by using some clothes pins. If you have to make this stand do double duty, I would do it even though it is designed for laptops.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419926400, 'question': 'I would like actual dimension (inches from floor) for highest/lowest heights.', 'answer': "32 to 52. It's in the reviews. You might want to read them."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418371200, 'question': 'Could I type on it without it being wobbly or is it mainly for looking at the screen (not typing)?', 'answer': 'You can type it. It is heavy and very sturdy.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Sep 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411023600, 'question': 'What is the height range for this stand. Lowest and highest?', 'answer': 'The stand sits at 34" at the lowest setting and about 54" at the highest. It has a stop at the 54" level so you can\'t pull it out. Very sturdy at any height and excellent value for the money.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084CRYOG', 'answerTime': 'Jun 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402642800, 'question': 'What are its dimensions when folded up? Can the top surface be removed for traveling? and does the surface tend to tilt over when there is weight on it?', 'answer': 'With the top completely vertical and the stand collapsed, it\'s about 34" tall and the top is 15.75" wide. The top could be removed, but you\'re really just disassembling it. And the surface won\'t tilt - when tightened, it\'s very solid.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0084F8BU4', 'answerTime': 'Feb 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393574400, 'question': 'Do these produce the same color light as your "HitLights Cool White(6000K) 600 LEDs (Double Density) Flexible Light Strip" product? Which is brighter?', 'answer': 'I have no experience with the double density strips but the hitlights web site says the color temp for both is 6000K so I would expect the to be very close in color. The 300 ct ribbon uses smd5050 led which are brighter than the smd3528 leds on the 600 ct ribbon. I have no way to compare the brightness of the 300 ct vs 600 ct ribbons.'}
