{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085KBLIW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393747200, 'question': 'For sure it is a FIXED bell case right?', 'answer': "Yes, it's for a non removable bell, or I suppose a detachable one that you've left screwed-in. It's still going strong for me by the way. Love this case."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085KBLIW', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2013', 'unixTime': 1383724800, 'question': 'What position do the backpack straps hold the horn in? Upright - bell facing sky , or horizontal - horn sticking out from the sides of the body?', 'answer': "The horn lies flat on your back with the bell skyward. Since the bell is at an angle it does not stick out on the sides at all, i.e., I have never had trouble getting through a door. I have the shoulder straps high, but the bell is still below the top of my head. I would like to have an additional strap to join the shoulder straps across my chest, as another case I have does, which this one does not come with. So far, the straps appear solid with no sign of coming apart from slinging it around. I love being able to easily stow the straps. You might not want to put your mouthpiece in the case slot. Mine is a bit tall an I think it damaged the hinge next to it by putting upward pressure on the two halves of the case. Put the mouthpiece in its own case in the side pocket, where I always carry my metronome/tuner. I love the music pock on the back as well. It fits my Conn double well, but is too small for a larger horn (Geyer style horn) - which they don't tell you. Overall, it is a great, light case at a reasonable price."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0085KBLIW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426748400, 'question': 'Will this work well for a King single horn to be used by a 10 year old?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "The case is very light, but good protection. Inside the nylon material is a hard shell of some sort. I showed it to a member of the San Francisco Symphony and he was impressed. I am pretty sure a King single would fit - if it is too loose add some foam padding. You don't want the horn to move in the case."}
