{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085UPUI4', 'answerTime': 'May 27, 2014', 'unixTime': 1401174000, 'question': 'lumen', 'answer': "I'm assuming you mean the actual output. Can't give you the specific answer to this because it would, of course, depend on how much of the strip you use and then calculating the per-bulb output, which I can't supply. We use the strips in the entertainment cabinet. It's on 24/7 and is a night light when the tv is not on. When the tv is on, the light strip does not interfere at all with the television. Hope this helps."}
