{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0085UPTT4', 'answerTime': 'Dec 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386835200, 'question': 'does this strip of lights come with the adapter to actually plug it into a 110v wall plug or is it just the strip of lights and you need to buy something else to be able to plug it in?', 'answer': "You need to buy the adapter, it's still a great deal I used this to make a light panel for a film I was working on and I sved 500 bucks :) good luck"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0085UPTT4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 30, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391068800, 'question': 'Can this led strip be connected to a Malibu lights type outdoor power cable and controller?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'This strip is powered by a 12 volts DC converter, so as long as your power supply has an output of 12vdc then I would not hesitate hooking them up. This is a very versatile set of lights. Have fun with them.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0085UPTT4', 'answerTime': 'May 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399705200, 'question': 'dumb question, cove lighting in a room, 15 feet long.. if i double the led strip, will it make it double brighter? (add 2 strips side by side)', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. The more lights the brighter it will be. Not the individual light but the overall effect.'}
