{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPW58', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': 'what is the weight limit', 'answer': "Not sure - it's not in the specs? My son uses it, and he's just under 100 pounds."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Nov 23, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385193600, 'question': 'How tall wil this go, suitable for standing? Will the top lay horizontally? How is it holding up for you? Thanks!', 'answer': 'Yeah, I just extended it all the way, and you can raise the bottom edge (where you would rest your music) up to 48". You can lay the top horizontally (in fact, it\'ll flip 180 degrees), and with the knob you can get it to hold pretty tight. I\'m not using it professionally, so I can\'t say to what degree it would hold up when it\'s regularly being used/abused as it\'s being broken down on a regular basis. I mostly have had it in one position since I got it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406358000, 'question': 'Weight? Is it convenient to transport for frequent rehearsals or gigs?', 'answer': 'I am not sure I would want to move around. It is heavier than I would like for that. However it is a really nice stand! I am happy with it BUT it stays in one room.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395817200, 'question': "Does the tray tilt? Is there an adjustable screw or something on the back to hold it in place? I have a semi heavy binder I don't want it to tip.", 'answer': "Yes, the tray tilts, the legs can be adjusted to keep the stand from falling over, raise it up, or down. I really like the stand, I got this one for my granddaughter and she loves it. I have another brand which cost more, works the same way, and it's a tad bit heavier than this one, it's also 12 years old. If I had to replace it, I would buy this stand for myself as well."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Aug 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407049200, 'question': 'What is the minimum height adjustment?', 'answer': '2 ft from the floor to the lip of the stand that holds the music'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Sep 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410591600, 'question': 'Is this sturdy enough to use as a textbook stand for 5lb books? I need a tall textbook stand, and all I can find are desktop ones with no pole/legs.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I don't think there would be a problem with a 5lb book, it seems sturdy enough, the legs can be stretched out far enough to stay balanced. I have some large music books that weigh 3lbs, or more, and I haven't had any problems."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386230400, 'question': 'height adjustment suitable for a petite (10 yrs) girl?', 'answer': "Most of the 10 year old kids I teach are able to use the stand. I buy one every time I see them here on sale because they're more expensive in the stores. I think the height of the stand would only affect my younger students who are 4 and 5 years old. The stand is very sturdy to hold music, a metronome, etc. I've only had one that broke and it was because I have students repeatedly leaning their whole body weight on the stand. Understandably a music stand won't be able to sustain 50 to 60 lb kids."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B0087UPXG6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 9, 2015', 'unixTime': 1428562800, 'question': 'What are the dimensions of the tray? We are looking for something 20+ inches that will enable several sheets of music to be viewed at one time?', 'answer': 'The tray is exactly 19-3/4 inches wide and the ledge is 2-1/4 inches deep. Item is very sturdy.'}
