{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008IYP8ES', 'answerTime': 'Nov 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415606400, 'question': 'Would this fit on a Fender MIJ 1986 Contemporary Telecaster?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No. The tremolo unit on this guitar is a fender modified licensed Floyd rose tremolo and most likely built by Schaller. You will need to find one of similar build. The problems too, as you may be aware are that these guitars were build during a transitional period for Fender guitars and so there were many different styles and types of builds. The only good thing being that most of the Floyd Rose Tremolo units were made by Schaller and so you may be able to obtain replacement parts or units that will fit from them.'}
