{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008O516L0', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'Does this have a built in noise-gate, or would I have to buy a separate noise-gate?', 'answer': 'The QX1002USB does not have a built in "classic" noise gate function although you could use the built in one-knob compressor to smooth out (i.e. compress) audio on channels 1 and 2. There is also a low-cut filter to remove low frequencies from channels 1 and 2. If you need a "classic" noise gate to mute a channel when there is no live signal coming to a channel, you need to buy a separate a unit and put it in front of the channel mix. I hope this helps.'}
