{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008O516L0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'to connect my 80\'s synth (has the midi 5-pin in/out on the back), would I only need one plug going from midi out to the 1/4" outlets on the mixer?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, the MIDI output of your synth does not send audio, it\'s just for control signals. This mixer does not have any MIDI capabilities. To get sound from your synth to this mixer, you\'d need to connect the audio outputs (1/4" or whatever your synth has) to the 1/4" inputs of this mixer with appropriate cables/adapters.'}
