{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008O516JW', 'answerTime': 'Jul 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406098800, 'question': 'Is there a way to monitor through headphones while listening to accompaniment track and not record this all on one track? HELP!!', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "It kind of depends on the program that you are using but if you look at this 2 black buttons where it says USB/ 2-Track then don't put the main mix on. Maybe its different with other Softwares, but I'm shure if you try around a lil bit with them 2 buttons you'll get it done."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008O516JW', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': 'Does the headphone jack have latency? I have noticed slight latency in the headphone monitor on other inexpensive Behringer devices (i.e. the UCA202)', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "I haven't noticed any significant latency with the headphone monitor, especially for monitoring directly from the mixer. Additionally, while using it to monitor audio from my PC I haven't noticed anything significant. I would like to note that I have been using my Q502 in a Windows 8.1 64-bit environment."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008O516JW', 'answerTime': 'May 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399618800, 'question': 'what is the bit depth? can this record 96khz?', 'answer': 'Hi, The manual says "They enable you to use the greatly extended dynamic range of your 24-bit/192-kHz HD recorder to the fullest, thereby maintaining optimal audio quality But the specs say usb 48 khz Guess you\'ll have to call Behringer on that one.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008O516JW', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'It is compatible with Steinberg Cubase recording software?', 'answer': 'Yes, it is compatible with Cubase. The mixer will be recognized by your computer as a STEREO input device (because all 5 inputs are mixed down to two channels). This means that you will not be able to record each of the 5 inputs independently in Cubase (you would want an audio interface like the Native Instruments Komplete Audio 6 if you wanted to do something like that).'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008O517IW', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': 'How do I connect an RCA audio source (CD player) into this while maintaining the audio from my 3 mics? The 2-track mutes the mics.', 'answer': 'I haven\'t tried it, but I would think you would need to convert from your RCA to 1/4" banana plug type adapters such as the Hosa Cable GPR101 RCA To 1/4 Inch TS Adaptor - 2 Pack. (Search it on Amazon). You need to connect it as an audio source, the RCA plugs on these don\'t seem to do much but give you sound through the headphones coming back in so for example if you were using a metronome to keep time while laying down a bass groove, you wouldn\'t actually be passing that metronome click back through to your recording, just the headphones...'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008O517IW', 'answerTime': 'Dec 9, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386576000, 'question': 'Can this mixer control the audio input from USB cable or RCA ? It do have controls(EQ,level, comp, etc) for all 12 channel, but no control for USB or', 'answer': 'No, the USB/RCA "returns" can be sent to the Headphones or Control Room Output; but not as an Input that can be actively mixed. This return is more of a confidence audio return.'}
