{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008R7F4YU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'Are these piano keys?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hello Catherine (my Mom\'s name.. also spelled with a "C") Yes and No....... They are standard sized piano keys made of lite plastic.. They are "weighted" to "mimic" the "feel" of real keys.. there are 61 not 88... as this is a keyboard. It is missing some "octaves"... not an issue for general playing .. the unit has good "note" sound reproduction.. I bought it mainly for the CASIO song "learning system" witch is first rate I have a full sized "high end" YAMAHA digital piano...which is my main instrument ... but, they cost many, many times this Casio . A necessity ONLY if you want to be "serious player". REC III'}
