{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008XEYT48', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1416384000, 'question': 'How portable are these? Would they be OK a crowded subway? Can you rest them around your neck comfortably (without adjusting the head size)?', 'answer': "Can't really rest them on my neck with comfort. I tried them walking around in an airport but found them a little bulky, hard to keep up with what's going on around me. Love the sound and use them a lot in coffee shops."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008XEYT48', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413529200, 'question': "Where can I buy a replacement cable that doesn't cost 20% of the original price payed for the headphones?", 'answer': "The replacement cable is just a generic 3.5mm male-to-male wire. I've been using these. http://www.amazon.com/Monoprice-109764-3-Feet-Stereo-Plated/dp/B00AJHB8R8/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1413554120&sr=8-1&keywords=3.5+male+to+male"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B008XTV8G0', 'answerTime': 'Apr 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1397199600, 'question': 'Would this device run off of a type of rechargeable battery? I would like to put one on my bicycle for riding at night.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Used these lights on our haunted trail. Before setting them in place and running power to a transformer we used a 12 volt, rechargeable battery used for jumping a car. Worked fine for our purposes, yet very heavy. Possibly a deer feeder/uninterruptible power supply battery or similar may do the job.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008XTV8G0', 'answerTime': 'Jun 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402815600, 'question': 'If I buy more than one, will one remote be able to control the lights or will I need to have a separate remote for each light?', 'answer': 'The ones that I bought all worked with the same remote.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008XTV8G0', 'answerTime': 'Jul 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1375081200, 'question': 'How bright is this light? I want to use it to light up my small backyard fountain. I am afraid it will be too dim...', 'answer': 'I have mine install on a fountain and it is bright and very pretty. It is as bright as a 100 watt spot light. Quality is very good. Make sure to pick up a power supply/ driver. As these are 12 volt, the driver/ power supplies are very inexpensive, around 5- 15 dollars. So you need a 12 volt to 120 volt driver/ power supply. But trust me for the price these are awesome lights. I have 25 around my yard and it make a stunning lighting effect. They can also be connected to a low voltage system. We will be very happy with it.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B008XTV8G0', 'answerTime': 'Feb 12, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392192000, 'question': "I'd like to use a DMX controller inside do you have access to the RGB?", 'answer': "It came with a (seemingly) standard RGB remote, but I powered the unit up and could not get it to work. I pulled the tape on the coin cell in the controller and tried from many angles but could not get it to operate. Haven't tried it since then."}
