{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009AK3NDW', 'answerTime': 'Apr 17, 2015', 'unixTime': 1429254000, 'question': 'I see it has 1/4 outputs R--L. If you run it to a mono PA, if you take only L to pa input will that be the full sound or does it have to be a dual 1/4', 'answer': "I have ultranova, but both synths has same engine. So if I plug UN to mono power amp I will have only R or L channel on stereo patches. If you going to play bass or any mono sound (without FX) this doesn't matter, both channels yield same signal. But if you have mono amp and want to play stereo sounds (loosing stereo but saving spectrum) you can make (or buy) stereo to mono cable and mixdown both channels in mono like this http://www.cambridge-mt.com/SitePix/Fig2-7aUpdate.jpg May be need to change resistors to 2.5K, depends on your amp"}
