{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009QU3MKK', 'answerTime': 'Jul 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406012400, 'question': 'This product vs. TC Electronic Ditto Looper X2 ? Debating between the two... which has greater features and performance would you say? Does it record/play in 24bit?', 'answer': "I started with the Ditto but sent mine back right away. Too bare bones. Limited features. I wound up with the JamMan Solo XT which I like a lot for guitar practice, improvising, etc. Tons of memory on micro SD card, connects to computer for backing up loops or importing them into a DAW. I don't think the TC Ditto has connectivity with computers. i'd say go with the jam man if you can."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009QU3MKK', 'answerTime': 'Mar 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395298800, 'question': 'Will the JamMan Solo XT "JamSync" with the JamMan Express XT, or even the JamMan Stereo? That would be great.', 'answer': 'Anything with "XT" in the name (which right now is the JamMan Express XT and Solo XT) can sync with other XT\'s. Be careful not to get a JamMan Solo (no XT) if you need that feature.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009QU3MKK', 'answerTime': 'Feb 25, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424851200, 'question': 'I get bad feedback from JamMan Solo XT when I press the pedal to record. Guitar and amp hooked up per instructions.', 'answer': 'Try reducing the output volume. I have to keep mine fairly low. Takes some tweaking'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B009QU3MKK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': 'IF you hold down the LOOP UP or LOOP DOWN buttons, does it "scroll" through the presets or must you press the UP/DOWN button once for each number?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'If you kept it pressed, you will scroll up or down continuosly until you take your finger off the button.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009QU3MKK', 'answerTime': 'Aug 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407999600, 'question': 'The power supply jack is labeled 9 VDC/200 mA . Is this compatible with most multi-jack adapters for several pedals or is the polarity reversed?', 'answer': "Yes, It is reverse polarity. No, it won't necessarily work with a multi-Jack because even with a polarity reversing adapter, it still needs to be 200 amps. I have the Joyo multi and the Visual Sound multi and they're both 100 amps."}
