{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009SXJL50', 'answerTime': 'Jul 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374649200, 'question': 'With 1 transmitter and 2 receivers, is it possible to have the 2 receivers on different channels? i.e. one light turn red and other turn green?', 'answer': 'Each receiver and transmitter has about 5 or 6 different frequencies it can communicate across (using the word channels is confusing since that is the data its transmitting). For example, you can set the transmitter to red (it uses colors to distinguish between frequencies) and only the red receiver will recieve the data it send, and if you set a reciever to green, it will not receive that data unless it is coming from a green transmitter. I hope that makes sense, i wasnt entirely certain of your question.'}
