{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009WQJCLQ', 'answerTime': 'Mar 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395558000, 'question': 'What very basic items would I need to make sound out of this item? I mean cords, amps, etc. I have never owned one, and do not own an amplifier.', 'answer': 'You need something that makes the actual sound, and something to connect this item to your sound producer. There are several ways to do this. The standard way is to get some sort of amplifier, and connect this to that with a 1/4" instrument cable. If you don\'t want to buy an amp, and you have a stereo that has RCA inputs (the red & white cables), you could connect this to that stereo with a 1/4" to RCA audio cable.'}
