{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009WQJCLQ', 'answerTime': 'Nov 28, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385625600, 'question': 'What not-included items does this NEED or are RECOMMENDED to operate this theremin properly: mic stand, amp, foot pedal, mixer, and/or...?', 'answer': "You'll need an amplifier and a cable to connect the theremin to the amp. That's it! As you become accustomed to the instrument, you can add effects, if you wish, but they are not necessary. The Great Sounding Theremin at a Great Price is a table top model, so there's no need for a mic stand."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009WQJCLQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387353600, 'question': "i receive this theremin today and it doesn't work, is it because of adapter or what should i do?", 'answer': "Are you located outside of the North America? If the answer is 'yes', you will need to either use a power converter or you can replace the U.S. standard supply with one that is compatible for your country. This instrument needs to receive between 12 and 24 volts DC to play properly. It draws very little power, so that isn't a concern. Don't forget to check the cable connecting the theremin to your amplifier. Bad cables can causes problems. Thanks!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009WQJCLQ', 'answerTime': 'Dec 26, 2012', 'unixTime': 1356508800, 'question': 'Do you ship to the UK? and will the US power supply be compatible with UK sockets?', 'answer': "Burns Theremins does ship to the UK. They do so often. This instrument comes with a US standard supply. To play in the UK, you'll need to either use a power converter (readily available via Amazon or Amazon UK) or you can replace this supply with one that is of the UK standard that you acquire there. Burns Theremins includes instructions how to do this with all overseas shipments. Also available here on Amazon is a battery powered model in a different case configuration. Called the 'Zep Theremin - Battery Powered' this instrument may be what you are looking for!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B009YC78BY', 'answerTime': 'Jun 12, 2013', 'unixTime': 1371020400, 'question': "Must this mic be used with a transmitter or can it be used on it's own?", 'answer': 'It can be used on its own only if your recording device can supply condenser mic voltage (approximately 3 VDC). This is an option on many field and portable recorders, as well as many PCs and laptops. I hope this is what you are asking.'}
