{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AFJ820G', 'answerTime': 'Dec 24, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387872000, 'question': 'Can I input songs using an ipod? Looking for a high quality way for my daughter to sing and record current songs-would an amp,ipod, and mic do it?', 'answer': "No you cannot input an ipod on this player, I haven't looked into ipod's and karaoke. The concept sounds like a good idea and I'm sure it has been done. I own this karaoke player and it will record singing to an sd card or a flash drive. I own several Karaoke CD+G's and I record them to flash drives. I've never recorded my own singing LOL"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AFJ820G', 'answerTime': 'Sep 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410850800, 'question': 'can you copy a karaoke DVD to a USB drive and have this player play it from the USB? Same question for VCD.', 'answer': 'The product description states: "The DGX-213\'s most important feature is to convert CD+Gs into MP3+Gs and storing them on a USB device or SD card. You also have the option to record using many sources such as from your CDs, VCDs, CD+Gs, MP3+Gs, or AVI files (AVI audio track must be encoded in MP3)." Even if it didn\'t or you decide to purchase a different Karaoke player, you can copy the CD+G\'s to your computer, then using a free software called AudioGrabber, you can convert it to any number of file types and copy them to a USB, or to a CD in a format some other player uses like MP3.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AFJ820G', 'answerTime': 'Nov 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384502400, 'question': 'When you do karaoke, is there default videos or images that scroll by or play in the background?', 'answer': "It's depended on the media that you are playing. CD+G and MP3+G Karaoke will have onscreen lyric and a blue background. DVD/VCD Karaoke will have onscreen lyrics and moving background. This Karaoke player will read all of the format mentioned above."}
