{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AH9P1CG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396854000, 'question': 'Where is this guitar made?', 'answer': "The build is very, very good on this Korean made guitar. Not mentioned is the impressive one piece side and center block construction. Also Grovers and Duncan designed pickups and nicely sized body. Packed with perks, great fit and finish. Don't know why Samick didn't make more of a splash. (Too many sheeples out there, I would guess)"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AH9P1CG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396854000, 'question': "I was told by the company that production of RL4's was moved to Indonesia in 2005. Do you think this would be the same guitar as the Korean made?", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "guitarguy , I recieved my Korean RL-4 late last month . It had inspection tags dated 4/12/2005! Although the Samick box looked like it was accosted by a grizzly bear, the guitar itself was pristine and obviously never handled. Seeing that Amazon has (had?) only one more, I might assume they were from the same batch, although this assumption has no guarantees , of course. If not to your satisfaction (wink, wink), who could fault you for returning a 9 year old guitar . If it's in the same shape as the one I recieved, I'm sure you'll be thrilled !! Be sure to let me know ...."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AH9P1CG', 'answerTime': 'Apr 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396681200, 'question': 'where is this guitar made?', 'answer': "The guitar is made in Korea, but don't let that stop you... The craftmanship is very good to excellent. I'm a pro guitar tech , I play Jazz and it has served me well . I've compared it to other US and chinese made guitars and it is a great guitar for the money you spend . I will continue to use it until I can afford a custom carved top and back Jazz Box... JJ Vibrato"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AHRVDDO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 7, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386403200, 'question': 'If you used this with a Blue Snowball, would you mind pointing me in the right direction to what size adapter I need for this to work? Thank you.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I created my own. I used an old T-shirt wound around the stem coming from the Blue. It doesn't look too bad (no one really sees mine anyway), and may help isolate an vibrations even better."}
