{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AL77P8W', 'answerTime': 'Oct 17, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413529200, 'question': 'I have a set of QSC K8 (powered) speakers - can I connect these to the 600i to effectively have a 4 speaker set-up?', 'answer': 'You can. All you\'ve got to do is connect them to the "monitor out" 1/4" outputs (which are unpowered) and into the inputs in the K8s (GREAT SPEAKERS!). The only problem is that the "monitor" channel functions as an aux channel so you\'ll have to either use the K8s as monitors or reverse the mix ("monitor" for the mains and main for the monitors). Other than that, should work like a champ. Great unit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AL77P8W', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': 'Are the RCA jacks on channel 7/8 line outputs? I also am wanting to record from the board, but may also need to run monitors at the same time.', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': "Only line inputs, not line outputs in channel 7/8. You can't record from the board and run monitors at the same time, only one or the other"}
