{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AOFJBSI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2013', 'unixTime': 1387526400, 'question': 'What does PU leather mean?', 'answer': 'Bicast leather (also known as bycast leather or PU leather, sometimes described as split leather) is a material made with a split leather backing covered with a layer of polyurethane that is applied to the surface and then embossed. The resulting product has an artificially consistent texture that is easier to clean and maintain, as is the case with most plastic materials.'}
