{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AZ57KZI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 4, 2013', 'unixTime': 1386144000, 'question': 'Is there some place I can get assembly instructions?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'They did not have them last I asked. They would have been handy :('}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AZ57KZI', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'Where do I get instructions? Seems like a bad thing to have to put together without them...', 'answer': 'i built a b004 about a year ago. my first and i dont play, just like woodwork and projects. the kit had no instructions and i could not find any. assume you have all the parts of the kit. then get started. look everything over. get an idea in your head about what this guitar will look like. fit the neck and body together. they may have matching numbers. make sure the neck and body fit perfectly before gluing up. stain or paint the parts before assembly. do not get stain or paint in the joint area of the neck and body. tape it off. tape off the fret board and end nut. now sand and paint. youll be ok. takes a little time.'}
