{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00AZ98Z8U', 'answerTime': 'Nov 19, 2013', 'unixTime': 1384848000, 'question': 'Does it support Launchpad', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00AZ98Z8U', 'answerTime': 'Oct 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412492400, 'question': 'One of the reviews wrote, "..you can only use around 3 Plugin sounds per project." What? Each project is limited to three plugins?', 'answer': 'He may have been talking about third-party plug-ins. You can use "unlimited" Ableton audio and MIDI effects, however many of the Ableton effects are not available in the lite version (obviously, because they want you to buy the 500 version) However, my advice is to get the cheap version, use it alot, and get really good at it. That\'s more important than all the bells and whistles. For example, a guy that can play just plain piano really good, is better than a guy with a synth with 1000 voices that can\'t play. For the record, here\'s the official comparison of Live 9 versions: https://www.ableton.com/en/live/feature-comparison/'}
