{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': "Hey there! I'm using iXY and Rode Rec (payed) but still can't monitor the sound by headphone. It has to be activated? Help! Tks", 'answer': 'If using headphones with a headset mic attached, make sure they are plugged in BEFORE the iXY otherwise they will be automatically selected by your device as the input.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Nov 29, 2013', 'unixTime': 1385712000, 'question': 'Will this mic rotate so it can be used to provide HD sound over a video recording?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Does not rotate and is fixed in position by the 30 way connector on iPhone, iPad or iPod Touch. But you can rotate the Apple device that you are using for the recording so that mic channels are vertical or horizontal etc. Rode were supposed to be bringing out a hot-shoe clamp to hold iXY mic attached to iPhone or iPod Touch. You can also take analog output from the iPhone jack socket and record direct onto the camera.'}
