{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': 'Does the app allow for multi-tracking?', 'answerType': 'N', 'answer': 'No, the Rode app only caters for L&R from either the Rode iXY or the iOS device internal mic. But you can export .wav or .mp3 recordings to Audacity and manipulate them there.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Aug 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408518000, 'question': "What's the frequency response for this mic? The description mentions 24-bit/96kHz recording, implying a frequency response of around 48kHz.", 'answer': 'Frequency response implies a lower and upper frequency and signal amplitude variation measured in decibels. For the RODE iXY that is 20Hz to 20KHz +/- 3dB in other words pretty flat. 48KHz is the maximum frequency that can be digitised by a 96KHz sampling frequency (the Nyquist criterion). You can access further details on the microphone by Googling RODE iXY Specs.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Mar 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394780400, 'question': 'Does this microphone work with I pad air, and I phone five S', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "This model will not work on the iPad Air or the 5 series phone. The reason being it needs the 30 pin connector to plug into. I use mine on the iPhone 4S and it is a fantastic mic. You can get true professional field recordings with it. The good news for you iPhone 5S and iPad Air owners is that Rhodes does make a model for you now. It's slowly been hitting some pro audio sales sites or just go to Rhodes website."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B41JIY8', 'answerTime': 'Jan 9, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389254400, 'question': "Since you can't charge the iphone while the mic is attached, how long can you expect to record on a full iphone charge?", 'answer': "I haven't recorded any longer than about 3.5 hours at a time, but that length was no problem for the battery. You'll want to put your phone in airplane mode though and turn off wifi, blue tooth, etc. so that iXY gets full resources and optimum battery usage. It sucks when the recording stops because the system was interrupted by something, and there's no indication from the app, it just cuts off in that case as if you had hit stop."}
