{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B5I9GYW', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'How noisy is this product?', 'answer': "Each output is not individually isolated, so you'll most likely get noise in your signal chain somewhere, especially if you're plugging power hungry digital pedals into the chain. If I plug my Walrus Audio Descent between a delay and pitch shifter (all connected to the brick), I get very obvious digital clicks from the Descent. I'd recommend a Voodoo Labs Pedal Power 4X4 if you want noise isolation."}
