{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 15, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405407600, 'question': 'when you export multi track recordings, do the files keep their individual tracks?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'You can export to only a 44.1K 16 bit stereo or mono file. However you can choose the track to be exported. Normally I export the multi track recordings into a few files and import to the computer for further process.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'Oct 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414306800, 'question': 'I want to play a recorded backing track while singing live. Can I do this through the recorder or do I need to add a mixer downstream from it?', 'answer': "Your best bet would be to record your backing track into the Tascam (you have 8 tracks to use), then add a mike and record into a different track. The. Tascam has an equalizer so you can adjust the spund of your vpice as desired. Great little device. I wasted two years buying one software package after another to use on my computer and none of them were worth a toot. I love the Tascam for its ease and portability. The learning curve is moderate but the manual is very good at walking your through the process of making a master track (wav file) which can then be uploaded onto your computer. I downloaded another free software to change the wav file into an mp3. You'll love the Tascam onvce you are used to using it."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'Feb 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392537600, 'question': 'Can you record a drum machine track on here and add vocals and guitar later?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I always record the basic drum track on track 1 on the left set of knobs and then add guitars, keyboards, vocals, etc on the other tracks 2-8. You can export some of thise tracks and empty them out and reuse them again if you need more than the 8 available. As long as you keep a couple of basic tracks to follow along with, you'll still be able to make them all match up time wise."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'May 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400742000, 'question': 'i really want this unit, the reviews sound great, but i have a question: do you absolutely HAVE to download your music via some music software to your computer for some reason? or can you directly download to a CD recorder if you wish to?', 'answer': "You could mix to stereo on the unit and put the line out to the line in on a CD recorder, then play from the Tascam and record straight to CD. It wouldn't be a digital transfer though, and you'd need to manually define the tracks on the recorder."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'Jul 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1405062000, 'question': 'Can you transfer the files to a computer using the SD card? And how do you get the song recorded on the SD card to transfer it?', 'answer': 'I do not actually remember. I believe it was more cumbersome to transfer than just dragging files off the sd card.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402124400, 'question': 'can you bounce tracks? and if so, is there any signal degeneration? how difficult is it to bounce if it is possible?', 'answer': 'Yes, there is such function but I have not use it. I suggest to read the user manual on Page 51. http://www.tascam.eu/en/docs/DP-008EX_Manual.pdf'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'May 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399705200, 'question': 'if I record a rythym guitar and vocal track, can I play it back and add another guitar track while listening to the 1st?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. You can record 2 new tracks at a time and it plays all the tracks while you are recording the new ones. If you don't want to hear the other tracks, you can manually turn them down or mute them. Hope this helps. it is a magnificent machine for the price."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00B9060X6', 'answerTime': 'May 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399100400, 'question': 'Can you record at the same time as playback (of another track)?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, you can. You can record one or two tracks simultaneously, while the remaining tracks are playing back.'}
