{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BEGS5NI', 'answerTime': 'Jan 28, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390896000, 'question': 'What type of microphone works well with this unit, and what kind of input (size) does it have? 3.5 mm or 1/4 "?', 'answer': 'I find for just sketching with my guitar or even catching a band practice the on board mics are pretty good. It only comes with two 1/4 input (channels 1 and 2). Ive used an sm 58 and beta 58 (for vocals) with a chord with the xlr and 1/4 on either end. I use an sm 57 for my amp, though sometimes I go di from the amp (its a DT25). I may just get an adapter and leave it plugged in to the unit. All these options have worked great for me.'}
