{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BHCMFXU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 8, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420704000, 'question': 'Im hoping to bypass the Fishman software and use it with NI Komplete 10 Ultimate does anyone have any experience with that? Thanks!', 'answer': 'It will work with pretty much any MIDI instrument. You will just have to program your own combis and layers in your DAW. Thats the way I use it most of the time because the Triple play software needs to be updated to be compatible with the newest software instruments that are available.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BHCMFXU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'Would the Tripleplay be reasonable for use in live performance situations? Can you change sounds quickly enough to make it work?', 'answer': 'IMHO, you will be dealing with the same kind of limitations/challenges as any other PC based configurations for live sets. If you are brave enough to work with computers in live performance, just consider the triple Play as any other controller. Delays and change in sounds will depend strongly on your computer configuration. Hope it helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BHCMFXU', 'answerTime': 'Apr 1, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427871600, 'question': 'Does Triple play use a propitiatory driver, or is it USB Class compliant for Windows?', 'answer': "I use a Mac, so I can't speak for Windows. After I set up the sensitivity and tuning in the Fishman application, the info was stored in the transmitter. Now I just put the USB receiver dongle into the Mac when needed and all my different softwares (Reason, Logic, Reaktor) see it as a MIDI keyboard without using the Fishman software."}
