{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BHN05H2', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'Love the Rode quality, but has anyone found a cheap alternative with good audio quality?', 'answer': "Ya... I bought the Sony ECMCS3 Clip style Omnidirectional Stereo Microphone http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0058MJX4O/ for $27.95, and got the 3.5mm StereoTRRS 4-Pole M to TRS Jack Microphone to iPhone Adapter http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B00DQH8NAS/ for another $20.00... I saved $10 dollars at the end of the day and the quality was much better on the Sony. You can just try any of the other cheap lavalier mics with that adapter above and probably save yourself even more. I'm returning this ASAP..."}
