{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BID0C1U', 'answerTime': 'Dec 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417507200, 'question': 'Can the plug be cut off and it then be hardwired in?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Perhaps. The trick is to supply 12v DC to the lights. I think the transformer is in the little box with the blades that fit into the plug, so you would have splice in before the transformer. When I replaced my fluorescent under-counter lights, my solution was to pull the old lights, install a plug at the end of those hard wires, and then plug into that. A bit of extra work, but not bad.'}
