{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BL6JDUA', 'answerTime': 'Dec 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417766400, 'question': "I'm reading the reviews and more than one person hasn't had much of an assortment when it came to their celluloid picks. I just wanted to know why?", 'answer': 'My assortment included 7 different thicknesses of picks, including 5 medium thickness, total of 12. This is exactly what it says-an assortment. I assume most people would prefer medium picks, thus the quantity. You will not find 12 quality picks for this price anywhere else. People should think before they write comments-Fred'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BL87C42', 'answerTime': 'Oct 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1412233200, 'question': "I'm hearing sound in only the left ear piece. Shouldn't the transmitter send both channels and the receiver receive both channels?", 'answer': 'You could if you had two XLRs and two mics for left and right. Then you would have both audio channels. Otherwise you have just the one channel and one mic. I prefer just the mono while shooting and recording. Then I balance it out in post, and in stereo.'}
