{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BLQ7M4E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 26, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403766000, 'question': 'Would this stand work well for a child-sized guitar and would it be easy for the child (age 7) to sit the guitar correctly in it?', 'answer': 'I would say yes, in fact it might fit better than the full size one my son uses it for. It is pretty stable so a 7 year old should be able to manage just fine. I got it for the portability as my son travels so I do not know if there might be a better model for a stationery situation.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BLQ7M4E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1403679600, 'question': 'Please this stand is good for Ovation guitars? Ovation is fatty and like Laud instrument.', 'answer': "I can't imagine that it would work for an Ovation. As you can see, it is designed to fit flat against the essentially flat back of a guitar. I would think you would need to look for a stand that holds the guitar up at the headstock and the body hangs free."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BLQ7M4E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402902000, 'question': 'will an electric guitar fit on this stand', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'When I purchased my stand, it was for only a youth guitar. I am not familiar with the size of electric guitars. The depth front to back with youth guitar allows for a second almost to fit. It is low to the ground. Not sure if that is an issue for you with connections and wires. I have not seen it be tipped over by a nearly 6 year old. It appears to have gray substance around the base which keeps it from sliding around.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BLQ7M4E', 'answerTime': 'Jun 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1402124400, 'question': 'Will this work for a junior/child-size acoustic guitar?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. But as I mentioned in my review, the stand is somewhat flimsy, so if the guitar has any real value, I'd recommend a sturdier stand (e.g. FretRest)."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BLQ7M4E', 'answerTime': 'Jul 2, 2013', 'unixTime': 1372748400, 'question': 'Will it work for electric guitars?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes, the stand base is adjustable but the guitar will have to be unplugged if it is an endpin jack. A top jack, like a strat, will likely be fine.'}
