{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BQ6KSKO', 'answerTime': 'May 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399446000, 'question': 'Will there be all of these specific effects included in the synth....Reverb, delay, fuzz, phasing?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The keyboard does not have sounds or effects built in. Its purpose is to control computer software that makes the sounds. It DOES come with software (Pro Tools Express), and it should have reverb, delay, distortion, and phaser. But again, this keyboard only works with a computer. Chances are, you\'re looking for a "workstation" or "synthesizer".'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00BQ6KSKO', 'answerTime': 'May 15, 2013', 'unixTime': 1368601200, 'question': 'hi, sorry but, not clear to me. This controller is actually compatible with major DAWS like REASON, FL STUDIO , CUBASE, ETC... ???', 'answer': "Yes it is! I use mine with Logic Pro. It may not automatically map to all DAWs. But it can be mapped manually to any of them! Just make sure you download the latest firmware to your computer. Remember, it's a basic midi controller! So it should work with any music software. Hope that helps you out!"}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00BQ6KSKO', 'answerTime': 'Feb 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392883200, 'question': 'Noticed there is no AC Adapter included. Is there one here on Amazon?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "I also bought one of these and noticed the same thing. Don't ask me why they don't come with one, it's honestly the most annoying thing, well kinda lol. But yes the M-Audio axiom air (any key) runs over 9v DC power. Amazon does sell power converters. So all you need to look for is a 9v DC power converter. A converter with to much voltage can fry your midi controller!"}
