{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CKFXKE6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 14, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421222400, 'question': 'How do I make this work with a 12 volt power supply in my vehicle? Not a/c', 'answer': 'The controller takes a 12 supply form the wall wart power supply. Just use the small round power connector and hook it to a 12 volt source and skip the wall wart completely. I have used them many times on parade cars doing just that. The wiring diagram is on the back of the unit.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CKFXKE6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395385200, 'question': 'I have a SuperNight SMD5050 multicolor light strip. Will this controller work with my set of light?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "It indicates on the page it is only for the 6803 Dream LED strips, which is how I have them setup. The 5050 is the LED emitter on the strip and the 6803 is the LED driver on the strip that runs 3 LED's. On your LED strip, the emitter is correct but because it appears as it is controlling a single LED, not a group of thre, I'm not sure. That would really depend on the driver on the strip. Look closely at the black controller chip between the LED's and see what number is on the chip, that will tell you what compatable controller will work with it."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CKFXKE6', 'answerTime': 'Jan 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1420358400, 'question': '6803 RF Controller 133 Change for Dream Magic Color Chasing 5050 RGB LED Strip for this I buy bat is not working with the smd 5050 how I setup', 'answer': "You can't use just any smd 5050 lights, they have to be the corresponding lights for the remote. The lights plug right into the remote, and power is connected by control box through power cord. It should work without remote. If remote doesn't work then you need aBee battery for it."}
