{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CP4IIJY', 'answerTime': 'Aug 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407222000, 'question': 'Focusrite Saffire Pro 14 vs this focursrite 6i6? whats the difference?', 'answer': "The Saffire Pro 14 is spec'd 8 in 6 out interface and the 6i6 is 6 in 6 out. However technically the Saffire only has 6 physical inputs (3 stereo pairs). The other 2 input and outputs come for a virtual loopback port that is software controlled. Loopback allows you to record audio coming out of your system back into your system (Example audio from a youtube video in your daw). While the 6i6 lacks software loopback you can connect an SPDIF cable from the spdif output back into the spdif input to achieve the same thing. The Saffire is a Firewire interface while the 6i6 is a USB interface. The other difference is the 6i6 gives you two headphone outputs (1 tied to output 1/2 and other to output 3/4). The Saffire only has 1 headphone out. Other than that they're about the same. Some may argue that Firewire will be better but keep in mind it's getting harder to find computers with firewire. You can use a firewire to thunderbolt adapter on Macs. Personally I love having the extra headphone out on the 6i6. Loopback is not something that I use very often so the extra internal option in the software is not a loss at all for me. HTH."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CP4IIJY', 'answerTime': 'Jul 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1374908400, 'question': 'will it be able to give out sound to 2 pairs of monitors, i own a 2i2 and i have a problem with that i can only send sound to one pair of monitors', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes you can. The 6i6 has four line outputs and a S/PDIF output. You can assign separate mixes or the same one to each.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CP4IIJY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1393833600, 'question': 'Has anyone had a problem pluging an electric guitar directly into the 6i6 ? I understand some have experienced a faint high pitched whine caused by a design flaw in the USB jack of the unit.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Probably a ground loop. I don't usually have an issue until we plug in the keyboard to a PA and the midi input at the same time. Then I get a noise. Fix plug the keys into the midi port only."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CP4IIJY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426057200, 'question': 'Are there 6 inputs? Your image is not showing 6 inputs as far as I can see.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. 2 combination mic/line inputs w phantom power supplies and 4 1/4 in line in jacks on the back as well as midi and USB in/out.'}
