{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CSKKZX2', 'answerTime': 'Feb 19, 2015', 'unixTime': 1424332800, 'question': 'I am planning on using this with my roland tdw-20 drums, for drumming over tunes on my ipad. Would it work? can you record multiple tracks?', 'answer': 'George, there are a number of apps that record multiple tracks.... It should work just fine. Are you going to mic your drums? You can likely only record one track at a time. If you are doing midi you should be able to record multiple tracks at a time but again that will depend on the app you choose.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CSKKZX2', 'answerTime': 'Dec 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419235200, 'question': 'Does the is202 support ipad 2 with ios 8.1.2? I have the Alexis io dock 1 and after updating my ipad to lastes firmware, iy does not charge anymore.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'I would imagine it does. More than likely it has to do with Apple and not Alesis. You should check and make sure that audio is on in iOS settings also. I have the iPad 4 and use a 30 Pin To Lightning adapter and the iStudio has always worked with each iOS update. Never had a problem with the iStudio working with iOS 8 updates.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CSKKZX2', 'answerTime': 'Oct 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1413442800, 'question': "Can you bring electric drums in using midi? I tried with my yamaha set and it's not working (wrong assignments/not triggering sounds).", 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Justin,I have connected my Roland HD3 kit to is202,it works with apps.Check your Yamaha manual,there may be control functions to tweak into service.First time I tried(5 mins ago,)it worked. So the midi port does work.Best way is to put your query to YouTube,I have always got answers this way.Good luck, JonJon'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTKI10A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408431600, 'question': "I assume this supply's Phantom power but does it supply 48V Because my AT2020 XLR takes 48V", 'answer': 'I am using a MXL 770 with it which also requires 48V and it works great. So, yes.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTKI10A', 'answerTime': 'May 5, 2014', 'unixTime': 1399273200, 'question': 'Must I connect this mixer with RCA cables into an interface/computer to record? Or can I simply plug my XLR microphone in, and record through the USB?', 'answer': "You can record straight through the USB. Nifty little thing. But beware, its more of a mixer than a traditional interface, so it doesn't split the tracks you may have already laid down from the new ones you're recording. So basically, EVERYTHING you can hear it in your monitor mix, it's going to be on the track you're currently recording. So if you're recording something live, its perfect. If you're tracking something, not so much..."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CTKI10A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407481200, 'question': 'Can I hook this up to a piano keyboard, laptop/ipod and a sound system to perform on stage together? My goal is to play piano and have backing track', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'Hi Gloria, I don\'t have any "top-of-the-line" keyboard, however, when I tried to get hook up my keyboard to it and run the mixer to the laptop I didn\'t hear a thing through the system or the main mix/phones on the mixer. I\'m guessing you may need a Direct Input (DI) Box to pass the keyboard through first before routing to the mixer. Other than that, yes you should be able to do what you thinking of doing. Hope this helps. :)'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTKI10A', 'answerTime': 'Dec 18, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418889600, 'question': 'What software comes with/is needed for this, it works with Audacity and Windows Media, but how do those compare to similar software? Suggestions?', 'answer': 'After you register with behringer, they will send an email with a code and link to traction. There you can download traction software. It works well, I have an older pc with only 2.5gigs of ram. Also at behringer you can download asio drivers. Nice little mixer, also works well with live lite software.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CTKI10A', 'answerTime': 'Aug 10, 2014', 'unixTime': 1407654000, 'question': 'can i power it with USB only , or its need power supply all time ?', 'answer': "Sorry, but you will need the power cable at all times. It's a great mixer. I use it everyday. Good luck."}
