{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWGINUY', 'answerTime': 'Mar 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394092800, 'question': '2 questions: What size(ohms/watts) DJ power amp &amp; mixer should I get for this to Dj? Also, I can use this for home theatre, wt size reciever? (ohms/wt', 'answer': 'These are not intended for home use or with a stereo receiver as they are a PA system speaker and require a pro audio power amp and a mixer to function properly. So something like a 2000 watt amp that runs around 500 watts a side at 8 ohm would be a good match for these.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Jul 25, 2014', 'unixTime': 1406271600, 'question': 'Which DMX controllers will work well with these lights?', 'answer': 'I use Chauvet Obey 10 and it has been working for me. The tricky part is setting the right address..'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': "I'm having a little trouble with the included instructions. I want to enable DMX control mode and put the light on channel one - any ideas?", 'answer': 'The dip switches on the back. Switch #1 and switch #10 need to be in the on position. If you have the 4 channel version, slider 1 controls strobe and overall intensity. Slider 2 controls red. Slider 3 controls green. And 4, blue. If 5 channel, 1 is strobe, 2 is intensity, 3 is red, 4 is green, and 5 is blue.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Nov 2, 2014', 'unixTime': 1414911600, 'question': 'I am looking for a light to change colors on a huge indoor Christmas card. Can this light do that without using a outside program?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'One of the ten or so switches on the back makes the light alternate through each color continuously.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1391414400, 'question': 'how many lights can I link up as master/ slave. How many feet of wire can I run between them? I want to hook up 14 lights over about 300 feet. thx', 'answer': 'I have run 10 but it was with about 300 feet of DMX cable. Just make sure to use a DMX Terminator for a run that long or you may see some strange crosstalk and lighting changes.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Feb 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1392278400, 'question': 'Looking for cheap uplights on a wall for a banquet dinner: can this light shine one color continuously without any color change? Thanks!', 'answer': "Of course it can! You just have to manipulate the switch in the back and select the color yopu need. It's really very easy.Good Luck!"}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394521200, 'question': 'What is the difference between this and two other models sold by TSSS? Beam, Bulb Count, Brightness...', 'answer': 'There are three models including this one. The 18 led seems to be the one with the most output. However, I love the 86 led par can, they are similar to chauvet splash jr. There is also another par can that has the leds divided to form a cone shape, I do not own those, but I have seen them in action and those are more for decoration rather than flood.'}
