{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Dec 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419062400, 'question': 'Is this light able to be used under a 6ft long table w/white spandex cloth to make it look like a specific color? How many colors?', 'answer': "I would think you could use it under a table cloth. It doesn't off very much heat, but, don't allow any light to come into contact with a combustible. I've gotten red, blue, green, violet, pink as a stand alone unit. If you use a DMX controller, you can get a large range of color, effects, strobe, etc. It can also be made to respond with random colors to ambient noises, music and sounds as a stand alone unit."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Oct 27, 2013', 'unixTime': 1382857200, 'question': 'How big is it in inches? I dont understand how the dimentions on the page only say 0.5 cm', 'answer': 'I don\'t have this here with me, but if I recall the circle is about 4-5.5 inches in diameter. One of the stock photos has a rear view that shows an "XLR" (DMX in this case) input. For scale that should help give you an idea how small this light is. It throws a pretty bright beam for it\'s size.'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00CWYONFU', 'answerTime': 'Mar 7, 2014', 'unixTime': 1394179200, 'question': 'Can anyone post dip switch settings to make this light fade between colors and how to put it into strobe mode? Any other settings would be helpful too', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The instructions are pretty vague or just plain wrong, just a couple of things I found out, though: Switch 1-6 will turn on the various colors at various brightness- DS 1, 3, and 5 turns on the various colors at low, 2 4 6 at a brighter setting, 1-6 all on gives max brightness. 8 by itself gives mic (ambient sound) control, 9 by itself gives chase.'}
