{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00D6KTHRS', 'answerTime': 'Sep 14, 2014', 'unixTime': 1410678000, 'question': 'Hi, is it possible to add another cymbal? Maybe purchase another cymbal from Yamaha? Thank you.', 'answer': "From Yamaha's FAQs: Dtx Electronic Drum Kits Adding Extra Pads To a Module With No Unused Trigger Inputs. 1) Any trigger input that has dual trigger numbers next to it can be split for two single zone pad operation. The toms and the kick typically can be split. 2) Connect to the dual tom triggers trigger input with a trs inch to two mono ts inch plugs input splitter cable. Each mono plug connects to a pad for single zone operation only irrespective of the pads true 2 or 3 zone capability. 3) The kick pedal, such as a kp125, often has a jack for pad input built into it. Plug in a pad with a standard inch cable for single zone operation."}
