{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DN43PQ6', 'answerTime': 'Dec 23, 2014', 'unixTime': 1419321600, 'question': 'How many watts does it draw? Is it possible to run it off of a 400 watt inverter in a class 8 truck?', 'answer': "It draws 18w, 3A @ 9v dc on its input side afer the ac to dc conversion so with typical losses of a switch mode power supply it would draw around 20 to 25w.480W is over kill if its just for the pod. It could probably run of a modulated sinwave inverter since the switch mode chops the ac anyway. The modulated ones are cheaper than the pure sinewave. I wouldnt try the really cheap square wave ones tho. If are running an amp then it may affect your sound quality if ur not running off pure sinewave, solid state amps would be effected less than tube amps but thhere are transformers in both so I wouldnt try it. If you plan to use head phones then make sure they are really good, something that can handle mids and bass. Using headphones is a let down if you don't have a good pair. Buying a pod for this application alone is like buying a Ferrari but never being able to go over 60km/h."}
