{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DUKP37C', 'answerTime': 'Jan 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1388995200, 'question': 'Why does this monitor sound so terrible over 1/4" TRS to my Galaxy S4? I hear almost no vocals, but instrumental is fine. Am I doing something wrong?', 'answer': 'I am not sure, are you using a balanced cable (1/4)" with mono connection? Galaxy S4 might be sending out a stereo signal and the connecting cable might be downgrading the signal to a single channel (mono) connection. You may need two speakers to play the left and right channels. Perhaps your vocals are coming through the other channel. Also check the settings on the lo-pass and high-pass filters (LF Trim and HF Trim). Hope this helps.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00DUKP37C', 'answerTime': 'Feb 7, 2015', 'unixTime': 1423296000, 'question': 'Is there anyway to hook these up with my Schiit Magni/Modi? Or should I buy a separate audio interface?', 'answer': 'Buy a Schiit Sys Preamp, it acts as a volume control and you can connect each speaker to it easily. Then you can connect the Sys to your DAC/amp'}
