{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E71EG0I', 'answerTime': 'Nov 6, 2014', 'unixTime': 1415260800, 'question': 'Considering using as a monitor for small school programs. What cable(s) do I need to hook it up to our soundboard? What kind of input for the mics?', 'answer': 'You should only need to power it up and feed the "XLR through output" from your mix board into one of the XLR inputs on the front this amp. If you\'re plugging in mics they should be XLR balanced mics for best results.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E71EG0I', 'answerTime': 'Dec 1, 2014', 'unixTime': 1417420800, 'question': 'Is there a way to mount this on a wall? Also, do you need any additional purchase to mount on a mic stand?', 'answer': "There are no provisions to mount this on the wall, besides, you will occassionally need access to the rear anyways. Also - you dont need to purchase anything additional to mount it on a mircrophone stand, as it already comes with an adaptor just for that purpose. If you are handy enough, you could mount it on the wall using the bottom center hole that's supposed to be used for the mircophone stand, so it would work like a swivel mount. You would have to fabricate this type of mount yourself."}
