{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00E8CEW7I', 'answerTime': 'Mar 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425369600, 'question': 'Are these ones suitable for a small room (130ft&sup2; i.e. 12m&sup2;)... or should I buy the 305 model? Thanx...', 'answer': 'The 305 version may work but you will eventually want a subwoofer. The 308 version pushes enough bass to eliminate the need for a subwoofer. The 308s are excellent speakers and cheaper if you consider a pair of 305s and a JBL subwoofer. I have both setups and I prefer the 308s. I hope this helps'}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00E8CEW7I', 'answerTime': 'Jan 22, 2014', 'unixTime': 1390377600, 'question': 'Looking at these monitors for computer speakers. Will I need any additional items?', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': 'The inputs on these are, one XLR and one 1/4", you will use one or the other, so you would need cabling to match that on one end and to match whatever the output is on your computer. Usually a 3.5mm trs to either two xlr or two 1/4" does the job. Such as a Hosa CMP-159 Stereo Breakout or a Hosa CYX-402M Stereo Breakout.'}
