{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EACW8VI', 'answerTime': 'Aug 16, 2014', 'unixTime': 1408172400, 'question': 'Title says "7 Color," but description says " RGB(16 pcs Red,16pcs Green,16pcs Blue" -- I\'d call that 3 color. Where are those other 4 colors?', 'answer': "I'm guessing they are going with red+blue = violet, red+green = yellow, blue+green= teal, and red+green+blue= white. These colors only appear in the areas of overlapping colors. The lights are so close together that there is some overlap. It is unmistakably RGB, but on a white wall, other colors, particularly white, can be seen."}
