{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EBK6C20', 'answerTime': 'Mar 4, 2015', 'unixTime': 1425456000, 'question': 'The reason is that the build in microphone of my webcam has a lot of noise in the background. Any recommendation?', 'answer': "I am not an audio expert. However, I do use many of these lavalier microphones with my Sennheiser wireless system at my school's theatre. Noise will sometimes be a problem if the area around the microphone is noisy, especially outside where wind can be a significant problem (possibly reduced with a foam wind screen. Try a lavalier connected directly to your camera; I think you'll be pleasantly surprised with the improved sound."}
