{'answer': "The short answer is yes, but it's never going to sound quite like a high-end tube amp. It is its own animal...One of the secrets you learn as time goes on is that even a cheap amp can do a lot in the hands of an expert. The Champion 100 is fully capable of handling most rock styles, including those you mentioned. I've found a sweet spot on mine using the second-highest distortion setting on the rotary knob selector, and with my basic settings, I can play pretty much any rock style I want. I prefer tone over distortion, but there's plenty of distortion in there, and it handles pedals well....", 'asin': 'B00EM5UOBE', 'answerTime': '28 days ago', 'question': 'Would this amp be good for some heavier rock like Black Sabbath or Metallica?', 'questionType': 'open-ended'}
