{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EO4A7L0', 'answerTime': 'Dec 11, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418284800, 'question': 'So, if I want to use it with a laptop and the program called camtasia, what do I need?', 'answer': "I think I read somewhere, or saw a YouTube vid that explained that plugging a Lavalier mic directly into a PC using the mic jack doesn't produce good results because there is no power. Seems odd that connecting to an iPhone works great, but not a laptop, but that's what the article said. I use the Rhode when recording to my iPhone, and it is superb. For recording to Camtasia I use a USB mic."}
{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EO4A7L0', 'answerTime': 'Sep 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411110000, 'question': "Thanks for the reviews! Now I'm a bit confused - I'm very happy with the video that my iPhone 5s takes, but I'm just looking for a mic that will allow me to do an interview video with a person standing several feet away. Do I need to install an...", 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': "Yes. Plug the lav mic into the iPhone and shoot the video. Also know that you can add extensions to the mic cable in order to move the camera further away from subject, if necessary. I've been using two extensions to my Rode mic. The extensions are by Edutige and available here on Amazon."}
