{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00EO7UNXO', 'answerTime': 'Jan 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421827200, 'question': 'I hear what sounds like some type of static like fm type noise when i turn both my speakers up past -30db in volume??', 'answer': 'I heard a lot of noise as well, that is before i bought a dedicated audio interface, like an m-audio m-track, preSonus, focusrite, etc.. If you\'re not using one, then i\'d say get that first. I have no noise now at all settings. From -30db, and i usually have my speakers set at the +6db and nothing. i\'m also using the 1/4" to 1/4" plug into the balanced inputs. If you\'re using an audio interface, then i\'d say call customer support and get it fixed.'}
