{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00EQDITGO', 'answerTime': 'Dec 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1418025600, 'question': 'Can someone get really basic. How is this thing set up, i presume it plugs into an amp and a guitar, but are two channels needed for stereo, etc.', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yep. I just plug my guitar into the top slot and then pass the other top-slot output to the amp. The only downside of this is that distortion from the amp is applied after the looping, which can cause some strange effects. On a clean-sound it works just fine, otherwise you'll want a distortion pedal before the loop-pedal."}
