{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00F2ATEDC', 'answerTime': 'Sep 24, 2014', 'unixTime': 1411542000, 'question': 'Is the fog very misty/ wet to the touch? I am trying to use this to analyze airflow patterns instead of tracer smoke which is quite exp.', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'I think it could work for what you want to do, but it can leave a light oily residue. I mix my own solution--check the internet and find out how. Doing that you could make adjustments to fit your need. Glycerin is involved, it spoils and has to be used quickly. It is available at pharmacies. Mixed with distilled water it will spoil when stored, over the counter mixes are laden with additives to prevent spoilage. You will be warned that doing so is dangerous. I report, you decide. I always mixed my own and I could fog out our street, both sides, at least two blocks worth. The unit you are looking at worked real well for us and I think it will last a long time.'}
