{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00F37SX5Y', 'answerTime': 'Mar 24, 2015', 'unixTime': 1427180400, 'question': 'Can it be used as a VSTi controller via MIDI?', 'answerType': 'Y', 'answer': 'Yes. People have used Aerodrums with EZ Drummer, Superior Drummer, BFD, SSD, Studio Drummer and others, using Logic, Pro Tools, Kontakt, Reaper and others as hosts. We provide presets for the popular drum samplers.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F37SX5Y', 'answerTime': 'Mar 21, 2015', 'unixTime': 1426921200, 'question': 'Can I add octobans? Chinas? Or whatever drum or cymbal I want?', 'answer': 'Aerodrums comes with samples for a China cymbal. You can make additional drum kit pieces using your own sound samples. Aerodrums will sort them by velocity so you can have proper dynamics. So if you have samples for octobans, you can add them to your Aerodrums kits. Aerodrums is also MIDI compatible. This lets you drum into any sampler that can take MIDI notes as input.'}
