{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00F5C06T8', 'answerTime': 'Feb 3, 2015', 'unixTime': 1422950400, 'question': "What's the difference between the output and satellite output connections?", 'answer': 'Hello. The XLR male outputs are a passive line level throughput to share an unfiltered signal to another device like a powered speaker or an amp. The Satellite outputs are affected by the high pass and eq options and are designed to send amplified signal to power a passive speaker.'}
