{'questionType': 'yes/no', 'asin': 'B00GOIC1S6', 'answerTime': 'May 20, 2014', 'unixTime': 1400569200, 'question': 'is this a good tuner for a nube? i have another electric tuner and it is set correct 440 htz but i will get the green light and it is all wrong... TY', 'answerType': '?', 'answer': "Yes, I'm also a nube. It's preset to 440 Hz and has a tuning range of 435 Hz to 445 Hz. Before I had this I was always told you're not tuned up properly even though I was using an electronic tuner. Now I don't have that problem and I don't need help tuning properly. I hope this helps you."}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GOIC1S6', 'answerTime': 'Apr 8, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396940400, 'question': 'What battery does it take? And what is the average life of the battery?', 'answer': 'It uses a CR2032 Lithium battery, availble for small $$ here at Amazon, & at almost any drugstore. Average life -- this tuner draws very little power. I have played for many days, hours at a time, never turning the tuner off. The battery is still doing just fine. In other words, battery life is quite lengthy.'}
{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GOIC1S6', 'answerTime': 'Mar 19, 2014', 'unixTime': 1395212400, 'question': 'Does this tuner show the octave? For example does it display A1, A2, A3, A4, etc??', 'answer': "In the chromatic mode it doesn't show the octave. However, in the instrument mode (Guitar, Bass, etc.) it does show the string number. So the guitar mode can show E6 or E1."}
