{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00GQDORA4', 'answerTime': 'Jan 13, 2014', 'unixTime': 1389600000, 'question': "Should I get a used Rode Video Mic Shotgun Microphone or The rode Videomic go? assume I can't go far over 100$ in budget", 'answer': 'Best qualities of the Videomic Go: Small, no battery (powered from the camera), easy to transport. Best qualities of the Rode Videomic over the Videomic Go: Battery powered (better range), high pass filter, PAD switch (for reducing sensitivity on louder recordings). Not having a battery can be nice (using the GO), but the camera you use has to be able to power over the 1/8" mic input. The high pass filter and PAD switch are nice on the Videomic, but not always necessary. If you don\'t think you\'ll need them, then the Videomic GO is the way to go.'}
