{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HHEVL3C', 'answerTime': 'Jul 3, 2014', 'unixTime': 1404370800, 'question': 'Where would MIC 96k be positioned in relation to a drum kit to record optimal balance of the components of the drum kit, cymbals, kick, snare, hi-hat?', 'answer': "If it's the only mic you're using, probably back in the room, about 8-10 feet away. Make sure you're compressing the hell out of the signal... I've never tried this on drums but wouldn't be surprised if it's too sensitive and is prone to distortion. I haven't seen a USB mic that can handle a drum kit. A better drum/general purpose mic is the Rode stereo mic... The Rode iXy is great too. But the Apogee is the best sounding USB mic I've ever used by far for vocals."}
