{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HWHSXYE', 'answerTime': 'Mar 29, 2014', 'unixTime': 1396076400, 'question': 'Can you overdub when in reverse mode or in half speed mode? If not, do any loopers on the market now do this? Thanks!', 'answer': 'Yes, you can. When you start recording your initial loop in reverse, hit the FX switch again - this will stop the recording, disengage the Reverse FX and start an overdub so your loop is played back in reverse immediately, enabling you to solo on top of it right away.'}
