{'questionType': 'open-ended', 'asin': 'B00HWHSXYE', 'answerTime': 'Jan 16, 2015', 'unixTime': 1421395200, 'question': 'Jjust want to play rhythm track (maybe an intro) and then play the loop when I solo. If I hit "stop" will that erase loop, or can use again for outro?', 'answer': "Not at all, stopping the loop leaves all the information intact. Even when power is removed the loop is there waiting when you plug it back in. Actually deleting the loop requires that you stop the loop and hold down the record button; feels much like smothering it with a pillow. Holding down the record button while the loop is still playing simply undoes the last thing you recorded. In my humble opinion, the Ditto's a real solid pedal."}
